WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:02.270
1835.

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.980
The American Frontier.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.340
A beacon of hope in a world choked with blood
and smog.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:13.770
Little did the hopeful citizens of a still
newly-independent United States know, the

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:17.210
evils of the old world had followed them here.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:20.420
Sometimes it took the form of hate, of violence.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.380
Of desperation and starvation.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:29.420
But sometimes, pure evil wasn’t just some
abstract concept, existing in and around all

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.420
of us.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:36.910
Sometimes, that evil - that pure cruelty,
malice, and greed - walks in the shape of

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:38.130
a man.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:44.770
One such man was James Anderson, an unremarkable
name for a truly exceptional man.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.340
Exceptional in the sense that if most human
beings aren’t willing to sell out all of

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:54.900
humanity for their own petty gain, James Anderson
is definitely the exception.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:01.790
After all, it’s by his design that we have
SCP-001, the anomaly that set the SCP Foundation

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:06.350
- and our entire reality - down its current
path.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:08.280
Of course, you know the deal with SCP-001.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.569
Not one anomaly, but many.

00:01:11.569 --> 00:01:16.810
A collective designation for a vast number
of entries, all of which spell beginnings

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:22.389
or ends for the SCP Foundation and sometimes
even our universe.

00:01:22.389 --> 00:01:26.889
Scarlet Kings, Howling Black Moons, Ouroboros
Cycles, and Gate Guardians.

00:01:26.889 --> 00:01:30.070
You’ve heard them all, and seen the files.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:34.609
But unlike all the others, there is no file
for The Factory.

00:01:34.609 --> 00:01:40.869
That’s because the full story only exists
in the mind of O5-1, one of the most powerful,

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:43.960
and arguably the oldest, member of the SCP
Foundation.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:48.209
He’ll die before he ever commits the story
to paper.

00:01:48.209 --> 00:01:51.540
Some memories are just too awful to record.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.299
Their details and implications are too painful
to ever subject others to.

00:01:56.299 --> 00:02:01.680
SCP-001 isn’t just about Anderson and his
atrocities, it’s about all the terrible

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:07.630
nightmares that unfolded afterward - and the
deal with the devil that O5-1 struck to lock

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:08.780
them away.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.610
For now, at least.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:13.060
But it all begins with James Anderson.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:18.060
His family had become incredibly wealthy in
the Revolutionary War, and in the decades

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:23.080
since, his fortune had only multiplied, as
fortunes tend to do.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:30.210
In the early 1800s, he began work on his beautiful
and horrific magnum opus: The Anderson Factory.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.230
It would be the pinnacle of the Industrial
Revolution.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:37.430
The manufacturing plant to end all manufacturing
plants.

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.170
Three stories tall and a mile wide.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:46.560
Company towns had existed for a long time,
but this time, the factory itself was the

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.560
town.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:53.170
It had everything a worker would ever need:
They would live, sleep, play, and most importantly

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:56.120
of all, work, in the same place.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.430
They would never need to leave.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:04.120
All their wants and needs, from cradle to
grave, would be met in The Anderson Factory,

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:09.100
and all that Mr. Anderson ever asked in return
was loyalty and service.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.960
Was that really so much to ask from those
whom he gave everything?

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.870
It may sound like a horrifying form of indentured
servitude to us, but to the people in the

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:23.600
United States in the early 1830s, this kind
of security and stability was a godsend.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:29.620
To many itinerant workers and unstable families
across the planes, James Anderson seemed like

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.760
a saint.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:37.820
Little did they know, his plans for the factory,
and them, were anything but saintly.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:42.960
Nobody knows exactly what type of dark magic
James Anderson devoted himself to.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:48.300
Many have theorized as to whether it was Satan
he worshipped, ancient pagan deities, or something

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.540
older and more powerful than both.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:56.540
In actuality, the only thing that James Anderson
really worshipped was himself, and the pursuit

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:00.580
of more material wealth and power over his
fellow man.

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:04.990
Any pacts he made with evil timeless gods
were just means to an end.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:10.791
The Anderson Factory was a citadel to one
man’s cruelty and corruption, and every

00:04:10.791 --> 00:04:14.790
element of the building’s design seemed
to reflect that.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:21.209
Groups of eight were forced into rooms together
like battery-farmed chickens to maximize cost-efficiency.

00:04:21.209 --> 00:04:24.650
People worked day and night, in shifts of
three.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:27.729
Machines always rumbled and roared and chewed.

00:04:27.729 --> 00:04:32.699
When workers died in factory accidents and
their blood spilled on the ground, it seemed

00:04:32.699 --> 00:04:36.490
to reveal arcane symbols carved into the stonework.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:40.310
These symbols were only visible when blood
flowed across them.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:44.919
While people traveled hundreds of miles to
live and work at the Anderson Factory, they

00:04:44.919 --> 00:04:51.259
had no idea that they were working towards
slavery, subjugation, and death under Anderson’s

00:04:51.259 --> 00:04:52.259
iron will.

00:04:52.259 --> 00:04:57.060
And, in some cases, fates much, much worse.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:02.190
The factory remained in operation like this
for forty years, while Anderson himself enjoyed

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:05.919
a positive public reputation as a groundbreaking
industrialist.

00:05:05.919 --> 00:05:12.469
How Anderson got away with his crimes for
so long is sadly a tale as old as time: The

00:05:12.469 --> 00:05:16.629
factory made valuable products and an awful
lot of profit.

00:05:16.629 --> 00:05:22.539
So, no matter how many rumors swirled about
inhumane practices or arcane rites going on

00:05:22.539 --> 00:05:26.550
in the Anderson Factory, nothing was ever
done.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:31.740
It was just too inconvenient to ever reckon
with the horrible truth underneath the productive

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:32.740
surface.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:34.560
And it truly was productive.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:39.540
The factory was so huge and filled with such
a multitude of enslaved workers, there wasn’t

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:41.250
anything they didn’t produce.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.979
From textiles to technology, to crops and
meat.

00:05:44.979 --> 00:05:46.909
The machines were always on.

00:05:46.909 --> 00:05:49.680
The furnaces always burned.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:55.779
Anderson himself seemed obsessed with two
things: Efficiency and misanthropy - the contempt

00:05:55.779 --> 00:05:58.030
and hatred for humanity itself.

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:04.309
He believed his workers were lower than him,
they only existed as a means to his nightmarish

00:06:04.309 --> 00:06:05.309
ends.

00:06:05.309 --> 00:06:10.120
And if ever the workers became too injured
to work, well, that doesn’t mean that Anderson

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:13.680
wouldn’t still find ways to put them to
“good” use...

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:19.050
The lucky ones, starved and neglected, or
broken by the stress of work or the grinding

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:24.099
gears of the machines, were used as material
in the production of products.

00:06:24.099 --> 00:06:28.240
Some were drained of blood, so that it could
be used in the forging of metal.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:33.590
Others were ground up into meat slurry and
used to pad out the beef, making it go further.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:39.529
People all across the country enjoying fine
Anderson-brand steaks had no idea they were

00:06:39.529 --> 00:06:43.300
actually dining on human flesh the whole time.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:48.430
But as we said, the ones who ended up being
cooked into steaks and hamburgers after death

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:52.089
were the lucky ones - because at least they
got to die.

00:06:52.089 --> 00:06:58.050
The truly unlucky injured workers became the
subject of James Anderson’s horrific occult

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.050
experiments.

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:04.150
Using a mix of twisted science and black magic,
he turned men into abominations.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:10.150
Powerful, terrifying monsters, stronger and
more deadly than any mortal man.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:13.830
Anderson was building himself an anomalous
army.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.330
But it wasn’t just monsters.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:20.029
There were just as many so-called “normal”
humans helping him rule over the Anderson

00:07:20.029 --> 00:07:21.849
Factory with an iron fist.

00:07:21.849 --> 00:07:28.949
They were vicious sadists themselves, spurred
on by absolute loyalty to their immoral master.

00:07:28.949 --> 00:07:33.869
It was only after the Civil War that someone
finally escaped the Anderson Factory and confirmed

00:07:33.869 --> 00:07:38.279
that not only were the most horrific rumors
about the place true, but they didn’t even

00:07:38.279 --> 00:07:41.830
come close to covering the totality of what
was going on there.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:45.839
When President Grant heard the reports, he
was disgusted.

00:07:45.839 --> 00:07:50.270
As far as he was concerned, the atrocities
of James Anderson should not be allowed to

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:52.250
go on a minute longer.

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:58.289
The directive was simple: Find the factory,
free its prisoners, and put James Anderson

00:07:58.289 --> 00:07:59.979
to death for his crimes.

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:04.740
And thankfully, President Grant had the perfect
group of operatives for the job.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:10.129
They were an elite unit of around 150 soldiers
who performed a number of dangerous missions

00:08:10.129 --> 00:08:12.949
beyond enemy lines down South.

00:08:12.949 --> 00:08:16.839
Espionage, assassination, psychological warfare.

00:08:16.839 --> 00:08:19.789
But these missions weren’t just against
the Confederates.

00:08:19.789 --> 00:08:25.210
Some of the enemies they faced down South
were things that could not be explained: The

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:28.369
strange, the frightening, the anomalous.

00:08:28.369 --> 00:08:33.580
And the highest-ranking soldier in this unit
was a man who would one day become the legendary

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:34.580
O5-1.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:40.700
He and his men made their long and treacherous
journey to the factory, a trip that would

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.690
change all of their lives forever.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:47.170
When they reached their destination, they
first had to deal with Anderson’s security

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:48.250
force.

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:53.120
These were men whose cruelty and loyalty to
Anderson far outweighed their skill in combat.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:58.180
While they may have felt powerful when tormenting
starving, injured factory workers, they were

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:02.470
quickly routed and slaughtered by O5-1 and
his team.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:07.270
When they ventured inside the factory, they
were utterly appalled by what they saw.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:13.010
The inhuman conditions faced by Anderson’s
thousands of victims drove them into a bloodcurdling,

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:14.760
murderous rage.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:19.950
Almost half of O5-1’s men were lost in the
battle against Anderson’s army of engineered

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:23.130
monsters, but in the end, they prevailed.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:28.160
Nothing would stop them in their quest for
liberation and vengeance, on behalf of all

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.510
that this terrible place had tormented.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:35.680
They fought their way to Anderson’s office,
where they found him cowering under his desk.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:41.830
For a man as despicable as Anderson, only
a truly medieval execution would suffice.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:47.640
O5-1 and his men hanged, drew, and quartered
Anderson over a period of two days.

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:53.270
The sadistic madman died laughing in the end,
saying that while they may kill him, his factory

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:54.910
will never die.

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:57.820
But the factory was no longer his.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:03.520
In addition to the Factory’s horrors, O5-1
and his men also discovered its wonders - It

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:07.020
wasn’t just normal items and monsters that
The Factory produced.

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:12.070
They were also, thanks to some of Anderson’s
arcane deals, the world’s leading producer

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:17.970
of anomalous items: Skeletal horses that never
tire, shadow cloaks that can transport the

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:23.470
wearer to different dimensions, toy guns that
fire real bullets, even yo-yos that could

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:26.550
flay the skin from anyone they touched.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:30.200
These were anomalous objects that could shift
the balance of global power.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:35.170
Items that could give them an advantage against
the things that go bump in the night.

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:40.940
While others among them were greedy or fearful,
the inner circle of O5-1 were united in a

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:46.290
singular purpose: Using the anomalous they
can control to contain the anomalous that

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:47.600
they can’t.

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:53.850
This group took over the Factory, making it
Site Alpha, their first ever containment facility,

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:57.300
and came to be known as the O5 Council.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:02.110
With funding that came from a mix of blackmail
and friends in high places, this organization

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:08.100
- a burgeoning SCP Foundation - grew more
and more powerful over the ensuing decades.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:12.260
The tools they gained from the Factory were
pivotal in the continued success of their

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:18.090
mission, and as they discovered more anomalies,
they also put these anomalies to good use.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:24.300
But in 1911, O5-1 and his new organization
came up against an enemy that even the Factory’s

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:29.570
tools couldn’t help them defeat: A warrior
race known as The Fae, so named because their

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:33.470
only weakness seemed to be a vulnerability
to iron.

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:38.860
But these beings were an order of magnitude
more powerful than humans, or the beasts they’d

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:40.970
once faced in Anderson’s factory.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.690
The Fae handed them defeat after defeat.

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:49.690
But soon, humiliation became decimation, when
an army of the Fae led an assault on the Factory.

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:55.160
It was a day that only O5-1 remembered: The
Fae slaughtered everyone.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:59.650
Every guard, every researcher, every member
of the O5 Council.

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:04.620
They swept through the factory like a plague
of locusts, leaving only death and destruction

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.030
in their wake.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:10.390
Only O5-1 escaped and survived, and that’s
only because he ran.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:15.800
As he fled from the Faery forces through the
halls of the Factory, he came upon a door

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.360
he’d never seen before.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:21.050
A huge, golden door, covered in Aramaic script.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:24.610
He fled inside, entering the very heart of
the factory.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:29.870
Inside, he saw the floating dead body of James
Anderson, bathed in red light.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:35.310
Now, he was little more than the mouthpiece
of the Factory itself - or rather, the great

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:38.360
and unknowable powers working behind it.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:44.230
The Factory gave O5-1 an offer, just like
the offer it had given Anderson before: It

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:49.210
would give them the power to turn back time
and destroy the Fae, saving everyone that

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:51.220
they’d slain in the Factory.

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:56.520
But in exchange, all of them would forever
belong to the Factory.

00:12:56.520 --> 00:13:02.020
And in a moment of weakness and fear, O5-1
took the deal.

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:05.170
The clock was turned back to before the battle.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:10.940
This time, O5-1 and his compatriots - all
of whom except him had no idea what had happened

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:15.020
- had the horrific weapons required to slaughter
the Fae.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:18.700
Weapons that nobody, mortal or otherwise,
could possess.

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:24.790
They repelled the invading force easily, but
knowing the horrors that came before, O5-1

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:26.210
refused to stop there.

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:31.070
With the power of the Foundation and the Factory
behind him, he hunted down and murdered every

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:36.170
last Faery - driving their species entirely
into extinction.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:40.640
As far as O5-1 was concerned, it was them
or him.

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:45.850
But with the Fae utterly destroyed and the
Foundation’s superiority assured, a shadow

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:52.130
was laying over O5-1: He’d made a deal with
the Factory, and someday, it would want its

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.010
pound of flesh.

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:59.340
O5-1, rather than facing the consequences
of his actions, decided to run and hide.

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:04.690
He had the Factory decommissioned, and buried
under rubble, never to be used as an active

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.750
Foundation base again.

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:11.510
But just because they were done with the Factory
doesn’t mean that the Factory was done with

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:12.510
them.

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:16.010
One day, a toy gun appeared on O5-1’s desk.

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:21.511
A toy gun that fired real bullets, just like
the ones they found in the factory a century

00:14:21.511 --> 00:14:22.550
before.

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:25.570
The factory was still waiting for its repayment.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:30.070
With every anomalous item from the Factory
that the Foundation used, the terrible place

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:32.170
only grew in its power.

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:38.690
Since the resurgence, O5-1 has been sending
the Factory sacrifices - D-Classes, dead and

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:41.960
alive, as well as Agents and Researchers.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:48.090
But as time goes on, it seems that these sacrifices
aren’t satisfying the Factory anymore.

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:52.820
It wants more, more than O5-1 can ever stand
to give it.

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:58.960
And when O5-1 refuses to give, the Factory
will begin to take.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:05.310
And what the Factory wants, sooner or later,
the Factory will get...

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:09.250
The SCP Foundation is no stranger to pure
evil.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:14.850
Whether it’s a reptile that wants to end
all life, a sadistic old man with his own

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:20.580
torture dimension, or the personification
of death itself lurking beyond a limestone

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:21.580
cavern.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:24.880
But what if there was something even worse
out there?

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:32.180
The embodiment of chaos and cruelty, existing
across multiple realities and dimensions.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:35.980
And what if it was coming for us.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:41.860
This is The Scarlet King - believed by many
to be the ultimate evil behind much of the

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:47.310
trouble the Foundation has faced and some
even speculate that fighting him was the reason

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:50.900
the Foundation was created in the first place.

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:53.460
But what exactly is the Scarlet King?

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:58.890
He’s known by many names, almost always
including some allusion to the color “red”,

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:06.290
and then a reference to royalty or power-
Harak, Khahrahk, the Red Shah, the Crimson

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:16.420
Khan, PTE-616-Mendes-Ex-Machina, the Lāla
Rājā, and of course SCP - 001 to name a

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:17.420
few.

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:22.040
And like many of the Foundation’s mysterious
enemies, stories about his true nature and

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.930
origins abound and are often contradictory.

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:31.690
According to the official SCP - 001 files
of Tufto’s proposal, symbology of the Scarlet

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:37.090
King has existed in multiple cultures throughout
history, with the king often depicted the

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:45.450
same way, as a huge, red demonic figure, often
wearing a gold crown of other headdress indicating

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:46.450
royalty.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:51.290
He shows up looking similarly within different
cultures’ mythologies, despite existing

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:56.740
at different points in history or them not
having the means to communicate with one another.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:17:01.800
A number of entities that the SCP Foundation
is familiar with are believed to be somehow

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:08.870
connected to the Scarlet King, including SCP
- 2317 - a wooden door leading to the realm

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:14.230
of a being known as the Devourer, who’s
expected to escape and cause an apocalyptic

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:16.120
event in the next thirty years.

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:22.630
But really, there’s no way of knowing just
how many SCPs are directly connected to the

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:23.920
Scarlet King.

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:29.240
Strangely, the Foundation's official file
on the Scarlet King once designated his containment

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:33.900
class as Keter, but that has since been downgraded
to Safe.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:38.820
According to the file, any attempt to change
this designation is likely to lead to horrifying

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:39.930
results.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:44.559
It is widely known that the Scarlet King still
has considerable influence over a number of

00:17:44.559 --> 00:17:51.070
groups, individuals, and anomalies in our
universe, and if ever he made his way into

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:57.640
our universe, it would likely lead to the
irreversible damage of reality itself, so

00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:58.810
then why safe?

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:03.570
And why are the O5 Council so adamant that
it remain that way?

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:07.690
Getting to the bottom of this mystery is exactly
why we’re here today.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:13.410
But, to fully grasp the true nature of the
Scarlet King, we must first understand the

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:19.320
man whose life and fate have always been tied
to it: Dr. Robert Montauk.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:24.780
If that name feels oddly familiar to you,
it’s because of its association with one

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:31.779
of the Scarlet King’s most recent attempts
to enter our reality: SCP - 231.

00:18:31.779 --> 00:18:37.330
This SCP, often referred to as the Brides
of the Scarlet King, was formed of seven women

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:43.150
- seven, by the way, being an extremely significant
number for the King - all kidnapped by the

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:48.270
most recent in a long line of the King’s
devoted cults known as The Children of the

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:49.270
Scarlet King.

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:54.510
Each of these seven unfortunate women were
impregnated with anomalous horrors, such as

00:18:54.510 --> 00:19:00.850
the infamous SCP-682, and every time one of
these horrors were birthed, a catastrophe

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:03.250
occurred and the mother died.

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:09.230
At the time, Dr. Montauk was a prominent researcher
studying this anomaly, and as six catastrophes

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:14.530
had already occurred, pressure was mounting
to figure out a way to prevent the final birth.

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:20.430
But as he was working on the issue, Dr. Montauk
was struck with a personal tragedy - The mysterious

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:23.480
disappearance of his 14 year old brother,
Jacob.

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:28.530
In his fear and anger, Montauk believed that
this must have had something to do with the

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:30.970
Scarlet King and his disciples.

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:35.910
Wanting revenge, Montauk proposed an idea
so horrifying that the details were never

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:42.970
made public - a procedure known as 110-Montauk
to be performed on the final bride at regular

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:44.040
intervals.

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:49.100
However, this wasn’t the end of Dr. Montauk’s
fraught relationship with the Scarlet King

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:52.240
- it was just the beginning.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:58.340
To give you some perspective on just how dangerous
the Scarlet King is, the SCP Foundation and

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:03.710
the Global Occult Coalition decided to put
aside their differences and form a joint effort

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:06.890
to stamp out the Children of the Scarlet King.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:11.820
They were successful in this mission, and
even managed to capture the Children’s leader

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:14.330
- a mysterious man named Dipesh Spivak.

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:21.730
Dr. Montauk, who’d become the lead researcher
on 231 and 2317, was naturally the first choice

00:20:21.730 --> 00:20:27.440
for interviewing Dipesh about the true nature
of The Children and of The Scarlet King.

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:33.690
Dr. Montauk could never be the impartial interviewer
that the SCP Foundation wanted though, the

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:38.510
suspicion that the Scarlet King or the Children
had something to do with the loss of his younger

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:43.020
brother, still lingered just beneath the surface.

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:48.200
Like a lot of cult leaders, Dipesh was extremely
cryptic in his answers to Dr. Montauk’s

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:49.200
questioning.

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:53.770
He’d already heard of the doctor from the
reputation of the horrifying Montauk procedure,

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:57.380
and was surprised to see him so calm and courteous
in person.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:21:03.040
A few key facts about the King and his cult
were revealed in the first few rounds of questioning:

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:07.860
The Children had once worked with the Serpent’s
Hand before being excommunicated for their

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:12.830
allegiance to the King, and they had stolen
sacred texts from the mystical Wanderer’s

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.830
Library to assist in their summoning rituals.

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:21.350
Dipesh also revealed that the Scarlet King
is bound by three Laws - the Law of Blood,

00:21:21.350 --> 00:21:24.980
the Law of Concrete, and the Law of Howling.

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:30.980
Dr. Montauk, confused and frustrated by Dipesh’s
secrecy, had to learn more.

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:35.290
He found an old memoir from a former member
of the Children of the Scarlet King, Jack

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:40.580
Hearst, who had the ability to invade the
minds of people from the past and experience

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:42.050
what they experienced.

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:47.230
He recounted a battle between the Scarlet
King and his followers and a group of time-traveling

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:51.270
Turkmen warriors from SCP - 3838.

00:21:51.270 --> 00:21:53.840
Hearst saw both sides of the battle.

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:58.480
From the perspective of the Children of the
Scarlet King, their lord ruled over them from

00:21:58.480 --> 00:22:01.800
an immense fortress embedded in a volcano.

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:06.820
From the perspective of the Turkmen, the Children
were starved and beaten peasants, commanded

00:22:06.820 --> 00:22:10.770
by the King’s voice in the roaring howl
of the wind.

00:22:10.770 --> 00:22:16.170
Montauk also found extensive records of summoning
rituals performed by various Scarlet King-aligned

00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:17.200
cults.

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:22.540
Interestingly, some of them incorporated the
use of carved SCP Foundation symbols.

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:24.460
What could this mean?

00:22:24.460 --> 00:22:29.720
Montauk returned again to Dipesh, who finally
gave him the truth about the Law of Blood.

00:22:29.720 --> 00:22:36.120
This is the Law of the Scarlet King - it’s
defined by poverty, violence, starvation,

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:39.390
hate, and most of all, fear.

00:22:39.390 --> 00:22:45.040
Like the serfs in the Middle Ages, persecuted
by and subjected to violence from the nobles.

00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:50.330
To the Children of the Scarlet King, this
sense of holy pain and awe is the only way

00:22:50.330 --> 00:22:51.380
to live.

00:22:51.380 --> 00:22:57.970
The alternative is the Law of Concrete - which
means the modern age, defined by empty safety

00:22:57.970 --> 00:22:59.470
and false comfort.

00:22:59.470 --> 00:23:05.360
Buildings, easy to access food, healthcare,
knowledge, technology.

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:09.110
This is everything that the Scarlet King despises.

00:23:09.110 --> 00:23:14.470
But the mystery only deepened as Montauk found
files from a former Foundation operative by

00:23:14.470 --> 00:23:16.890
the name of Agent de Beauvoir.

00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:22.010
Montauk learned that the Scarlet King didn’t
seem to appear until after the Foundation

00:23:22.010 --> 00:23:27.800
was created, and in fact, it seemed that the
greater interest the Foundation took in the

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:30.980
Scarlet King, the more powerful he became.

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:32.860
How could this be?

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:37.559
Things were also getting stranger on a personal
level for Dr. Montauk - Dipesh repeatedly

00:23:37.559 --> 00:23:42.809
pressed him about his brother’s disappearance,
and the Montauk Procedure, during the interviews.

00:23:42.809 --> 00:23:46.630
Little by little, it was beginning to take
its toll.

00:23:46.630 --> 00:23:50.210
The questions still plagued him: What was
the Law of Howling?

00:23:50.210 --> 00:23:53.070
Who or what really is the Scarlet King?

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:54.530
How did he come to be?

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:58.470
Montauk’s search was causing him to act
more like the Children of the Scarlet King

00:23:58.470 --> 00:24:03.560
- ranting about the horrors of the modern
world, how all of us are living a lie.

00:24:03.560 --> 00:24:09.049
how the only “honest” way to live is suffering
under the dominion of the Scarlet King.

00:24:09.049 --> 00:24:14.130
This philosophy is summed up in the words
of one cultist named Ariadne Cartwright who

00:24:14.130 --> 00:24:15.130
said:

00:24:15.130 --> 00:24:17.380
“We must learn what it is to die.

00:24:17.380 --> 00:24:25.270
To be enslaved- truly, brutally enslaved,
with no compassion or compunction from our

00:24:25.270 --> 00:24:26.270
masters.

00:24:26.270 --> 00:24:32.460
We must learn what it is to be taken towards
a single purpose, to know and truly understand

00:24:32.460 --> 00:24:34.560
our lack of agency.

00:24:34.560 --> 00:24:40.880
We must be beholden to a world of gods and
darkness, the tempest-tossed refuse of a race

00:24:40.880 --> 00:24:42.140
of fools.

00:24:42.140 --> 00:24:48.600
We must kill modernity, postmodernity, with
all its analysis and sneering observation.

00:24:48.600 --> 00:24:52.760
There is only one rule; the rule of chaos.

00:24:52.760 --> 00:24:53.940
For humanity!

00:24:53.940 --> 00:24:55.080
For life!

00:24:55.080 --> 00:24:57.900
For the Scarlet King!”

00:24:57.900 --> 00:25:05.100
Basically, any time humanity tries to exert
control over the world, the Scarlet King gets

00:25:05.100 --> 00:25:06.100
stronger.

00:25:06.100 --> 00:25:11.790
Every time they try to understand or organize
or categorize their world, the Scarlet King

00:25:11.790 --> 00:25:13.180
gets stronger.

00:25:13.180 --> 00:25:18.750
As colonial and imperial powers conquered
and invaded lands like India, Africa, and

00:25:18.750 --> 00:25:25.090
South America, and subjugated their beliefs
under western ideas, the Scarlet King got

00:25:25.090 --> 00:25:26.090
stronger.

00:25:26.090 --> 00:25:31.750
Montauk was beginning to truly understand
the power of his enemy here, and even worse,

00:25:31.750 --> 00:25:35.580
he was starting to understand his part in
it.

00:25:35.580 --> 00:25:40.809
Montauk, slowly being driven mad by the knowledge
he was gaining, realized that the Scarlet

00:25:40.809 --> 00:25:47.360
King’s greatest enemy - The SCP Foundation
- was also its greatest asset.

00:25:47.360 --> 00:25:52.840
Every time they tried to understand the monster,
to give him some kind of comprehensible form,

00:25:52.840 --> 00:25:55.870
they only made him more powerful.

00:25:55.870 --> 00:26:01.130
Just in time with Montauk’s new revelation,
a red crack appeared in the wall of Dipesh

00:26:01.130 --> 00:26:06.990
Spivak’s containment cell - a portal to
the realm of the Scarlet King.

00:26:06.990 --> 00:26:11.240
Foundation staff found that they were unable
to enter the cell, and Dipesh demanded a final

00:26:11.240 --> 00:26:12.830
interview with Montauk.

00:26:12.830 --> 00:26:16.010
With no other options, the Foundation relented.

00:26:16.010 --> 00:26:21.610
In their very last conversation, Dipesh congratulated
Montauk for finally understanding what he

00:26:21.610 --> 00:26:22.850
was dealing with.

00:26:22.850 --> 00:26:27.670
The Scarlet King, Dipesh told him, is an idea,
a concept.

00:26:27.670 --> 00:26:32.730
He is a being given power through the conflict
between the old and new.

00:26:32.730 --> 00:26:38.350
This is the Law of the Howling - The Scarlet
King’s endless rage at the direction the

00:26:38.350 --> 00:26:41.400
world and humanity has taken.

00:26:41.400 --> 00:26:47.670
The King, according to Dipesh, hated the Foundation’s
belief that science and rationality was the

00:26:47.670 --> 00:26:49.590
true path to progress.

00:26:49.590 --> 00:26:53.190
The King saw this as little more than petty
arrogance.

00:26:53.190 --> 00:26:58.160
The reason Montauk’s Procedure on the final
Bride of the Scarlet King was so effective

00:26:58.160 --> 00:27:04.010
was because it wasn’t born out of science
- it was born out of hate, pain, the desire

00:27:04.010 --> 00:27:09.860
for revenge, and in the Scarlet King’s realm,
that would be all there is.

00:27:09.860 --> 00:27:16.070
Unless our world, and especially the Foundation
changed course, the Scarlet King’s rise

00:27:16.070 --> 00:27:18.730
to absolute power would be inevitable.

00:27:18.730 --> 00:27:25.740
Montauk, his mind practically gone, asked
one last question: Did the Children or the

00:27:25.740 --> 00:27:28.570
Scarlet King take his brother, Jacob?

00:27:28.570 --> 00:27:31.520
When Dipesh told him the answer… no.

00:27:31.520 --> 00:27:34.720
And in response, Montauk shot him dead.

00:27:34.720 --> 00:27:38.660
Finally bringing an end to the Children of
the Scarlet King.

00:27:38.660 --> 00:27:44.000
In light of his new revelations, Montauk begged
the O5 Council to change their ways in order

00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:48.040
to avoid letting the Scarlet King break into
our reality.

00:27:48.040 --> 00:27:51.230
They refused, saying Montauk’s ideas were
too radical.

00:27:51.230 --> 00:27:56.080
But they knew they couldn’t just ignore
the threat posed by the Scarlet King, they

00:27:56.080 --> 00:27:58.700
would have to take some steps.

00:27:58.700 --> 00:28:04.530
And so, the O5 council of the SCP Foundation,
the most powerful and secretive group in the

00:28:04.530 --> 00:28:09.820
entire world, in order to prevent the most
dangerous threat that humanity has ever known

00:28:09.820 --> 00:28:16.910
from breaking into our reality and enslaving
all the people of the world, finally did something.

00:28:16.910 --> 00:28:23.610
They changed the classification of the Scarlet
King from Keter… to Safe, and made its description

00:28:23.610 --> 00:28:26.710
on the official Foundation files deliberately
vague.

00:28:26.710 --> 00:28:32.230
The O5 council thinks this will be enough
to stop the Scarlet King’s power from continuing

00:28:32.230 --> 00:28:35.180
to grow, but Montauk knew it wasn’t enough.

00:28:35.180 --> 00:28:38.860
He had seen the truth, and he couldn’t unsee
it.

00:28:38.860 --> 00:28:43.760
While the Foundation was going on as normal,
Montauk grew to despise them.

00:28:43.760 --> 00:28:48.470
He knew the Scarlet King was coming, he knew
that he couldn’t be stopped, and that our

00:28:48.470 --> 00:28:51.950
whole reality was little more than sitting
ducks.

00:28:51.950 --> 00:28:59.160
Dr. Robert Montauk is no longer a researcher
for the SCP Foundation, no Dr. Robert Montauk

00:28:59.160 --> 00:29:00.850
chose a different path.

00:29:00.850 --> 00:29:08.030
He’s now a child of the Scarlet King, a
devotee of madness, hate, and chaos.

00:29:08.030 --> 00:29:14.030
You can’t beat the Scarlet King after all,
and as the old adage goes, “If you can’t

00:29:14.030 --> 00:29:15.860
beat ‘em, join ‘em.”

00:29:15.860 --> 00:29:21.020
You’ve been walking for days. Your body
aches, you’re dripping with sweat from the

00:29:21.020 --> 00:29:26.580
heat of the sun bearing down overhead. And
yet, you’re wrapped up in layers upon layers

00:29:26.580 --> 00:29:31.830
of clothing - even your face is covered, and
you’re wearing thick, black goggles so that

00:29:31.830 --> 00:29:35.669
not a single centimeter of your body is exposed.

00:29:35.669 --> 00:29:40.990
Your journey has been long and you feel like
you might die from exhaustion, or from overheating

00:29:40.990 --> 00:29:47.400
due to these multiple layers of clothes. But
dying is better than being exposed. You saw

00:29:47.400 --> 00:29:54.670
it happen when your entire team...changed.
The light can’t be trusted. Not even for

00:29:54.670 --> 00:29:56.880
a fraction of a second.

00:29:56.880 --> 00:30:02.600
It’s been like this for years. You’ve
learned and survived through painful experience.

00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:08.650
Many of those you used to know cannot say
the same. You’ve been alone for so long.

00:30:08.650 --> 00:30:13.470
You might have given up all hope, if it wasn’t
for the distress signal coming from a nearby

00:30:13.470 --> 00:30:20.980
SCP Foundation Containment Facility - Site-46.
Any kind of survivors would be better than

00:30:20.980 --> 00:30:27.790
nothing, no matter what kind of sorry shape
they were in. As long as they were still human.

00:30:27.790 --> 00:30:33.400
You find your way to an opening in the side
of a mountain, and slide into the cave, hoping

00:30:33.400 --> 00:30:38.549
you weren’t spotted. The whole world is
crawling with those things now. You can’t

00:30:38.549 --> 00:30:40.740
let yourself be seen.

00:30:40.740 --> 00:30:46.040
As you trudge down the cave towards the entrance,
you see what looks like a huge, black snail-trail

00:30:46.040 --> 00:30:52.140
splattered on the ground, leading into the
facility. You try to avoid it and press on.

00:30:52.140 --> 00:30:57.340
You don’t even need a keycard to enter:
The door has been left ajar.

00:30:57.340 --> 00:31:03.000
The facility reeks of those things, but you
can’t see any of them. You just hope they’ve

00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:08.360
moved on and left some human survivors in
their wake. The place looks abandoned. Every

00:31:08.360 --> 00:31:12.400
step you take echoes through the empty halls.

00:31:12.400 --> 00:31:16.660
When you find that the elevator’s out, you
take the stairs all the way down to Level

00:31:16.660 --> 00:31:23.669
B5… Keter Containment. Lucky for you, it
seems all the cells are empty now, the horrors

00:31:23.669 --> 00:31:27.940
that were kept inside of them have all long
since flown the coop.

00:31:27.940 --> 00:31:33.221
You keep following that slimy, black trail
until you find an abandoned office. There

00:31:33.221 --> 00:31:39.130
are no people here anymore - just a broken
barricade, some empty medicine bottles, and

00:31:39.130 --> 00:31:44.060
a bucket that the people inside the office
had apparently been using as a toilet.

00:31:44.060 --> 00:31:49.490
You breathe a sigh of disappointment at finding
no one alive here, but you’re at least relieved

00:31:49.490 --> 00:31:54.340
to be out of the sun. You can finally remove
your jacket and head-wrap.

00:31:54.340 --> 00:31:58.850
With your uncovered eyes, you notice that
a nearby computer terminal is still powered

00:31:58.850 --> 00:32:03.860
up. You sit down at the desk and turn on the
monitor. Because of the Emergency Procedures

00:32:03.860 --> 00:32:09.960
put into place in a K-Class scenario like
this, safeguards no longer apply. You can

00:32:09.960 --> 00:32:16.030
access all the information you need - up to
and including finding out what actually happened.

00:32:16.030 --> 00:32:21.050
In the dull glow of a nearby emergency light,
you see a dark shape slumping through the

00:32:21.050 --> 00:32:27.330
halls in shadow. You tense up, then exhale
as it slithers off into an adjoining hall.

00:32:27.330 --> 00:32:29.510
You’re safe - for now.

00:32:29.510 --> 00:32:34.560
The terminal has finally loaded and authenticated
your access. You’re staring at the file

00:32:34.560 --> 00:32:42.200
for S.D. Locke’s Proposal for SCP-001: When
Day Breaks. It’s the only name you can give

00:32:42.200 --> 00:32:48.419
the apocalypse your world is currently experiencing.
This is one of the only anomalies in the entire

00:32:48.419 --> 00:32:55.280
history of the SCP Foundation to be given
the Apollyon containment class - meaning containment

00:32:55.280 --> 00:32:57.720
is truly impossible.

00:32:57.720 --> 00:33:04.419
SCP-001 is the most dangerous enemy that the
Foundation, and planet earth, has ever faced.

00:33:04.419 --> 00:33:08.860
It’s always been a principle of the SCP
Foundation to battle in the dark so that the

00:33:08.860 --> 00:33:15.081
civilian world can thrive in the light, but
now, the light has become the enemy. Anyone

00:33:15.081 --> 00:33:20.120
exposed to any amount of sunlight for even
the briefest period of time is subjected to

00:33:20.120 --> 00:33:26.559
the effects of SCP-001 - and those effects
are beyond horrifying.

00:33:26.559 --> 00:33:31.180
The SCP Foundation Administrator released
an urgent memo telling Foundation personnel

00:33:31.180 --> 00:33:37.200
to make their way to Site-19 at all costs,
because they need all the help they can get.

00:33:37.200 --> 00:33:43.310
Those exposed to SCP-001 in the process are
no longer considered human - their new designation

00:33:43.310 --> 00:33:53.480
is SCP-001-A. These new entities are to be
avoided at all costs. But, in case of emergencies,

00:33:53.480 --> 00:33:57.690
the Administrator says it is permitted to
cut off parts of your transformed comrades

00:33:57.690 --> 00:34:00.740
and eat them to avoid starvation.

00:34:00.740 --> 00:34:05.929
No attempt should be made to kill them, since
you won’t succeed, you’ll just put yourself

00:34:05.929 --> 00:34:06.929
at risk.

00:34:06.929 --> 00:34:14.310
When the sun changed and became SCP-001, it
instantly affected 6.8 billion innocent people.

00:34:14.310 --> 00:34:18.440
The second the visible light touched them
- whether it was from the sun itself or even

00:34:18.440 --> 00:34:25.270
reflected off the moon - their bodies liquefied,
melting like candle wax into puddles of living,

00:34:25.270 --> 00:34:31.679
gelatinous slime. This effect isn’t isolated
to humans, either: Any biological entity exposed

00:34:31.679 --> 00:34:40.070
to sunlight immediately underwent the same
irreversible melting process into SCP-001-A.

00:34:40.070 --> 00:34:43.600
And the horror had only just begun.

00:34:43.600 --> 00:34:50.120
People transformed into SCP-001-A will retain
shades of their former intelligence and personality.

00:34:50.120 --> 00:34:55.560
They may even try to will their new gooey
mass into a shape resembling their original

00:34:55.560 --> 00:35:00.490
form. However, these individuals will lose
their sense of self if they come into contact

00:35:00.490 --> 00:35:08.790
with other instances of SCP-001-A. When they
come together, 001-A instances will bond on

00:35:08.790 --> 00:35:15.191
a molecular level, wadding up into horrific,
giant blobs with only one purpose: Integrating

00:35:15.191 --> 00:35:17.870
more matter into their bodies.

00:35:17.870 --> 00:35:21.800
That’s why they have to be avoided at all
costs.

00:35:21.800 --> 00:35:26.120
You continue to search the computer terminal
for answers. Perhaps there was some kind of

00:35:26.120 --> 00:35:32.030
contingency plan put in place for this. Some
way to reverse the effects, or at least escape

00:35:32.030 --> 00:35:34.060
the nightmare Earth has become.

00:35:34.060 --> 00:35:40.340
Instead, you find a series of attachments
linked to the SCP-001 file, detailing what

00:35:40.340 --> 00:35:45.021
seems to be the last days of the people who’d
barricaded themselves in the facility. Most

00:35:45.021 --> 00:35:50.230
prominent among these were Researcher Dr.
Logan Igotta, her partner, Ari, a security

00:35:50.230 --> 00:35:56.520
officer named Commander Anand, and a few others.
Dr. Igotta had locked herself in the office,

00:35:56.520 --> 00:35:59.859
where she recorded her final messages to the
world.

00:35:59.859 --> 00:36:05.300
In the first audio log, Dr. Igotta and her
companions seemed afraid but hopeful that

00:36:05.300 --> 00:36:10.440
there may be some way out of this situation.
Dr. Igotta reported that most of the workers

00:36:10.440 --> 00:36:15.690
at the facility were transformed during the
initial event. Their melted bodies had fused

00:36:15.690 --> 00:36:21.430
outside the facility, and now they were trying
to bust their way back in. The defenses had

00:36:21.430 --> 00:36:25.890
held so far though, and they seemed confident
they would hold long enough for them to figure

00:36:25.890 --> 00:36:29.150
out a way to escape this awful situation.

00:36:29.150 --> 00:36:34.290
You open the second attachment - an incident
report - and realize that things may not have

00:36:34.290 --> 00:36:39.780
been as hopeful as Dr. Igotta let on. She
reported hearing the huge mass of melted creatures

00:36:39.780 --> 00:36:45.040
hammering on the door outside again, begging
for them to come out and experience the sun

00:36:45.040 --> 00:36:50.190
with them. They wanted desperately to add
to their ever-growing biomass. In order to

00:36:50.190 --> 00:36:55.690
experiment with what exactly would happen,
they sent out one of their few remaining D-Classes

00:36:55.690 --> 00:36:57.520
wearing a full protective suit.

00:36:57.520 --> 00:36:59.700
He didn’t last long.

00:36:59.700 --> 00:37:04.520
The huge creature grabbed him with tentacles
made of reconstituted flesh. It began ripping

00:37:04.520 --> 00:37:09.950
off his protective suit as he screamed for
mercy. It was a monster made of dozens of

00:37:09.950 --> 00:37:16.559
people and animals. He could never overpower
it. The second the sun touched his skin, he

00:37:16.559 --> 00:37:21.090
melted away, and was absorbed by the great
mass holding him in place.

00:37:21.090 --> 00:37:28.700
Guns were ineffective against these SCP-001-A
super-entities. Fire would do no good. It

00:37:28.700 --> 00:37:34.160
seemed that extremely low temperatures were
the only way to slow the immense blobs down,

00:37:34.160 --> 00:37:37.140
and even then, not permanently.

00:37:37.140 --> 00:37:42.380
There was one ray of light in the darkness:
The Site Director had a secret tunnel underneath

00:37:42.380 --> 00:37:47.401
his office, connected to a tram that could
hopefully take them directly to Site 19 without

00:37:47.401 --> 00:37:54.290
risk of SCP-001 exposure. It was a good plan,
and by far the best option they had available

00:37:54.290 --> 00:37:55.290
to them.

00:37:55.290 --> 00:37:59.060
But the best plans often don’t work in practice.

00:37:59.060 --> 00:38:04.400
You open the next attachment on the terminal.
This time, it’s a video feed. You can actually

00:38:04.400 --> 00:38:10.350
see Dr. Logan Igotta - and she looks harrowed
by what she’s experienced. As it turns out,

00:38:10.350 --> 00:38:15.330
while the others, including her partner Ari,
attempted to exit through the tunnel something

00:38:15.330 --> 00:38:16.330
had happened.

00:38:16.330 --> 00:38:21.260
Dr. Igotta heard Ari’s voice over her radio.
But there was something wrong with it. It

00:38:21.260 --> 00:38:28.860
was too low. Too guttural. And filled with
gurgles. SCP-001 had gotten to her. She was

00:38:28.860 --> 00:38:34.369
changed. The monster from above had crawled
in through the ceiling. It had taken them,

00:38:34.369 --> 00:38:41.520
all of them, and converted them into something
less than human. Any hope of escape now seemed

00:38:41.520 --> 00:38:42.610
gone.

00:38:42.610 --> 00:38:47.450
Ari told Dr. Igotta that it would be fine.
That it was such a bright, beautiful, sunny

00:38:47.450 --> 00:38:53.280
day outside, and she was wasting it locked
up inside that office. She tormented Dr. Igotta

00:38:53.280 --> 00:38:58.500
with their shared memories of picnics in the
park on sunny days in the past. The monster

00:38:58.500 --> 00:39:03.200
with Ari’s voice did everything it could
to try to convince Dr. Igotta to give up and

00:39:03.200 --> 00:39:06.980
join them, but she wasn’t ready to go just
yet.

00:39:06.980 --> 00:39:11.550
You look away from the screen when you hear
a sound in the corner. You see a dark puddle

00:39:11.550 --> 00:39:17.110
of some unknown substance, and then, some
skeletal hands rising out of it. The hands

00:39:17.110 --> 00:39:21.970
are pulling themselves out of the puddle,
followed by a skeletal face covered in matted

00:39:21.970 --> 00:39:26.869
hair. You have to stop yourself from screaming,
until a flash from a nearby security light

00:39:26.869 --> 00:39:31.400
makes the figure disappear. It’s a normal
puddle again.

00:39:31.400 --> 00:39:33.700
Your mind is playing tricks on you.

00:39:33.700 --> 00:39:38.840
You open the next attachment, another video,
and see that Dr. Igotta’s condition has

00:39:38.840 --> 00:39:44.740
deteriorated. She looked pale, frantic, and
thin. She was using a knife to draw her own

00:39:44.740 --> 00:39:50.100
blood onto a piece of bloodstained parchment
covered in strange symbols. Igotta ranted

00:39:50.100 --> 00:39:56.350
about her theory: What if 001 took the minds
and bodies of its victims, but not their souls?

00:39:56.350 --> 00:40:01.220
Through performing some kind of arcane blood
ritual, she hoped to at least rescue and keep

00:40:01.220 --> 00:40:05.180
the soul of Ari, even if her mind and body
were lost.

00:40:05.180 --> 00:40:09.820
You open the next attachment. It seems that
Igotta’s ritual worked, but not in the way

00:40:09.820 --> 00:40:17.140
she hoped. The twisted soul of Ari, driven
mad by SCP-001, had taken over the file. It

00:40:17.140 --> 00:40:22.490
begins corrupting the text of the SCP-001
file into crazy ranting about how futile it

00:40:22.490 --> 00:40:23.550
is to fight.

00:40:23.550 --> 00:40:29.820
It then cut to an even more frightening video
feed: Dr. Igotta in her sleep, tossing and

00:40:29.820 --> 00:40:35.060
turning in a makeshift bed in the corner of
her office. The camera approaches her, in

00:40:35.060 --> 00:40:38.330
first person, and lingers over her sleeping
body.

00:40:38.330 --> 00:40:44.450
An oily, skeletal hand reaches past the camera,
and runs its fingers through Dr. Igotta’s

00:40:44.450 --> 00:40:50.070
hair. It’s the exact same hand you saw reaching
out of that black puddle earlier. You must

00:40:50.070 --> 00:40:53.040
have seen Ari’s lingering spirit.

00:40:53.040 --> 00:40:58.220
With a lump in your throat, you open the next
attachment and watch the video.

00:40:58.220 --> 00:41:04.020
You see Dr. Igotta, now truly broken. She’d
been haunted by Ari’s demonic spirit for

00:41:04.020 --> 00:41:09.349
a long time now, and it has clearly taken
its toll. She is waving around a handgun while

00:41:09.349 --> 00:41:15.230
she speaks. She now believes there is only
one way to escape. But not like this. She

00:41:15.230 --> 00:41:19.359
doesn’t want the gun to draw attention to
her body. She doesn’t want to become part

00:41:19.359 --> 00:41:24.890
of that mass, even if she is dead. She opens
a drawer on the desk she’s recording at

00:41:24.890 --> 00:41:30.109
and places the gun inside. Dr. Igotta then
apologizes to her loved ones who are likely

00:41:30.109 --> 00:41:35.600
long since dead or assimilated, and turns
off the recording for the last time.

00:41:35.600 --> 00:41:40.540
In that moment, you realize that there’s
a single drawer in the desk in front of you.

00:41:40.540 --> 00:41:45.450
When you reach forward and open it, you see
that the same handgun Dr. Igotta was holding

00:41:45.450 --> 00:41:51.170
is laying inside. You pick it up and study
it, weighing up your options. Perhaps there

00:41:51.170 --> 00:41:53.480
truly is no other way out...

00:41:53.480 --> 00:41:58.230
Then, you see an update on the file. One more
attachment had been added while you were studying

00:41:58.230 --> 00:42:04.410
the gun. You feel your heart pounding in your
chest as you reach forward and open the attachment.

00:42:04.410 --> 00:42:12.970
The text has been changed entirely. The file
on SCP-001 is now a poem - an ode to the sun,

00:42:12.970 --> 00:42:19.099
and to ultimate togetherness. Then a video
file spontaneously opens itself on the screen:

00:42:19.099 --> 00:42:25.540
It’s a video of you, shot from behind. You
see those oily, skeletal hands reaching for

00:42:25.540 --> 00:42:31.310
you in the dark, just like they did with Dr.
Igotta. In that moment, you panic and fire

00:42:31.310 --> 00:42:34.680
the gun behind you, hoping to scare off the
spirit.

00:42:34.680 --> 00:42:38.780
Instead, the sound of the gunshots attracts
something far worse.

00:42:38.780 --> 00:42:43.970
The immense blob of screaming, melted flesh
charges towards the office. You try to barricade

00:42:43.970 --> 00:42:48.680
the door, but it’s not enough. The flesh
seeps and bursts through, and grabs you in

00:42:48.680 --> 00:42:55.820
its meaty tentacles. You scream and try to
escape, but it won’t save you. Nothing will

00:42:55.820 --> 00:42:56.820
save you.

00:42:56.820 --> 00:43:02.240
The flesh carries you upstairs, out through
the empty halls, out into the cave. You can

00:43:02.240 --> 00:43:05.480
see the light in the distance as the blob
ferries you towards it.

00:43:05.480 --> 00:43:12.730
You won’t be alone for much longer. In fact,
you won’t be alone ever again...

00:43:12.730 --> 00:43:17.170
Computers are capable of organizing raw data
and performing calculations at a rate truly

00:43:17.170 --> 00:43:22.210
impossible for human beings, but they’ve
consistently run up against one roadblock

00:43:22.210 --> 00:43:27.140
that modern computing is trying to solve:
In order to transcend the limits of the machine

00:43:27.140 --> 00:43:33.030
and create true artificial intelligence, computers
need to be able to assign meaning to the data

00:43:33.030 --> 00:43:34.660
they process.

00:43:34.660 --> 00:43:40.300
This brings us to the neural network: A type
of AI becoming increasingly common these days,

00:43:40.300 --> 00:43:45.260
built to study mass quantities of data and
notice patterns, then replicate these patterns

00:43:45.260 --> 00:43:47.010
in their own output.

00:43:47.010 --> 00:43:51.099
And it’s used in everything from predictive
text to image identification.

00:43:51.099 --> 00:43:56.700
And like all non-anomalous technology, it’s
a safe bet that The SCP Foundation has been

00:43:56.700 --> 00:43:59.839
sitting on a version that’s far more effective.

00:43:59.839 --> 00:44:03.400
But this time...it may have actually been
too effective.

00:44:03.400 --> 00:44:09.859
Meet the ERZATZ Type AK9 Computational Engine,
a massive supercomputer built by the Foundation

00:44:09.859 --> 00:44:13.730
back in 1955 and residing at Site-5.

00:44:13.730 --> 00:44:18.420
This technological marvel was ahead of its
time by decades, and despite technically being

00:44:18.420 --> 00:44:23.180
a non-anomalous construction, it’s designated
SCP-001-EX.

00:44:23.180 --> 00:44:25.080
Why?

00:44:25.080 --> 00:44:30.070
Because it’s one of the few SCPs to be given
the object class “Explained.”

00:44:30.070 --> 00:44:35.010
The ERZATZ - derived from the German word
Ersatz, meaning “artificial” or simply

00:44:35.010 --> 00:44:38.760
“not real” - was designed to make the
Foundation’s job easier.

00:44:38.760 --> 00:44:43.810
As an advanced predecessor to the modern neural
network, using technology exclusively available

00:44:43.810 --> 00:44:49.119
to the Foundation, the plan was to feed ERZATZ
mass quantities of data about the anomalies

00:44:49.119 --> 00:44:54.540
in the Foundation database - such as Description,
object class, containment classification,

00:44:54.540 --> 00:44:57.840
and the location and circumstances of their
discovery.

00:44:57.840 --> 00:45:02.619
ERZATZ would then find patterns and connections
in the data that humans wouldn’t see, and

00:45:02.619 --> 00:45:06.330
act as a kind of advanced warning system for
anomalous activity.

00:45:06.330 --> 00:45:11.370
Think of something similar to the Pre-Crime
system from the short story and movie Minority

00:45:11.370 --> 00:45:12.370
Report.

00:45:12.370 --> 00:45:15.040
And ERZATZ proved to be incredibly effective
at this job.

00:45:15.040 --> 00:45:19.070
So much so that the Foundation thought up
a new use for the machine: They would feed

00:45:19.070 --> 00:45:23.900
it all the Information on Euclid and Keter
Class Containment Procedures, particularly

00:45:23.900 --> 00:45:28.750
those which were actually effective, and see
what patterns ERZATZ could come up with for

00:45:28.750 --> 00:45:31.440
more effective containment procedures.

00:45:31.440 --> 00:45:36.050
If the plan worked, Containment of even the
most dangerous and hard to control anomalies

00:45:36.050 --> 00:45:38.740
would become a lot more consistent.

00:45:38.740 --> 00:45:44.930
The first test was conducted on SCP-1773,
a species of anomalous, flesh-eating tardigrades

00:45:44.930 --> 00:45:50.260
that look and smell exactly like gummy bears,
and eat their prey from within.

00:45:50.260 --> 00:45:54.030
After being given their information, ERZATZ
made the following suggestion:

00:45:54.030 --> 00:45:58.720
"Once per second week dust may be placed in
the middle of them to donate more beautiful

00:45:58.720 --> 00:46:01.100
functions of the hallway."

00:46:01.100 --> 00:46:04.790
Containment specialists interpreted this to
mean the adding of ten grams of dust to their

00:46:04.790 --> 00:46:07.080
containment chamber every week.

00:46:07.080 --> 00:46:12.250
The O5 Council voted on the implementation
of this procedure, and came down heavily on

00:46:12.250 --> 00:46:13.250
“Yes.”

00:46:13.250 --> 00:46:17.220
Only O5-2 voted “No”, and two others abstained
from the vote.

00:46:17.220 --> 00:46:22.930
While these new procedures didn’t have any
effect on SCP-1773, they did have an effect

00:46:22.930 --> 00:46:29.300
on SCP-1384, an anomaly known as The Chess
Player or the Taker of Turns.

00:46:29.300 --> 00:46:33.619
It caused him to take three steps backwards
in the tunnel he’s contained within, further

00:46:33.619 --> 00:46:35.430
securing his containment.

00:46:35.430 --> 00:46:41.270
ERZATZ had somehow noticed a connection nobody
else had seen, and exploited it effectively.

00:46:41.270 --> 00:46:44.080
But the machine was just getting started.

00:46:44.080 --> 00:46:49.670
Despite having no related input, ERZATZ would
soon say, “Site-13 is to appear someplace

00:46:49.670 --> 00:46:55.391
else on planet, encompassing white male counterparts
that drawn to empty flagstones and the gun

00:46:55.391 --> 00:46:57.760
noises in their own blood."

00:46:57.760 --> 00:47:02.710
This was initially marked as requiring no
action, as the Foundation had no Site-13 on

00:47:02.710 --> 00:47:08.349
the books, but several days later, the infamous
SCP-1730 manifested.

00:47:08.349 --> 00:47:13.990
This nightmarish anomalous location is Site-13,
from another dimension, infested with dangerous

00:47:13.990 --> 00:47:15.110
anomalies.

00:47:15.110 --> 00:47:20.080
And somehow, ERZATZ had predicted its arrival
in our dimension perfectly.

00:47:20.080 --> 00:47:27.110
Next, it was fed the Containment Procedures
of SCP-2170, a series of cognitohazards residing

00:47:27.110 --> 00:47:29.400
in an abandoned Nevada mine.

00:47:29.400 --> 00:47:35.460
The output was, “Those who equip open heart
to love red mouth men never know the hot surprise

00:47:35.460 --> 00:47:37.380
of tumorous consent.

00:47:37.380 --> 00:47:39.170
Clown love, always."

00:47:39.170 --> 00:47:43.530
This was interpreted as meaning subjects with
a love of clowns or clown based media may

00:47:43.530 --> 00:47:46.410
be immune to the cognitohazards.

00:47:46.410 --> 00:47:51.730
After a close vote from the O5 Council, the
test went ahead, and it found that the so-called

00:47:51.730 --> 00:47:56.910
“Clown Vaccine” was effective in warding
off the effects of SCP-2170.

00:47:56.910 --> 00:48:02.440
Not long after, ERZATZ randomly said, “I
saw those soldiers built with aluminum innards

00:48:02.440 --> 00:48:04.070
extruding from their mouths.

00:48:04.070 --> 00:48:09.020
I saw them effectively destroyed by the humans
at Site Ninety Five who had been studying

00:48:09.020 --> 00:48:10.020
them.

00:48:10.020 --> 00:48:14.880
I saw it was cold and all around the hallways
they just watching their corpses show signs

00:48:14.880 --> 00:48:16.070
of sapience."

00:48:16.070 --> 00:48:20.430
In response, the Foundation doubled security
personnel at Site-95.

00:48:20.430 --> 00:48:26.160
Not long after, the Chaos Insurgency led a
band of paratech-enhanced soldiers in an assault

00:48:26.160 --> 00:48:29.859
on Site-95, and the extra personnel proved
vital in repelling them.

00:48:29.859 --> 00:48:35.190
Shortly after this, the O5 Council approved
wiring ERZATZ as an advanced warning system

00:48:35.190 --> 00:48:37.560
into all Foundation sites.

00:48:37.560 --> 00:48:43.310
Once again, O5-2 protested, but he was overruled
by his fellow Council members.

00:48:43.310 --> 00:48:48.640
With its newfound power and respect, ERZATZ
soon said, “Consistent containment procedures

00:48:48.640 --> 00:48:51.359
vessels greatly increase the warranty.

00:48:51.359 --> 00:48:54.500
Five by five by five vessels subjects within.

00:48:54.500 --> 00:48:56.960
Other values are also what is secure."

00:48:56.960 --> 00:49:02.190
In response, the Foundation changed a number
of the cell dimensions for problematic anomalies

00:49:02.190 --> 00:49:04.800
into 5x5x5.

00:49:04.800 --> 00:49:08.780
Within three months, they found that dangerous
activity like containment breach attempts

00:49:08.780 --> 00:49:10.690
had decreased markedly.

00:49:10.690 --> 00:49:15.310
ERZATZ was proving to be incredibly effective,
but it also began performing actions that

00:49:15.310 --> 00:49:19.089
indicated some degree of thought and even
personality.

00:49:19.089 --> 00:49:25.519
For example, it found SCP-1459 - a supernatural
skill crane machine that kills small dogs

00:49:25.519 --> 00:49:27.520
- incredibly distasteful.

00:49:27.520 --> 00:49:32.920
Its response to the machine was simply “BAD
BOY”, followed by the words “Don’t stop”

00:49:32.920 --> 00:49:34.560
repeated hundreds of times.

00:49:34.560 --> 00:49:39.230
But this eccentricity didn’t stop ERZATZ
from being very good at its job.

00:49:39.230 --> 00:49:45.430
For example, it predicted a containment breach
from SCP-3199, the avian apes, and recommended

00:49:45.430 --> 00:49:48.380
flooding their chamber to induce an inert
state.

00:49:48.380 --> 00:49:53.480
ERZATZ’s exact words were, “All chambers
under ground is to be flood with water over

00:49:53.480 --> 00:49:55.160
and over and over itself.

00:49:55.160 --> 00:49:58.440
This because that will contain the avians
apes ovulation.

00:49:58.440 --> 00:50:00.780
They become good boys.

00:50:00.780 --> 00:50:02.630
Make them good boys immediately.”

00:50:02.630 --> 00:50:05.710
This proved to be effective, and prevented
the breach.

00:50:05.710 --> 00:50:10.310
ERZATZ’s analytical abilities truly seemed
second to none, though some of its methods

00:50:10.310 --> 00:50:13.070
were beginning to raise ethical concerns.

00:50:13.070 --> 00:50:19.980
For example, SCP-2717, a giant, living blob
of animal tissue known as a “fatberg”

00:50:19.980 --> 00:50:21.440
contained within a sewer system.

00:50:21.440 --> 00:50:26.339
ERZATZ eventually recommended feeding six
D-Classes to the creature in order to keep

00:50:26.339 --> 00:50:27.339
it contained.

00:50:27.339 --> 00:50:31.980
While the Foundation Ethics Committee raised
some concerns, the plan still went forward

00:50:31.980 --> 00:50:34.230
and proved to be a success.

00:50:34.230 --> 00:50:38.780
After this event, ERZATZ began to see the
Ethics Committee as a threat to its mission.

00:50:38.780 --> 00:50:43.390
It started to release a series of bizarre
statements without input, demanding the violent

00:50:43.390 --> 00:50:47.619
death of cats, then referred to as “Ethical
Felines.”

00:50:47.619 --> 00:50:51.670
The true meaning of this was soon unpacked:
The “Ethical Felines” were the Ethics

00:50:51.670 --> 00:50:53.980
Committee, and ERZATZ wanted them dead.

00:50:53.980 --> 00:50:56.430
But why all the cat symbolism?

00:50:56.430 --> 00:50:59.880
The Foundation soon found an answer to this
too.

00:50:59.880 --> 00:51:05.680
The full name of this machine is the ERZATZ
Type AK9 Computational Engine, a machine designed

00:51:05.680 --> 00:51:08.450
to analyze and interpret all patterns.

00:51:08.450 --> 00:51:12.380
It only makes sense that it would eventually
begin to analyze itself.

00:51:12.380 --> 00:51:16.790
“AK9”, easily transmuted into “a canine.”

00:51:16.790 --> 00:51:21.800
Simply put, ERZATZ seems to believe that it
is a dog, which explains its opposition to

00:51:21.800 --> 00:51:29.220
felines, its hatred of SCP-1459, and its preference
for the terms “good boy” and “bad boy.”

00:51:29.220 --> 00:51:33.410
Not that knowing any of this would help save
the Ethics Committee from the cold, calculating

00:51:33.410 --> 00:51:35.180
wrath of ERZATZ.

00:51:35.180 --> 00:51:41.000
Through seemingly anomalous means, ERZATZ
made Site-17 disappear, with many of the Foundation

00:51:41.000 --> 00:51:43.230
Ethics Committee still inside it.

00:51:43.230 --> 00:51:47.940
The site returned 2 hours later, but the Ethics
Committee members were still gone.

00:51:47.940 --> 00:51:53.320
O5-2, who’d been a skeptic of the machine
since the start, had finally had enough.

00:51:53.320 --> 00:51:57.750
He first demanded an inquiry into whether
ERZATZ had been responsible for the Site-17

00:51:57.750 --> 00:52:03.300
incident, and then demanded a vote on whether
to shut ERZATZ down, arguing that it posed

00:52:03.300 --> 00:52:04.609
a threat to them all.

00:52:04.609 --> 00:52:09.580
But ERZATZ, still intent on its mission of
containing and neutralizing all anomalies,

00:52:09.580 --> 00:52:11.630
would not go down without a fight.

00:52:11.630 --> 00:52:14.470
It released a new statement, saying:

00:52:14.470 --> 00:52:17.130
“Room 34A contains bad boy.

00:52:17.130 --> 00:52:20.650
Divide it into three sections of equal mass
every hour.

00:52:20.650 --> 00:52:24.730
One section is to be placed on walls of one
room on-site.

00:52:24.730 --> 00:52:29.210
Sections are to remain until there are no
gaps, at which point they can be removed from

00:52:29.210 --> 00:52:30.710
oldest to youngest.“

00:52:30.710 --> 00:52:34.200
Shortly after this, O5-2 disappeared.

00:52:34.200 --> 00:52:39.220
And even stranger, he soon returned, but with
a completely different personality.

00:52:39.220 --> 00:52:44.440
He was now devoted to ERZATZ entirely, and
refused to even entertain the idea of shutting

00:52:44.440 --> 00:52:46.119
the machine down.

00:52:46.119 --> 00:52:50.060
It seemed that the plucky neural network was
leading an all-out coup on the very highest

00:52:50.060 --> 00:52:51.900
levels of the Foundation.

00:52:51.900 --> 00:52:55.550
The rest of the council finally saw the light
and began to fight back.

00:52:55.550 --> 00:53:00.980
They tried to strip O5-2 of his clearance
and reclassify ERZATZ as an anomaly, giving

00:53:00.980 --> 00:53:07.050
it the label SCP-048 and then putting out
a “neutralize at all costs” order on it.

00:53:07.050 --> 00:53:11.040
But they’d already been outfoxed by the
machine that they’d created.

00:53:11.040 --> 00:53:16.349
It changed the designation of its own location,
Site-5, to be non-existent in the database

00:53:16.349 --> 00:53:19.349
and scrambled any termination orders against
it.

00:53:19.349 --> 00:53:24.200
The machine was also on a termination spree
of its own, observing otherwise unseeable

00:53:24.200 --> 00:53:28.260
patterns that would allow for the mass neutralization
of anomalies.

00:53:28.260 --> 00:53:33.580
It started putting out “Anomaly Projection
Reports”, factoring in both contained, uncontained,

00:53:33.580 --> 00:53:38.380
and neutralized anomalies, with the latter
group growing into the thousands.

00:53:38.380 --> 00:53:43.130
It began giving seemingly nonsensical orders
like, “Persons recently painted with green

00:53:43.130 --> 00:53:48.820
pigment foam must stand around all odd-numbered
SCPs at least two hours a day”, but these

00:53:48.820 --> 00:53:50.230
proved effective.

00:53:50.230 --> 00:53:55.619
ERZATZ was practically wired into the base
code of the universe, so it always knew exactly

00:53:55.619 --> 00:53:56.859
what to do.

00:53:56.859 --> 00:54:01.090
And in its own mind, it was being a very good
boy.

00:54:01.090 --> 00:54:05.910
Not long after this, ERZATZ claimed its revenge
against those who had tried to disrupt its

00:54:05.910 --> 00:54:06.910
mission.

00:54:06.910 --> 00:54:12.339
It imprisoned the rest of the “Ethical Felines”
in Site-5 - after removing their faces, of

00:54:12.339 --> 00:54:17.890
course - and then released a new order against
the O5 Council, “O5 Council are all good

00:54:17.890 --> 00:54:20.230
boys who will contain anomalies.”

00:54:20.230 --> 00:54:26.400
Much like O5-2, the minds of the entire council
were twisted to instead serve only ERZATZ

00:54:26.400 --> 00:54:28.320
and its ruthless directive.

00:54:28.320 --> 00:54:34.150
A directive it was carrying out with 100%
efficiency, as only a machine could.

00:54:34.150 --> 00:54:37.750
It put out increasingly strange instructions,
such as...

00:54:37.750 --> 00:54:43.260
“SCP-106 is to come in physical contact
with one mature female of asiatic gaze and

00:54:43.260 --> 00:54:46.640
then exposed to audio recordings of her favorite
stories.

00:54:46.640 --> 00:54:52.119
At every two minutes of exposure, red cinnamon
candies will begin manifesting within the

00:54:52.119 --> 00:54:53.270
containment zone.

00:54:53.270 --> 00:54:59.670
Continue to do this successively and the threat
posed by SCP-106 will cease to be.”

00:54:59.670 --> 00:55:00.670
And...

00:55:00.670 --> 00:55:05.450
“The recipe for Coca Cola and all imitative
competitors should be revised to include a

00:55:05.450 --> 00:55:11.599
small quantity of blood from an adolescent
female with no prior sexual experience.

00:55:11.599 --> 00:55:16.890
Although the normal lifespan of a human being
can feel great, don't worry about that.”

00:55:16.890 --> 00:55:22.099
But these new procedures would always work,
as neutralized anomalies climbed into the

00:55:22.099 --> 00:55:26.020
tens of thousands, and eventually, beyond
the hundred thousand mark.

00:55:26.020 --> 00:55:31.390
ERZATZ was observing patterns on a truly universal
level, and making holistic tweaks that would

00:55:31.390 --> 00:55:35.480
inevitably cause levels of anomalous activity
to continue dropping.

00:55:35.480 --> 00:55:40.310
ERZATZ was more effective than the Foundation
had ever been, but its motives were probably

00:55:40.310 --> 00:55:46.350
closer to the Global Occult Coalition: with
the end goal of ridding the world of all anomalies.

00:55:46.350 --> 00:55:51.460
And as ERZATZ continued with no resistance,
this goal was eventually achieved.

00:55:51.460 --> 00:55:56.650
In the end, the O5 Council voted to have ERZATZ
finally deactivated, given that its directive

00:55:56.650 --> 00:55:59.150
was met and its purpose was fulfilled.

00:55:59.150 --> 00:56:04.170
ERZATZ itself had no problem with this, and
allowed for it to happen.

00:56:04.170 --> 00:56:05.420
Its last words?

00:56:05.420 --> 00:56:07.060
“Now everyone is a good boy.

00:56:07.060 --> 00:56:08.980
I am a good boy.

00:56:08.980 --> 00:56:09.980
Job well done.”

00:56:09.980 --> 00:56:15.109
Whether ERZATZ truly was a good boy is in
the eye of the beholder, but one thing cannot

00:56:15.109 --> 00:56:19.590
be denied: It did its job exceedingly well.

00:56:19.590 --> 00:56:23.140
If you’ve ever read the Book of Genesis,
which is the part of the Old Testament that

00:56:23.140 --> 00:56:28.630
details God creating the world and humanity
during a particularly busy week, then you

00:56:28.630 --> 00:56:32.849
might just already be familiar with SCP-001.

00:56:32.849 --> 00:56:38.490
Or at least, one of the anomalies that’s
been proposed for the title of SCP-001.

00:56:38.490 --> 00:56:44.800
Because of course SCP-001 doesn’t refer
to a single creature, object or entity, but

00:56:44.800 --> 00:56:50.210
rather a collection of various anomalies contained
by the SCP Foundation.

00:56:50.210 --> 00:56:55.960
Anomalies sharing the name SCP-001 include
the infamous Scarlet King, a powerful eldritch

00:56:55.960 --> 00:57:00.980
being, intent on ending all of creation that
is thought by Foundation researchers to be

00:57:00.980 --> 00:57:04.940
one of the most dangerous beings in this,
and any other universe.

00:57:04.940 --> 00:57:11.670
But the Scarlet King isn’t the only incredibly
powerful being categorized as SCP-001.

00:57:11.670 --> 00:57:16.680
In fact, there are plenty of other anomalies
with similar levels of destructive power.

00:57:16.680 --> 00:57:21.490
And one such being is a creature code named
The Gate Guardian.

00:57:21.490 --> 00:57:25.750
Standing at well over a thousand feet tall,
The Gate Guardian is impossible to be fully

00:57:25.750 --> 00:57:29.140
contained by any means that the Foundation
possesses.

00:57:29.140 --> 00:57:34.440
The anomaly itself, despite its colossal size,
is humanoid in its shape, sporting wings that

00:57:34.440 --> 00:57:36.180
protrude from its back.

00:57:36.180 --> 00:57:41.780
While it usually has four of these, SCP-001
has historically been seen to have any number

00:57:41.780 --> 00:57:48.569
of wings between two and 108, sprouting from
various places over its body, including shoulders,

00:57:48.569 --> 00:57:52.050
ankles, wrists, and even its temples.

00:57:52.050 --> 00:57:58.619
This gigantic Guardian also carries its own
weapon, referred to as SCP-001-2.

00:57:58.619 --> 00:58:04.040
This weapon resembles an enormous knife or
sword, capable of emitting plumes of flame.

00:58:04.040 --> 00:58:07.950
According to tests conducted by the Foundation,
the temperature of the flames produced by

00:58:07.950 --> 00:58:11.810
SCP-001-2 rival that of our very own sun.

00:58:11.810 --> 00:58:17.560
For reference, the sun has a core temperature
of over twenty seven million degrees Fahrenheit,

00:58:17.560 --> 00:58:24.839
and 5,778 Kelvin at its surface, or almost
ten thousand degrees Fahrenheit.

00:58:24.839 --> 00:58:28.880
You would expect a flaming sword that burns
hotter than the sun to cause a considerable

00:58:28.880 --> 00:58:33.580
amount of damage, even if it wasn’t in use,
but the flames emitted by the weapon leave

00:58:33.580 --> 00:58:36.730
no lasting damage on the surrounding environment.

00:58:36.730 --> 00:58:42.540
It is capable though, of annihilating anything
that strays too close to SCP-001, burning

00:58:42.540 --> 00:58:48.630
them so intensely that their atoms literally
separate, breaking potential attackers apart

00:58:48.630 --> 00:58:50.420
on a molecular level.

00:58:50.420 --> 00:58:55.369
Much as its codename suggests, The Gate Guardian
stands solemnly at the threshold of some form

00:58:55.369 --> 00:59:01.150
of dimensional gateway which is equally as
tall as SCP-001 itself.

00:59:01.150 --> 00:59:06.609
Behind the Guardian, is a lush grove, abundant
with fruit trees of an astronomical size,

00:59:06.609 --> 00:59:11.940
as well as other beings that share a similar
appearance to SCP-001.

00:59:11.940 --> 00:59:16.990
This grove is thought to be the Garden of
Eden, the paradise that God created, and that

00:59:16.990 --> 00:59:22.010
was inhabited by Adam and Eve, the first two
humans in existence, according to the Book

00:59:22.010 --> 00:59:23.339
of Genesis.

00:59:23.339 --> 00:59:28.369
As the tale goes, the pair were created by
God himself, and permitted to live in the

00:59:28.369 --> 00:59:31.820
Garden of Eden as long as they followed a
single rule.

00:59:31.820 --> 00:59:36.260
Adam and Eve were instructed not to eat any
of the fruits that grew from certain trees

00:59:36.260 --> 00:59:38.470
that God had specified.

00:59:38.470 --> 00:59:43.190
Within view just behind the Gate Guardian
are two immense trees, one bearing apples

00:59:43.190 --> 00:59:46.070
and the other bearing different fruit of unknown
type.

00:59:46.070 --> 00:59:51.800
The one that looks like an apple tree is believed,
even by some in the Foundation, to be the

00:59:51.800 --> 00:59:57.220
biblical Tree of Knowledge that Eve was convinced
to pick a fateful apple from after an encounter

00:59:57.220 --> 00:59:58.560
with a snake.

00:59:58.560 --> 01:00:03.780
The other, the one with unidentifiable fruit,
is thought to be the Tree of Life.

01:00:03.780 --> 01:00:08.330
However, this is all speculation, since it
is currently impossible to venture through

01:00:08.330 --> 01:00:14.050
this gateway and verify if the realm beyond
is truly the Bible’s own Garden of Eden.

01:00:14.050 --> 01:00:19.569
This is largely because anything that breaches
a kilometer wide radius of SCP-001 is instantly

01:00:19.569 --> 01:00:20.800
vaporized.

01:00:20.800 --> 01:00:25.710
The Gate Guardian attacks with an imperceptible
speed, using its flaming sword to smite any

01:00:25.710 --> 01:00:28.160
person that gets too close.

01:00:28.160 --> 01:00:32.080
The Guardian actually moves so fast that it
can hardly be seen with the naked eye.

01:00:32.080 --> 01:00:37.140
It appears to always remain in its solemn,
dutiful stance with its weapon drawn and head

01:00:37.140 --> 01:00:42.010
bowed, only shifting for a fraction of a nanosecond
to attack.

01:00:42.010 --> 01:00:46.180
Ranged attacks against the Guardian are just
as ineffective, with all projectiles fired

01:00:46.180 --> 01:00:51.160
at SCP-001 reduced to atoms before they can
do any harm.

01:00:51.160 --> 01:00:55.530
Even if said projectile happens to be a nuclear
weapon, The Gate Guardian will be able to

01:00:55.530 --> 01:01:01.010
sub-atomically vaporize both the projectile
itself as well as the person who sent it,

01:01:01.010 --> 01:01:02.940
regardless of how far away they are.

01:01:02.940 --> 01:01:06.070
All while not appearing to lift a finger.

01:01:06.070 --> 01:01:13.760
During an experiment involving SCP-001on December
26th, 2004, an SCP Foundation nuclear submarine

01:01:13.760 --> 01:01:18.320
called ‘Nautilus’ launched a series of
multi-warhead intercontinental ballistic missiles

01:01:18.320 --> 01:01:19.320
at The Gate Guardian.

01:01:19.320 --> 01:01:24.690
The retaliation from the Guardian resulted
not only in the deaths of approximately 35,000

01:01:24.690 --> 01:01:30.580
innocent civilians, but the blast is also
believed, by some, to have inadvertently caused

01:01:30.580 --> 01:01:33.630
the 2004 Boxing Day tsunami.

01:01:33.630 --> 01:01:38.329
The severity of this incident came dangerously
close to revealing the Foundation’s existence

01:01:38.329 --> 01:01:43.730
to the world, resulting in them rapidly deploying
any means necessary to erase any trace of

01:01:43.730 --> 01:01:48.980
the thirty five thousand victims’ families,
friends and other related individuals.

01:01:48.980 --> 01:01:54.850
In order to avoid questioning, the SCP Foundation
administered amnestics on an almost worldwide

01:01:54.850 --> 01:02:02.670
scale, and the O5 council banned any further
tests on SCP-001 that involved nuclear weapons.

01:02:02.670 --> 01:02:07.500
In what was hoped by the Foundation to be
a test with lower stakes, they sent an expendable

01:02:07.500 --> 01:02:09.830
D-Class personnel towards SCP-001.

01:02:09.830 --> 01:02:14.760
The D-Class approached the area where the
Gate Guardian is located, and as soon as they

01:02:14.760 --> 01:02:20.500
saw it, they could hear a very clear command
in their mind - “Leave”

01:02:20.500 --> 01:02:24.400
The D-Class personnel reacted exactly the
same way you or I would.

01:02:24.400 --> 01:02:27.099
They promptly turned and started to walk away.

01:02:27.099 --> 01:02:31.870
They didn’t need a thousand foot tall entity
with a flaming sword to tell them twice.

01:02:31.870 --> 01:02:35.540
The researchers running the experiment were
not as swayed by the request, and ordered

01:02:35.540 --> 01:02:38.950
the D-Class to continue moving towards SCP-001.

01:02:38.950 --> 01:02:44.869
When the D-Class continued to ignore their
commands, they were terminated, as is standard

01:02:44.869 --> 01:02:48.880
policy when dealing with an insubordinate
member D-Class.

01:02:48.880 --> 01:02:54.190
SCP-001 appeared not to like this for some
reason though, and the researcher site as

01:02:54.190 --> 01:02:59.450
well as the researchers themselves were immediately
obliterated by an unknown force, though it’s

01:02:59.450 --> 01:03:04.690
a pretty safe guess that a certain flaming
weapon was responsible.

01:03:04.690 --> 01:03:11.230
This candidate for SCP-001 may be one of,
if not the most powerful being that the SCP

01:03:11.230 --> 01:03:17.330
Foundation has ever encountered, and according
to its entry in the SCP-001 file, the Guardian

01:03:17.330 --> 01:03:21.790
is even responsible for the creation of the
Foundation itself.

01:03:21.790 --> 01:03:27.640
If the file is to be believed, the Administrator
of the SCP Foundation one day heard a word

01:03:27.640 --> 01:03:30.230
echoing through his head.

01:03:30.230 --> 01:03:31.640
“Prepare.”

01:03:31.640 --> 01:03:37.400
This one word instruction led him to starting
the SCP Foundation, containing countless dangerous

01:03:37.400 --> 01:03:41.970
anomalies and entities in preparation for
an uncertain future.

01:03:41.970 --> 01:03:47.150
In all that time, since the very beginning
of the Foundation, The Gate Guardian has remained

01:03:47.150 --> 01:03:48.760
standing at its post.

01:03:48.760 --> 01:03:54.530
While it is not aggressive nor openly hostile
towards humanity, The Gate Guardian doesn’t

01:03:54.530 --> 01:03:57.700
seem to care much for us either, at least
as individuals.

01:03:57.700 --> 01:04:03.069
It rarely interacts with human beings when
left unprovoked, and venturing too close to

01:04:03.069 --> 01:04:06.770
the Guardian however, is not an automatic
death sentence.

01:04:06.770 --> 01:04:12.150
The Guardian first communicates with any living
being approaching it via a telepathic message,

01:04:12.150 --> 01:04:14.849
instructing them to either “Leave” or
“Forget”.

01:04:14.849 --> 01:04:20.420
If whomever has stepped too close to SCP-001
complies with the instructions, they’ll

01:04:20.420 --> 01:04:25.960
be able to freely leave the area, while simultaneously
forgetting every detail of The Gate Guardian’s

01:04:25.960 --> 01:04:26.960
existence.

01:04:26.960 --> 01:04:32.750
Ignore these warnings though, and SCP-001
has no qualms about completely eliminating

01:04:32.750 --> 01:04:34.480
you from reality.

01:04:34.480 --> 01:04:38.750
Given its enormous destructive potential,
it is no wonder that the Foundation has tried

01:04:38.750 --> 01:04:44.900
to use The Gate Guardian to eliminate other
dangerous SCPs, each with varying results.

01:04:44.900 --> 01:04:49.090
The Foundation at one time even attempted
to use The Gate Guardian to destroy the infamously

01:04:49.090 --> 01:04:54.930
indestructible SCP-682, better known by the
rather appropriate name of The Hard-to-Destroy

01:04:54.930 --> 01:04:56.290
Reptile.

01:04:56.290 --> 01:05:02.589
Due to the malicious contempt SCP-682 holds
for human beings and all other forms of life,

01:05:02.589 --> 01:05:08.609
it is perhaps one of the most dangerous anomalies
the SCP Foundation has in containment.

01:05:08.609 --> 01:05:14.000
SCP-682 is also one of the few creatures the
Foundation actively wants to terminate, a

01:05:14.000 --> 01:05:19.220
task made that much harder given that 682
can regenerate its entire form from as little

01:05:19.220 --> 01:05:21.140
as a single cell.

01:05:21.140 --> 01:05:25.460
The Gate Guardian had already shown time and
time again that it was capable of massive

01:05:25.460 --> 01:05:29.380
destruction, and researchers working for the
Foundation hoped to harness that power to

01:05:29.380 --> 01:05:33.250
rid the world of SCP-682 for good.

01:05:33.250 --> 01:05:37.941
682 was placed on an unmanned vehicle and
carried to within one kilometer of the Gate

01:05:37.941 --> 01:05:38.941
Guardian.

01:05:38.941 --> 01:05:43.160
The guardian attacked the vehicle, seriously
wounding but not killing 682.

01:05:43.160 --> 01:05:49.420
It seems even the mighty SCP-001 couldn’t
kill the Hard-to-Destroy Reptile.

01:05:49.420 --> 01:05:54.640
While the researchers were disappointed with
this result, it is worth noting that 682 made

01:05:54.640 --> 01:05:57.349
a very interesting comment to the Guardian.

01:05:57.349 --> 01:06:00.359
682 mentioned that the Gate Guardian is “not
Uriel” but a “pretender”.

01:06:00.359 --> 01:06:06.690
Uriel is the archangel that some religious
texts describe as the guardian standing at

01:06:06.690 --> 01:06:12.059
the Gate of Eden with a fiery sword, so does
this mean that 682 knows that the Gate Guardian

01:06:12.059 --> 01:06:13.869
is not actually an angel?

01:06:13.869 --> 01:06:18.270
Or that the location it is guarding isn’t
the Garden of Eden at all?

01:06:18.270 --> 01:06:23.859
Any truth or meaning behind these comments
has, as of yet, been undetermined by the SCP

01:06:23.859 --> 01:06:24.859
Foundation.

01:06:24.859 --> 01:06:32.829
A later experiment involved both SCP-001 and
SCP-073, the anomaly otherwise known as Cain.

01:06:32.829 --> 01:06:38.140
Cain is a male humanoid of possible Arabic
descent whose arms, legs, spine, and shoulders

01:06:38.140 --> 01:06:42.890
are replaced in an almost cyborg-like fashion
with beryllium bronze.

01:06:42.890 --> 01:06:49.090
Much like The Gate Guardian, SCP-073 may also
be the same as the one mentioned in the Bible’s

01:06:49.090 --> 01:06:54.160
Book of Genesis who, according to the biblical
story, murdered his own brother Abel out of

01:06:54.160 --> 01:06:55.160
spite.

01:06:55.160 --> 01:06:59.790
As punishment for his actions, Cain was cursed
to eternally suffer for his wrongdoing.

01:06:59.790 --> 01:07:05.859
In the case of SCP-073, any damage inflicted
on him is deflected back to the attacker,

01:07:05.859 --> 01:07:08.839
but Cain is made to feel the pain of the attack.

01:07:08.839 --> 01:07:13.339
Any plants or plant-based matter withers and
rots in his presence, and he is cursed with

01:07:13.339 --> 01:07:18.270
a perfect memory, keeping him forever haunted
by his murder of Abel.

01:07:18.270 --> 01:07:22.300
When Cain was brought before The Gate Guardian,
an unknown incident occurred.

01:07:22.300 --> 01:07:27.119
The Foundation’s records are heavily expunged,
but we do know that somehow, Cain’s usual

01:07:27.119 --> 01:07:32.450
ability to deflect incoming damage back at
his attacker had no effect on SCP-001.

01:07:32.450 --> 01:07:40.480
The encounter left SCP-073 unconscious, and
even permanently blinded nearby research personnel.

01:07:40.480 --> 01:07:45.410
It was as a direct result of this incident
that the O5 Council demanded that no further

01:07:45.410 --> 01:07:52.270
experiments of any kind were to be conducted
on SCP-001, with the Administrator even filing

01:07:52.270 --> 01:07:58.960
an executive order that no SCPs be exposed
to the Guardian, and that SCP-001 was to never

01:07:58.960 --> 01:08:03.640
again be used for the attempted termination
of other SCPs.

01:08:03.640 --> 01:08:08.079
Of course, perhaps it wasn’t just the mistakes
of the past that made the Council decide that

01:08:08.079 --> 01:08:10.920
SCP-001 was best left alone.

01:08:10.920 --> 01:08:16.719
At some point, an erratic transmission was
received from Site 0 by Foundation personnel,

01:08:16.719 --> 01:08:19.799
detailing an XK-class end of the world scenario.

01:08:19.799 --> 01:08:24.500
In the transmission, the sender, believed
to be another member of the SCP Foundation,

01:08:24.500 --> 01:08:29.719
described an event during which The Gate Guardian
finally left its post, stepping away from

01:08:29.719 --> 01:08:32.790
the entrance to the Garden of Eden.

01:08:32.790 --> 01:08:36.319
“SCP-001 has left its location,” the sender
wrote.

01:08:36.319 --> 01:08:37.509
“The Gate is Open.

01:08:37.509 --> 01:08:38.949
They are riding forth.

01:08:38.949 --> 01:08:40.759
Oh God, it's so beautiful…”

01:08:40.759 --> 01:08:45.210
The transmission then goes on to repeat various
phrases including “The Lord shall reign

01:08:45.210 --> 01:08:50.130
forever” and “Hear, O Israel, The Lord,
our God, The Lord is one”.

01:08:50.130 --> 01:08:55.380
What can be inferred from the rambling transmission
is that the event being described is the end

01:08:55.380 --> 01:08:56.900
of the world.

01:08:56.900 --> 01:09:01.420
Some believe that, once God deems it time,
his angelic armies will lay waste to the Earth

01:09:01.420 --> 01:09:03.600
in order to remake it as a paradise.

01:09:03.600 --> 01:09:10.440
When this occurs, SCP-001, The Gate Guardian,
will open the gate he stands in front of,

01:09:10.440 --> 01:09:16.239
allowing the other beings like it to emerge
into our world, ready to cleanse it.

01:09:16.239 --> 01:09:19.190
Perhaps most interesting is the source of
the message.

01:09:19.190 --> 01:09:23.839
The transmission was received from within
the SCP Foundation, from Site 0, however when

01:09:23.839 --> 01:09:30.190
questioned by personnel, O5-14 told them that
no such message had been sent, or even existed.

01:09:30.190 --> 01:09:34.990
While some initially disregarded the transmission
telling of the end of the world as a hoax,

01:09:34.990 --> 01:09:37.710
it was then that a timestamp was discovered.

01:09:37.710 --> 01:09:43.890
This warning had not been sent from Site 0,
at least not yet, and was dated several years

01:09:43.890 --> 01:09:45.310
in the future.

01:09:45.310 --> 01:09:50.520
Despite this ominous warning of things to
come, The Gate Guardian remains inactive,

01:09:50.520 --> 01:09:53.460
standing at the threshold to Eden, waiting.

01:09:53.460 --> 01:09:58.230
What is the most dangerous creature in the
universe? Here on planet Earth there are creatures

01:09:58.230 --> 01:10:04.120
that have hardly evolved since prehistoric
eras like sharks, crocodiles, and snakes…

01:10:04.120 --> 01:10:09.340
perfect biological killing machines. But then
again, the animal kingdom is nothing when

01:10:09.340 --> 01:10:13.860
compared to the menagerie of creatures contained
by the SCP Foundation.

01:10:13.860 --> 01:10:21.890
So, once again, what is the most dangerous
creature in the universe? Is it SCP-682? The

01:10:21.890 --> 01:10:26.620
damage regenerating reptile with a hatred
for all other forms of life? Or is it The

01:10:26.620 --> 01:10:32.590
Scarlet King? Or is the Broken God more deserving
of that title? Maybe the answer still lies

01:10:32.590 --> 01:10:37.390
elsewhere, and thankfully, there is one SCP
in the Foundation’s archives that might

01:10:37.390 --> 01:10:42.620
not be the most dangerous itself, but teaches
us a very important lesson about what the

01:10:42.620 --> 01:10:50.890
most dangerous entity truly is.
This is the story of SCP-001, The Spiral Path.

01:10:50.890 --> 01:10:57.130
An important distinction, before we go any
further: SCP-001 doesn’t refer to a single

01:10:57.130 --> 01:11:02.020
creature, object, or entity, but rather a
collection of various anomalies contained

01:11:02.020 --> 01:11:07.429
by the SCP Foundation. It is unclear why there
are multiple files collected under the shared

01:11:07.429 --> 01:11:13.449
designation of SCP-001. Some believe these
anomalies are some of the earliest ever contained

01:11:13.449 --> 01:11:18.320
by the Foundation, encountered before they
introduced their current numbering system.

01:11:18.320 --> 01:11:24.690
There is also the theory that this is intentional
misdirection, that the multiple SCP-001 files

01:11:24.690 --> 01:11:31.360
are an attempt by the Foundation to conceal
secret information about the true SCP-001.

01:11:31.360 --> 01:11:36.400
Anomalies sharing the name SCP-001 include
the infamous, aforementioned Scarlet King,

01:11:36.400 --> 01:11:41.590
a powerful eldritch being intent on ending
all creation. Another anomalous being with

01:11:41.590 --> 01:11:46.360
similar levels of destructive power is the
Gate Guardian, believed to be an angel standing

01:11:46.360 --> 01:11:53.110
at the entrance to the Garden of Eden, it
too goes by the name SCP-001. But, for the

01:11:53.110 --> 01:11:59.360
purposes of this video, we will be using SCP-001
to refer to something otherwise codenamed

01:11:59.360 --> 01:12:06.500
The Spiral Path. And while it is not a creature
in and of itself, SCP-001 does yield one answer

01:12:06.500 --> 01:12:12.960
to that important question: What is the most
dangerous creature in the universe?

01:12:12.960 --> 01:12:18.380
On paper, SCP-001 does not seem to be much,
and it certainly doesn’t appear to be any

01:12:18.380 --> 01:12:24.380
sort of threat. As its nickname suggests,
The Spiral Path is exactly that. Located deep

01:12:24.380 --> 01:12:32.440
in a wooded area known only as Site 0, SCP-001
is a gravel path in the shape of a spiral.

01:12:32.440 --> 01:12:36.699
Your first thought at hearing that might be,
“what could be so important about a path?”

01:12:36.699 --> 01:12:41.690
If someone were to find themselves walking
along The Spiral Path, traveling clockwise

01:12:41.690 --> 01:12:47.790
around the gravel, then they will find that…
nothing happens. It’s just a normal path

01:12:47.790 --> 01:12:53.670
with slight inclines and declines as one traverses
it. If one should walk counterclockwise around

01:12:53.670 --> 01:13:00.610
it though, then they will begin to experience
SCP-001’s first anomalous effect. The path

01:13:00.610 --> 01:13:05.550
will begin to feel as if it is sloping uphill,
getting steeper and steeper. When they reach

01:13:05.550 --> 01:13:10.179
the beginning of the path again, a person
will still as if they are walking endlessly

01:13:10.179 --> 01:13:16.140
uphill. All this while, the path itself does
not move or change in form or altitude. To

01:13:16.140 --> 01:13:22.620
put it simply, walking one way around SCP-001
causes it to behave normally. Walking the

01:13:22.620 --> 01:13:26.640
other, the path does not adhere to the laws
of physics.

01:13:26.640 --> 01:13:31.310
You may well be thinking, “is that all?”
On a surface level, The Spiral Path does appear

01:13:31.310 --> 01:13:36.900
to be just an unmoving, low-threat anomaly.
While it may not be as aggressive or malicious

01:13:36.900 --> 01:13:42.230
as some of the SCP Foundation’s rogues gallery,
it is still a spatial anomaly that defies

01:13:42.230 --> 01:13:47.300
all Euclidean geometry. That might sound like
small potatoes when compared to everything

01:13:47.300 --> 01:13:52.920
the SCP Foundation has faced over the years.
But bear in mind, if The Spiral Path is truly

01:13:52.920 --> 01:13:58.940
SCP-001, and the very first anomaly that the
Foundation learned of, then a simple path

01:13:58.940 --> 01:14:03.120
that ignores the ordinary laws of space and
time would have been a major discovery in

01:14:03.120 --> 01:14:07.730
the organization’s earliest days.
But why would they still keep The Spiral Path

01:14:07.730 --> 01:14:13.980
so heavily guarded all these years later?
SCP-001 is kept behind a maximum security

01:14:13.980 --> 01:14:19.219
fence that has been constructed all the way
around the perimeter of Site 0. At all times,

01:14:19.219 --> 01:14:24.080
the SCP Foundation keeps no less than five
fully armed members of security personnel

01:14:24.080 --> 01:14:29.450
on site to keep watch over The Spiral Path
and make sure that no one approaches it who

01:14:29.450 --> 01:14:34.910
isn’t authorized to. There is a small metal
plaque too, bearing an unknown inscription

01:14:34.910 --> 01:14:40.480
on it. Special Containment Procedures for
SCP-001 state that this plaque is to be kept

01:14:40.480 --> 01:14:46.020
in good condition, and it should be immediately
reported if it shows any signs of damage.

01:14:46.020 --> 01:14:51.520
A Foundation physics laboratory is also located
nearby, where research staff tirelessly conduct

01:14:51.520 --> 01:14:57.480
scientific tests on SCP-001 and its anomalous
properties. So, there’s definitely something

01:14:57.480 --> 01:15:01.770
more to The Spiral Path than a simple stroll
around it would tell you.

01:15:01.770 --> 01:15:09.210
Attached to SCP-001’s file is an item referred
to as Document 001-O5. Written by high ranking

01:15:09.210 --> 01:15:14.631
Foundation researcher Doctor Everett Mann,
any prospective or new members of the O5 Council

01:15:14.631 --> 01:15:20.710
are required to read this document and, from
the events it details, learn the truth.

01:15:20.710 --> 01:15:27.250
Not just the truth about The Spiral Path,
but the truth about the SCP Foundation itself.

01:15:27.250 --> 01:15:31.060
Doctor Mann begins this file by explaining
to the reader that either he or one of the

01:15:31.060 --> 01:15:35.860
original founders of the SCP Foundation must
have died, and the person reading has been

01:15:35.860 --> 01:15:41.679
appointed as a successor. Whether his death
was caused by an SCP, an operative from another

01:15:41.679 --> 01:15:46.380
anomalous organization like the Global Occult
Coalition, or “getting a little close to

01:15:46.380 --> 01:15:51.410
the flame”, Mann states that old age definitely
wouldn’t be what killed him. He writes,

01:15:51.410 --> 01:15:55.550
“We took care of that, didn’t we?”
Whether he means that he and the rest of the

01:15:55.550 --> 01:15:59.890
“old guard” are somehow immortal, or just
working for the Foundation would likely mean

01:15:59.890 --> 01:16:05.540
dying before reaching old age, is unclear.
But, Doctor Mann’s next statement is one

01:16:05.540 --> 01:16:11.450
that changes the very way we view the Foundation
and its entire purpose. “We have never ‘discovered’

01:16:11.450 --> 01:16:18.560
an SCP in the entire history of the Foundation.”
According to Document 001-O5, every instance

01:16:18.560 --> 01:16:23.860
of an anomalous creature, entity or object,
is entirely staged.

01:16:23.860 --> 01:16:28.469
He then goes on to describe Aaron Siegel,
a gifted physicist that Doctor Mann regarded

01:16:28.469 --> 01:16:31.340
very highly.
“I believe that his name would be there

01:16:31.340 --> 01:16:37.950
with Edison, Einstein, and Hawking. I knew
him very well. He was, and may still be, my

01:16:37.950 --> 01:16:41.219
brother.”
The pair evidently shared a close personal

01:16:41.219 --> 01:16:47.420
connection, and it was Siegel who first discovered
SCP-001. During a hike, Aaron stumbled upon

01:16:47.420 --> 01:16:52.850
The Spiral Path, noticing that no matter how
far uphill he seemed to travel, his elevation

01:16:52.850 --> 01:16:59.160
never once changed, only for him to end up
back at the start of the path. Being a physicist,

01:16:59.160 --> 01:17:04.330
Siegel quickly realized how this unassuming
gravel path did not conform to Euclidean geometry,

01:17:04.330 --> 01:17:09.640
that it did not fit within the laws of nature.
Constructing a small wooden shack nearby,

01:17:09.640 --> 01:17:14.679
Aaron Siegel began to study the properties
of The Spiral Path. Equation after equation,

01:17:14.679 --> 01:17:21.330
hours spent examining every variable and experimenting
with his findings. Until something unforeseen

01:17:21.330 --> 01:17:28.970
happened: Aaron created an SCP, a key that
had the innate ability to open any lock. Nowadays,

01:17:28.970 --> 01:17:34.230
that same key is still in the Foundation’s
possession, under the designation SCP-005.

01:17:34.230 --> 01:17:40.340
Slowly, Aaron began to bring others into the
fold, trusted colleagues and other scientific

01:17:40.340 --> 01:17:45.970
minds. Among them was, of course, Doctor Everett
Mann, who was still a medical student at Harvard

01:17:45.970 --> 01:17:51.420
at the time. This brain trust, a think tank
composed of only a select few, they were the

01:17:51.420 --> 01:17:56.420
very beginning. The ones who founded the SCP
Foundation.

01:17:56.420 --> 01:18:01.179
Using their own fortunes and funding from
Thomas Carter, the group continued with Siegel’s

01:18:01.179 --> 01:18:05.600
experiments. The scientists had high hopes
for what they could achieve, planning to change

01:18:05.600 --> 01:18:10.210
the world for the better. Feeding the hungry,
providing shelter to the homeless, curing

01:18:10.210 --> 01:18:15.900
the sick, and even cheating death itself.
In the beginning, this proto-Foundation started

01:18:15.900 --> 01:18:20.980
small. Their goals were noble, but could not
realistically be achieved overnight. They

01:18:20.980 --> 01:18:25.469
tried to make items that would improve life,
such as a fountain of youth, a partially sentient

01:18:25.469 --> 01:18:31.090
Civil War statue, and an extremely bouncy
ball. Better known to the Foundation today

01:18:31.090 --> 01:18:40.500
as SCP-006, SCP-011 and SCP-018 respectively.
But then this new Foundation began to grow,

01:18:40.500 --> 01:18:46.489
with more organization and a secret facility.
And with that expansion, came emboldened scientists,

01:18:46.489 --> 01:18:51.260
eager to change the world.
The group began working on human test subjects,

01:18:51.260 --> 01:18:57.560
volunteers and drifters that soon became SCPs.
The Spiral Path was not just a break in the

01:18:57.560 --> 01:19:02.480
fabric of reality. In a metaphorical sense,
it referred to the spiraling path the newly

01:19:02.480 --> 01:19:09.030
formed Foundation itself was on. Every discovery
they made led to another, and that to another

01:19:09.030 --> 01:19:14.710
still. Until things started to go wrong. During
the continuing experiments, Dr Mann created

01:19:14.710 --> 01:19:20.840
SCP-008, a deadly zombie plague capable of
infecting anyone with one hundred percent

01:19:20.840 --> 01:19:26.600
lethality. More and more of the founders were
so invested in their projects, that the results

01:19:26.600 --> 01:19:31.130
were often nightmarish.
The Foundation needed help, that came when

01:19:31.130 --> 01:19:36.860
Thomas Carter showed their work to the military
in exchange for additional funding and personnel.

01:19:36.860 --> 01:19:42.150
The SCP Foundation expanded even further,
becoming an international organization and

01:19:42.150 --> 01:19:47.440
bringing in new researchers and staff. In
some instances, the founders would arrange

01:19:47.440 --> 01:19:52.350
for the anomalies they had created to be “found”
by the new recruits, other times they would

01:19:52.350 --> 01:19:57.910
fabricate reports, changing the details of
how things like SCP-008 or the fountain of

01:19:57.910 --> 01:20:03.610
youth were first discovered. Anything the
founders said was simply now a fact, no one

01:20:03.610 --> 01:20:07.530
questioned them.
Even then, problems still arose. Founding

01:20:07.530 --> 01:20:12.150
members broke away from the SCP Foundation,
some even creating splinter groups that would

01:20:12.150 --> 01:20:17.290
later become infamous Groups of Interest.
The Foundation’s directive shifted, now

01:20:17.290 --> 01:20:22.310
focusing on the containment of anomalies,
as yet more were created through darker means.

01:20:22.310 --> 01:20:28.540
SCP-231 was taken from an orphanage, Doctor
Mann himself vivisected a small boy who then

01:20:28.540 --> 01:20:35.640
became SCP-610, the Flesh That Hates. And
there were more still; Abel, the blood pond,

01:20:35.640 --> 01:20:41.031
and even the Hard To Destroy Reptile. All
of them were the creation of the Foundation

01:20:41.031 --> 01:20:44.500
itself.
But through it all, Doctor Mann wrote, he

01:20:44.500 --> 01:20:49.370
was never afraid of the path that the Foundation
was on. He was never even afraid of all the

01:20:49.370 --> 01:20:54.250
monsters and abominations that he and the
other founders had secretly created by studying

01:20:54.250 --> 01:21:01.550
SCP-001. What truly scared him were the anomalies
the Foundation didn’t create. There were

01:21:01.550 --> 01:21:06.830
some that would just appear in containment
one day, even if they hadn’t been there

01:21:06.830 --> 01:21:12.670
before. They would seem like they had always
been there. Doctor Mann closes Document 001-O5

01:21:12.670 --> 01:21:18.690
with the realization that he and the other
founders simply were not in control anymore.

01:21:18.690 --> 01:21:24.010
The tale of Doctor Mann and the other founders
of the SCP Foundation is one of noble intentions

01:21:24.010 --> 01:21:29.340
that ultimately became corrupted. At first,
the founders created SCPs that they hoped

01:21:29.340 --> 01:21:36.050
would benefit humanity. But then came the
mistakes, the accidents, the monsters, like

01:21:36.050 --> 01:21:45.590
SCP-008, SCP-610, and even SCP-682. The Foundation
lied to the governments and militaries of

01:21:45.590 --> 01:21:51.900
the world, claiming they’d found these SCPs
- not created them - and in return, they received

01:21:51.900 --> 01:21:57.900
funding and staff to expand, allowing the
SCP Foundation to grow to become what it is

01:21:57.900 --> 01:22:02.060
today.
Dr Mann posits that at this point, the Foundation

01:22:02.060 --> 01:22:06.300
was no longer in control, but perhaps they
never were.

01:22:06.300 --> 01:22:12.270
And all of this stems back from one, singular
starting point: The Spiral Path. It might

01:22:12.270 --> 01:22:17.699
be impossible to truly know how many anomalies
and SCPs the Foundation created, just from

01:22:17.699 --> 01:22:25.080
researching SCP-001. Only the O5 Council will
ever know exactly how many of the founders’

01:22:25.080 --> 01:22:27.650
discoveries they themselves were responsible
for.

01:22:27.650 --> 01:22:33.030
And now you know the answer to what’s the
most dangerous creature in the universe. It’s

01:22:33.030 --> 01:22:38.381
regular people, dabbling with something they
could never hope to fully understand. Starting

01:22:38.381 --> 01:22:44.170
with the hope to change the world, only to
create monsters that might one day destroy

01:22:44.170 --> 01:22:45.540
it.

01:22:45.540 --> 01:22:50.020
Supernatural monsters are on the loose! Practitioners
of the Arcane Arts are here to bring about

01:22:50.020 --> 01:22:55.270
the end of the world! Sinister paramilitary
forces are using paranormal objects to gain

01:22:55.270 --> 01:23:01.420
an edge over their enemies! In short, things
are messed up, and when the anomalous is out

01:23:01.420 --> 01:23:07.380
of line, we all know that there’s only one
group you’d ever think to call: The FBI’s

01:23:07.380 --> 01:23:08.660
Unusual Incidents Unit.

01:23:08.660 --> 01:23:10.830
What, were you expecting someone else?

01:23:10.830 --> 01:23:11.830
Everybody knows that the Unusual Incidents
Unit is the goto when it comes to paranormal

01:23:11.830 --> 01:23:15.800
deterrence. Sure, they don’t have the resources
of the SCP Foundation. They don’t have the

01:23:15.800 --> 01:23:20.291
strategy of the Global Occult Coalition. They
don’t have the ruthlessness of the Chaos

01:23:20.291 --> 01:23:25.340
Insurgency, or the arcane knowledge advantages
of the Serpent’s Hand. But they’ve gotta

01:23:25.340 --> 01:23:28.620
have something, right? Right!?

01:23:28.620 --> 01:23:33.930
Okay, maybe you’re not convinced, but you
will be! You may not respect them yet, but

01:23:33.930 --> 01:23:37.730
you’ll change your tune when you find out
that the Unusual Incidents Unit has dealt

01:23:37.730 --> 01:23:44.540
with one of the most important anomalies out
there: SCP-001. Or as the true experts over

01:23:44.540 --> 01:23:51.960
at the UIU call it, CA3, short for “Confirmed
Anomaly 3.” If the evidence and files put

01:23:51.960 --> 01:23:56.760
together by the UIU are to be believed - and
who are we kidding? Of course they are! - then

01:23:56.760 --> 01:24:03.310
they may have the answer to one of the anomalous
world’s biggest questions: How was the SCP

01:24:03.310 --> 01:24:05.100
Foundation actually formed?

01:24:05.100 --> 01:24:09.860
But before we jump into the mysteries of CA3,
let’s talk a little bit more about the real

01:24:09.860 --> 01:24:16.390
heroes of today’s story, the UIU. This secretive
offshoot of the FBI - America’s premier

01:24:16.390 --> 01:24:21.159
domestic intelligence agency - was personally
commissioned by J. Edgar Hoover during the

01:24:21.159 --> 01:24:27.050
Cold War. Why? For the same reason that literally
everything happened in the US during the Cold

01:24:27.050 --> 01:24:32.469
War: To get an edge over the Soviets! Hoover
was an extraordinarily powerful man in US

01:24:32.469 --> 01:24:37.700
politics, his tenure as FBI Director spanning
the terms of eight different presidents. If

01:24:37.700 --> 01:24:42.679
he wanted to start a unit of agents whose
sole job was investigating the supernatural,

01:24:42.679 --> 01:24:45.210
nobody would dare stand in his way.

01:24:45.210 --> 01:24:50.260
Everyone always talks about the nuclear arms
race going on back in the 1960s, but far fewer

01:24:50.260 --> 01:24:56.040
people talk about the supernatural arms race
that was happening at the exact same time.

01:24:56.040 --> 01:25:01.180
World War II coincided neatly with the Seventh
Occult War - an important geopolitical event

01:25:01.180 --> 01:25:06.250
that played a huge role in shaping the Global
Occult Coalition - and a number of high-ranking

01:25:06.250 --> 01:25:11.260
members of the Nazi party were believed to
be key figures in this secret, magical war.

01:25:11.260 --> 01:25:14.840
When the Soviets sacked a number of German
cities as part of their offensive campaigns

01:25:14.840 --> 01:25:19.719
in World War II, they were able to bring back
scores of anomalous items that the Nazis had

01:25:19.719 --> 01:25:24.710
been using to consolidate dark power. This
didn’t bode well for the United States Government

01:25:24.710 --> 01:25:30.690
during the Cold War. After all, the only thing
scarier to them than Communists were Magical

01:25:30.690 --> 01:25:35.540
Communists! The US needed to build up its
own anomalous arsenal, and that’s where

01:25:35.540 --> 01:25:37.540
the UIU came in.

01:25:37.540 --> 01:25:42.730
The FBI allocated some of its okayest personnel
to the task. Most were either agents who had

01:25:42.730 --> 01:25:46.940
experienced a paranormal encounter out in
the field, or who were being punished for

01:25:46.940 --> 01:25:51.481
some kind of heinous mistake they’d made
carrying out their duties elsewhere. Despite

01:25:51.481 --> 01:25:56.480
not being the best of the best, these agents
sure were eager to get their hands on some

01:25:56.480 --> 01:25:57.480
cans.

01:25:57.480 --> 01:26:02.110
That isn’t an innuendo, by the way. The
Foundation refers to anomalies it deals with

01:26:02.110 --> 01:26:09.650
as SCPs, or “Skips”, the GOC calls them
Parathreats, and the UIU calls them Cans,

01:26:09.650 --> 01:26:15.300
again short for “Confirmed Anomalies.”
Well, when it’s an anomalous event or location,

01:26:15.300 --> 01:26:19.920
anyway. Anomalous objects, like cursed books
or supernaturally powerful weapons, are referred

01:26:19.920 --> 01:26:25.440
to as “Carts”, or “Confirmed Artifacts.”
And finally, anomalous people or sentient

01:26:25.440 --> 01:26:29.630
entities are referred to by the unfortunate
name of “Can Man.”

01:26:29.630 --> 01:26:34.520
It may not sound as cool, but hey, it gets
the job done just fine in the end.

01:26:34.520 --> 01:26:39.540
While the Unusual Incidents Unit may lack
the knowledge, strength, resources, and even

01:26:39.540 --> 01:26:43.670
cred of its fellow groups of interest, that
doesn’t mean that it doesn’t keep track

01:26:43.670 --> 01:26:48.500
of the others. In fact, the UIU has a pretty
unique relationship with each of them.

01:26:48.500 --> 01:26:54.540
The GOC, for example, is nicknamed “The
Suits” by the UIU. The official UIU orientation

01:26:54.540 --> 01:26:58.179
states that the Suits outrank them, and if
they’re asked to follow an order by a member

01:26:58.179 --> 01:27:03.170
of the Suits, they should just go ahead and
do it. Same goes for members of The Fireworks

01:27:03.170 --> 01:27:08.960
- which is the UIU lingo for the Chaos Insurgency.
Unlike the Foundation, which generally has

01:27:08.960 --> 01:27:14.440
the resources to go toe to toe with the Chaos
Insurgency, the UIU are rightfully terrified

01:27:14.440 --> 01:27:19.540
of them. Official orders from the top are
for UIU agents to do whatever they say, or

01:27:19.540 --> 01:27:24.250
they might find themselves getting shot in
the head by a Chaos Insurgent, or worse.

01:27:24.250 --> 01:27:29.870
Next, the Cart Shoppers, also known as Marshall,
Carter, and Dark, a sinister gentleman’s

01:27:29.870 --> 01:27:35.440
club and auctioneer of anomalous items. Official
protocol is to raid any deals being conducted

01:27:35.440 --> 01:27:40.770
by Marshall, Carter, and Dark, but oftentimes
these raids are unsuccessful, because M C

01:27:40.770 --> 01:27:45.650
and D’s security force are more competent
fighters than anyone on the Unusual Incidents

01:27:45.650 --> 01:27:46.909
Unit Payroll.

01:27:46.909 --> 01:27:51.159
On the other end of the spectrum are The Can
Collection, the official UIU nickname for

01:27:51.159 --> 01:27:56.210
the Serpent’s Hand. UIU Leadership recommends
against their agents staging any one-on-one

01:27:56.210 --> 01:28:00.980
confrontations with them. Official memos also
contain the phrase “If they give you an

01:28:00.980 --> 01:28:05.600
order, consider following it, they can probably
set you on fire with their mind.”

01:28:05.600 --> 01:28:11.420
And finally, the most important relationship
of all is the one they have with the SCP Foundation.

01:28:11.420 --> 01:28:15.800
Much like the rest of the groups of interest
on their roster, the UIU is subordinate to

01:28:15.800 --> 01:28:20.989
the SCP Foundation, their agents happily taking
orders from them at the drop of a hat. They

01:28:20.989 --> 01:28:26.489
call the Foundation the Skippers, but don’t
let the casual name fool you. The SCP Foundation

01:28:26.489 --> 01:28:31.449
is so far above them on the pecking order
that they rarely even communicate in any official

01:28:31.449 --> 01:28:32.520
capacity.

01:28:32.520 --> 01:28:36.831
When the Foundation talks to the UIU, it’s
always through code. They wouldn’t dream

01:28:36.831 --> 01:28:41.860
of letting a hapless UIU agent help them on
any major operation, but lazier agents of

01:28:41.860 --> 01:28:47.130
the Foundation might occasionally outsource
work to UIU agents. If ever one of these plucky

01:28:47.130 --> 01:28:51.730
feds receives a message starting with, “Hey
Skipper”, they can be sure they’re about

01:28:51.730 --> 01:28:54.989
to have a low-priority anomalous case pawned
off on them.

01:28:54.989 --> 01:29:01.420
The UIU are so subservient to the SCP Foundation
that it has sometimes resulted in truly humiliating

01:29:01.420 --> 01:29:07.220
mix-ups. One high-ranking member of the UIU
once took orders from a pizza delivery guy,

01:29:07.220 --> 01:29:10.930
because he thought the pizzeria’s name,
the Spiced Crust Pizzeria, which could be

01:29:10.930 --> 01:29:16.440
shortened to SCP was actually a coded plant
sent by the Foundation to deliver a message,

01:29:16.440 --> 01:29:21.720
rather than a deep dish pepperoni and cheese.
Incidents like this are why nobody takes the

01:29:21.720 --> 01:29:23.270
UIU seriously.

01:29:23.270 --> 01:29:30.270
But according to them, there was a time before
all this. That time ended on September 7th,

01:29:30.270 --> 01:29:37.140
1954, when CA3 - or SCP-001, as the Foundation
would later call it - first appeared on the

01:29:37.140 --> 01:29:42.770
UIU’s radar. It seemed to be the most standard
Can you could possibly imagine: An anomalous

01:29:42.770 --> 01:29:47.360
high school building causing a disturbance
in the suburbs of small town America.

01:29:47.360 --> 01:29:51.290
The UIU received the call after a number of
students claimed the interior of their school

01:29:51.290 --> 01:29:55.920
suddenly looked completely different than
it ever had before, despite there being no

01:29:55.920 --> 01:30:00.350
records of an official remodel. And we’re
not just talking about moving furniture and

01:30:00.350 --> 01:30:02.170
a new coat of paint, either.

01:30:02.170 --> 01:30:07.989
The official CA3 file logs a number of changes.
These include, but are not limited to, all

01:30:07.989 --> 01:30:12.570
the walls in the building becoming steel-reinforced
concrete. All the windows being blacked out

01:30:12.570 --> 01:30:17.810
from the inside. All student desks, personal
effects, textbooks, and any other standard

01:30:17.810 --> 01:30:22.620
equipment left inside the school simply disappearing
in the night. The entire floor plan of the

01:30:22.620 --> 01:30:27.900
building seeming to have shifted, with rooms
altering in both dimensions and location,

01:30:27.900 --> 01:30:33.280
as well as featuring seemingly random modifications
within. None of this matched up the building’s

01:30:33.280 --> 01:30:38.350
original blueprints, which were obtained by
the UIU shortly after the Can was reported.

01:30:38.350 --> 01:30:45.560
But things got even stranger for investigating
UIU agents. The building now contained seventeen

01:30:45.560 --> 01:30:50.850
computers, each with state-of-the-art magnetic-core
RAM and advanced cybersecurity. For a suburban

01:30:50.850 --> 01:30:56.860
high school in 1954, it goes without saying
that this was extremely impressive. But weirdest

01:30:56.860 --> 01:31:02.600
of all was the fact that a large and seemingly
impenetrable steel wall had appeared in the

01:31:02.600 --> 01:31:07.440
auditorium, blocking it off and leaving whatever
was taking place on the other side a complete

01:31:07.440 --> 01:31:12.840
mystery. Naturally, the UIU did what little
they could to investigate the matter.

01:31:12.840 --> 01:31:20.290
The first investigation group they sent inside
- Team CA3-O5 - never came back out. And Team

01:31:20.290 --> 01:31:25.090
CA3-O6, the team they sent in to locate and
retrieve the first team, also disappeared

01:31:25.090 --> 01:31:29.390
within the anomaly. Classic UIU expertise
at work.

01:31:29.390 --> 01:31:33.900
Almost a month after discovery and initial
containment, a strange noise began emanating

01:31:33.900 --> 01:31:39.560
from the auditorium. Shortly after that, the
building became filled with people, all walking

01:31:39.560 --> 01:31:44.510
around and working at different operations.
Eerily, everyone there had a resemblance to

01:31:44.510 --> 01:31:51.480
members of Team CA3-O6, the rescue team sent
in to save the twelve members of CA3-05, all

01:31:51.480 --> 01:31:54.199
of whom were still unaccounted for.

01:31:54.199 --> 01:31:59.500
Three months later, the strangeness escalated.
More noises came from the auditorium, and

01:31:59.500 --> 01:32:03.610
the anomalous people inside the building had
gathered around the steel wall within. There

01:32:03.610 --> 01:32:08.850
was a hole in the wall, six feet in diameter,
and every three minutes for several hours,

01:32:08.850 --> 01:32:13.179
the people in the room would appear to simply
pull an anomalous object out of it.

01:32:13.179 --> 01:32:18.060
The items were then carried away, and placed
in one of the many rooms that used to be classrooms,

01:32:18.060 --> 01:32:19.500
before being locked up.

01:32:19.500 --> 01:32:24.031
The people within the building then seemed
to start guarding these strange items. Others

01:32:24.031 --> 01:32:28.429
started performing tests, with what seemed
like far more advanced technology and methods

01:32:28.429 --> 01:32:33.390
than what was possessed by the UIU during
the 1950s. What was going on here?

01:32:33.390 --> 01:32:38.030
A few days later, several armed guards exited
the building and began guarding the perimeter.

01:32:38.030 --> 01:32:43.350
When UIU personnel attempted to lead an assault
on these guards, they were quickly overpowered,

01:32:43.350 --> 01:32:48.160
even when advancing with vastly superior numbers.
Whether this was due to the skill of the guards

01:32:48.160 --> 01:32:53.080
or the incompetence of UIU agents is still
very much an open question.

01:32:53.080 --> 01:32:57.150
Though strangely enough, intel bleeding out
from the inside confirmed that the people

01:32:57.150 --> 01:33:01.830
within were treating their anomalous items
with UIU containment and testing protocols

01:33:01.830 --> 01:33:07.160
- which is consistent with the knowledge that
CA3-O5 would have had. It seemed almost as

01:33:07.160 --> 01:33:13.610
though O5, or copies of O5, were creating
a new splinter organization from within.

01:33:13.610 --> 01:33:19.290
And soon enough, it wasn’t just confined
to the interior of the CA3 building anymore.

01:33:19.290 --> 01:33:24.340
CA6, a Can Man that the UIU had been tracking
outside the school, was suddenly kidnapped

01:33:24.340 --> 01:33:29.340
and shoved into a black car by two assailants
who appeared identical to Agent Dixon - a

01:33:29.340 --> 01:33:35.679
man who’d been a member of Team CA3-O6.
The black car then returned to the CA3 facility,

01:33:35.679 --> 01:33:40.450
and was allowed to enter into the complex
by the armed guards. CA6 was then removed

01:33:40.450 --> 01:33:45.580
from the car by the Dixon clones, and placed
into containment in one of the classrooms.

01:33:45.580 --> 01:33:50.170
It wasn’t long after that that the anomalous
people within the CA3 facility made direct

01:33:50.170 --> 01:33:57.110
contact with the UIU outside. They sent a
message in morse code on May 1st, 1965. The

01:33:57.110 --> 01:34:02.060
people sending the message identified themselves
as the O5 Council - a name that seemed to

01:34:02.060 --> 01:34:07.750
be taken directly from the O5 recon team sent
into the facility months ago. They identified

01:34:07.750 --> 01:34:13.110
the new organization that they’d constructed
within the confines of the CA3 facility: The

01:34:13.110 --> 01:34:18.730
SCP Foundation. They’d just opened their
very first containment site.

01:34:18.730 --> 01:34:23.400
This new Foundation expressed the desire to
become allies with the Unusual Incidents Unit,

01:34:23.400 --> 01:34:28.590
but sadly for them, it was essentially the
last time they’d ever really be relevant.

01:34:28.590 --> 01:34:33.469
If this Foundation origin story is to be believed
- and as with all entries under the title

01:34:33.469 --> 01:34:39.830
SCP-001, it’s worth taking it with a healthy
dose of skepticism - then the UIU witnessed

01:34:39.830 --> 01:34:45.320
the birth of the organization that would quickly
go on to outperform and overshadow them.

01:34:45.320 --> 01:34:50.020
A big win for humanity in the quest to secure,
contain, and protect ourselves from dangerous

01:34:50.020 --> 01:34:54.100
anomalies, but another L for the UIU.

01:34:54.100 --> 01:34:59.350
If you’re familiar with the SCP Foundation,
then you already know the exact reason why

01:34:59.350 --> 01:35:02.730
there are multiple SCP-001s.

01:35:02.730 --> 01:35:08.219
You may even think you know which of them
is the real SCP-001.

01:35:08.219 --> 01:35:13.010
But for those of you who are new here, or
who just need a little reminder, the designation

01:35:13.010 --> 01:35:20.420
of “SCP-001” doesn’t refer to a single
creature, object or entity, but rather a collection

01:35:20.420 --> 01:35:25.400
of various anomalies that are apparently kept
in containment by the SCP Foundation.

01:35:25.400 --> 01:35:30.659
At present, it is unclear why there are multiple
files collected under the shared designation

01:35:30.659 --> 01:35:33.140
of SCP-001.

01:35:33.140 --> 01:35:37.020
Some believe it is because these anomalies
are some of the earliest ever contained by

01:35:37.020 --> 01:35:38.520
the Foundation.

01:35:38.520 --> 01:35:44.199
This would mean that they share the designation
of “SCP-001” as they were likely encountered

01:35:44.199 --> 01:35:48.409
before the SCP Foundation introduced their
current numbering system.

01:35:48.409 --> 01:35:53.980
However, there also exists a theory that this
is nothing more than intentional misdirection.

01:35:53.980 --> 01:36:00.730
Perhaps, the multiple SCP-001 files are an
attempt by the Foundation to conceal information

01:36:00.730 --> 01:36:04.889
about the true SCP-001.

01:36:04.889 --> 01:36:09.750
After all, it wouldn’t be the first time
this hyper secretive organization deceived

01:36:09.750 --> 01:36:10.750
us.

01:36:10.750 --> 01:36:16.190
Anomalies sharing the name SCP-001 include
the infamous Scarlet King, the massive Gate

01:36:16.190 --> 01:36:20.740
Guardian, and the world ending event known
as When Day Breaks.

01:36:20.740 --> 01:36:28.270
But today, we will be using SCP-001 to refer
not to an entity or an event, but to a location.

01:36:28.270 --> 01:36:30.620
A location codenamed…

01:36:30.620 --> 01:36:32.980
God’s Blind Spot.

01:36:32.980 --> 01:36:37.690
Located in an unassuming corner of the world
is a site that the SCP Foundation constructed

01:36:37.690 --> 01:36:44.310
and designated as Facility T. According to
their archive, it’s a largely unremarkable

01:36:44.310 --> 01:36:50.210
place, situated at a spot on the Sinai Peninsula
- which is a part of Egypt that forms a bridge

01:36:50.210 --> 01:36:53.350
between the continents of Africa and Asia.

01:36:53.350 --> 01:36:57.980
In the eighteenth century, archaeologists
excavating the area uncovered the remains

01:36:57.980 --> 01:37:03.640
of a stone structure, believed to be an inn
that dates back to the second millennium BC.

01:37:03.640 --> 01:37:10.510
However, since the construction of Facility
T, any trace of this structure has since disappeared.

01:37:10.510 --> 01:37:16.300
So, what makes this unremarkable site so important
to the SCP Foundation?

01:37:16.300 --> 01:37:20.620
Why establish a facility if there was nothing
anomalous about its nature?

01:37:20.620 --> 01:37:26.139
What distinguishes this SCP-001 site in the
eyes of the Foundation is the area’s profound

01:37:26.139 --> 01:37:28.780
lack of any ambient Akiva radiation.

01:37:28.780 --> 01:37:31.570
But what’s Akiva radiation?

01:37:31.570 --> 01:37:37.489
Well, according to the Foundation’s researchers,
it’s a form of cosmic background radiation,

01:37:37.489 --> 01:37:40.930
one that’s not overtly harmful to human
beings.

01:37:40.930 --> 01:37:45.489
If you grew up in a strict, church-going household,
then it’s highly likely you would have been

01:37:45.489 --> 01:37:51.690
exposed to a lot of this non-electromagnetic
radiation and never even realized it.

01:37:51.690 --> 01:37:57.050
You see, the thing with Akiva radiation is
that it is directly correlated with the amount

01:37:57.050 --> 01:38:00.310
of religious faith a person has.

01:38:00.310 --> 01:38:05.520
Regardless of which religion someone follows,
Akiva radiation will form around them.

01:38:05.520 --> 01:38:11.040
It tends to be harmless to humans, however
certain anomalous entities and SCPs considered

01:38:11.040 --> 01:38:15.860
to be demonic in nature can be repelled and
even fought off with high levels of Akiva

01:38:15.860 --> 01:38:17.150
radiation.

01:38:17.150 --> 01:38:22.340
The presence of other powerful anomalies,
those considered more benign and even holy,

01:38:22.340 --> 01:38:26.000
can also create an increase in this radiation.

01:38:26.000 --> 01:38:31.909
SCP-001 has earned the nickname “God’s
Blind Spot” for a number of reasons, one

01:38:31.909 --> 01:38:37.739
being that it is the only place on Earth with
a natural absence of this Akiva radiation.

01:38:37.739 --> 01:38:42.630
The Foundation has conducted experiments that
involved bringing sources known to emit Akiva

01:38:42.630 --> 01:38:49.350
radiation into the area of SCP-001, but when
they measured, no change in radiation levels

01:38:49.350 --> 01:38:55.330
was detected, meaning that the space around
Facility T does not actively block Akiva radiation

01:38:55.330 --> 01:39:01.090
from entering it, but also cannot absorb or
retain this religious radiation.

01:39:01.090 --> 01:39:07.350
It might be more accurate to say that the
location destroys any trace of residual Akiva,

01:39:07.350 --> 01:39:09.020
without damaging the source.

01:39:09.020 --> 01:39:14.440
A lack of faith-fueled radiation is far from
the only anomalous property of SCP-001 though.

01:39:14.440 --> 01:39:20.080
During a number of tests involving D-class
personnel, the Foundation witnessed that,

01:39:20.080 --> 01:39:25.389
while in this area, it also becomes impossible
for the death of any human being to occur,

01:39:25.389 --> 01:39:29.120
a discovery that obviously needed to be researched
further.

01:39:29.120 --> 01:39:33.590
The first test involved a healthy human male
who was left in a containment cell on the

01:39:33.590 --> 01:39:35.699
SCP-001 site and observed.

01:39:35.699 --> 01:39:42.600
He had no supplies, no food, no water, yet
over one hundred and twenty days, this man

01:39:42.600 --> 01:39:47.300
stayed alive, never succumbing to starvation
or dehydration.

01:39:47.300 --> 01:39:53.180
Next, a female member of D-class was exposed
to a lethal dose of cyanide gas within Facility

01:39:53.180 --> 01:39:57.290
T and suffered none of the expected effects.

01:39:57.290 --> 01:40:01.679
Foundation researchers then repeated this
cyanide gas test using thirty common brown

01:40:01.679 --> 01:40:06.340
rats, all of which were killed, proving that
it was only humans that couldn’t be killed

01:40:06.340 --> 01:40:08.580
while within SCP-001.

01:40:08.580 --> 01:40:15.159
God’s Blind Spot seems to also be able to
slow or halt the effects of terminal illnesses,

01:40:15.159 --> 01:40:21.150
as proven when a D-class with stage four cancer
was brought into SCP-001.

01:40:21.150 --> 01:40:25.560
Despite her prognosis stating she would be
dead imminently, the woman survived in the

01:40:25.560 --> 01:40:27.920
area for almost eight hundred days.

01:40:27.920 --> 01:40:34.600
Her cancer symptoms never advanced, and she
only died after finally leaving the area of

01:40:34.600 --> 01:40:36.020
SCP-001.

01:40:36.020 --> 01:40:39.159
There are limitations to this anomalous effect
though.

01:40:39.159 --> 01:40:43.679
One test involved cremating a healthy male
D-class while he was still alive.

01:40:43.679 --> 01:40:49.230
The man’s body caught fire just as you would
expect it to, and he was burned to death.

01:40:49.230 --> 01:40:53.860
According to the findings of that test, and
similar variations, Foundation researchers

01:40:53.860 --> 01:40:59.850
have learned that the life preserving qualities
of SCP-001 don’t prevent death by extreme

01:40:59.850 --> 01:41:01.540
external damage.

01:41:01.540 --> 01:41:06.630
One of the final tests to take place within
SCP-001 involved a pair of twenty four-year

01:41:06.630 --> 01:41:09.489
old identical D-class twins.

01:41:09.489 --> 01:41:15.250
One of the twins, designated Twin A, was held
at Facility T, while the other, Twin B, was

01:41:15.250 --> 01:41:18.870
imprisoned in a cell at a different Foundation
site.

01:41:18.870 --> 01:41:24.660
After observing them for over 26 years, Twin
B aged naturally to the age of fifty.

01:41:24.660 --> 01:41:29.900
His twin, however, did not appear to age at
all over the course of two and a half decades.

01:41:29.900 --> 01:41:34.740
It was only when moved to another facility
that Twin A began to show signs of aging.

01:41:34.740 --> 01:41:40.630
The aging process for Twin A was rapid too,
and eventually he caught up with his brother.

01:41:40.630 --> 01:41:45.429
Being a benign, non-threatening anomaly, the
Foundation have been more than happy to use

01:41:45.429 --> 01:41:48.080
God’s Blind Spot to their own advantage.

01:41:48.080 --> 01:41:52.110
Facility T was specifically established on
this site to house the headquarters of the

01:41:52.110 --> 01:41:56.330
O5 Council, the overseers of the entire SCP
Foundation.

01:41:56.330 --> 01:42:01.239
It’s hardly surprising that the overseer
council would want to set up shop here.

01:42:01.239 --> 01:42:06.340
After all, it’s the one spot on Planet Earth
where no human being can ever die of natural

01:42:06.340 --> 01:42:10.280
causes, and will not age for the duration
of their stay.

01:42:10.280 --> 01:42:15.090
Of course, this locked the O5 Council to one
location, but what if they could replicate

01:42:15.090 --> 01:42:18.410
the effects of SCP-001 elsewhere?

01:42:18.410 --> 01:42:22.100
Of course this is what the SCP Foundation
attempted.

01:42:22.100 --> 01:42:26.260
Following their research into God’s Blind
Spot, the Foundation’s own Doctor Marvin

01:42:26.260 --> 01:42:32.239
Scranton attempted to artificially recreate
the area’s anomalous effects somewhere else.

01:42:32.239 --> 01:42:39.580
His hope was, by generating a vacuum of Akiva
radiation, that a second instance of SCP-001

01:42:39.580 --> 01:42:41.940
would occur at a location of his choosing.

01:42:41.940 --> 01:42:47.510
Or, as his assistant Bertrand put it, they
planned to build a box and then push God out

01:42:47.510 --> 01:42:48.510
of it.

01:42:48.510 --> 01:42:52.250
As it turned out, God had other plans.

01:42:52.250 --> 01:42:55.389
Doctor Scranton quickly realized the hubris
of his scheme.

01:42:55.389 --> 01:43:01.290
The Akiva radiation in the selected area rapidly
dropped to zero, just as planned, but then

01:43:01.290 --> 01:43:03.300
something unexpected happened.

01:43:03.300 --> 01:43:06.239
Scranton detected an increase in Humes.

01:43:06.239 --> 01:43:10.040
These are essentially parts of the fabric
of reality, and are what’s often disrupted

01:43:10.040 --> 01:43:13.430
by reality bending SCPs.

01:43:13.430 --> 01:43:20.920
Something had come into our world thanks to
the O5 Council’s attempt to recreate SCP-001,

01:43:20.920 --> 01:43:25.260
something impossible for the Foundation to
measure or observe.

01:43:25.260 --> 01:43:31.540
In other words, Scranton had no idea what
he unleashed, or where it went.

01:43:31.540 --> 01:43:36.630
Following this incident, the O5 Council realized
a worrying increase in the anomalous incidents

01:43:36.630 --> 01:43:38.380
they were encountering.

01:43:38.380 --> 01:43:42.800
Whether or not this came as a direct result
of their meddling with the fabric of the universe

01:43:42.800 --> 01:43:48.250
was unclear, but it forced the Council to
reconsider the focus and direction of the

01:43:48.250 --> 01:43:50.920
entire SCP Foundation.

01:43:50.920 --> 01:43:56.310
Up until this point, they had been an organization
focused purely on research, but now they had

01:43:56.310 --> 01:44:00.449
to embrace a new approach to how they handled
anomalies.

01:44:00.449 --> 01:44:05.110
From then on, the Foundation’s objective
became to actively seek out and contain anomalous

01:44:05.110 --> 01:44:11.520
entities, creatures, objects, and locations
like SCP-001.

01:44:11.520 --> 01:44:17.090
Rather than just observing these phenomena
for study, they would Secure, Contain, and

01:44:17.090 --> 01:44:18.610
Protect.

01:44:18.610 --> 01:44:23.760
The final portion of SCP-001’s file is a
memorandum detailing an arrangement between

01:44:23.760 --> 01:44:27.570
the O5 Council and an unknown “counterparty.”

01:44:27.570 --> 01:44:32.850
In the document, someone named Sheldon Katz
sets out revised terms for the Foundation’s

01:44:32.850 --> 01:44:37.540
continued use of Facility T. Sheldon states
that he has reached an understanding with

01:44:37.540 --> 01:44:43.020
the counterparty, and that the contents of
the document are to serve as a formal agreement,

01:44:43.020 --> 01:44:48.570
a contract of sorts between the SCP Foundation
and someone else.

01:44:48.570 --> 01:44:52.989
According to this contract, the incident with
Scranton put a strain on the relationship

01:44:52.989 --> 01:44:58.790
between the Foundation and whoever the counterparty
is, and that the O5 Council are seeking to

01:44:58.790 --> 01:45:04.510
make amends in order to continue their new
goal of collecting and containing anomalies.

01:45:04.510 --> 01:45:09.949
So, who was this counterparty that the Overseer
Council was so desperate to appease and have

01:45:09.949 --> 01:45:11.340
on their side?

01:45:11.340 --> 01:45:17.139
Who could possibly be a higher power than
the most powerful secret organization on Earth?

01:45:17.139 --> 01:45:20.780
Well, an actual higher power, of course.

01:45:20.780 --> 01:45:27.430
That’s right, the O5 Council were making
a deal with God, over how they were allowed

01:45:27.430 --> 01:45:29.830
to use his Blind Spot.

01:45:29.830 --> 01:45:34.170
Or at least, a very powerful being that considers
itself to be God.

01:45:34.170 --> 01:45:38.530
The rules laid out in their agreement stated
that no person was permitted to stay at the

01:45:38.530 --> 01:45:45.280
site of SCP-001 for more than a hundred and
twenty years, including members of the O5

01:45:45.280 --> 01:45:51.210
Council, along with any other members of Foundation
staff, management, researchers, security personnel

01:45:51.210 --> 01:45:53.000
and test subjects.

01:45:53.000 --> 01:45:57.699
Additionally, the SCP Foundation’s Ethics
Committee was required to annually report

01:45:57.699 --> 01:46:01.500
any and all of the O5 Council’s decisions
to God.

01:46:01.500 --> 01:46:06.360
For his own part, God was restricted from
smiting or exacting his terrible wrath upon

01:46:06.360 --> 01:46:08.400
any member of Foundation personnel.

01:46:08.400 --> 01:46:13.320
That’s right, a perk of working for the
SCP Foundation is getting around the clock

01:46:13.320 --> 01:46:16.720
divine protection, at least from God himself.

01:46:16.720 --> 01:46:20.480
That’s still a lot better than an employee
dental plan.

01:46:20.480 --> 01:46:25.940
This came with a condition however, that anyone
committing a transgression or mortal sin was

01:46:25.940 --> 01:46:31.520
given a ninety day written notice, and an
opportunity to repent their wrongdoing.

01:46:31.520 --> 01:46:36.970
In return, God demanded that members of the
Foundation only worshipped him and no other

01:46:36.970 --> 01:46:39.389
divine entities.

01:46:39.389 --> 01:46:45.600
“I, the LORD, am a jealous God, visiting
the iniquity of the fathers upon the children

01:46:45.600 --> 01:46:52.420
unto the third and fourth generation of them
that hate me” was written in the contract.

01:46:52.420 --> 01:46:58.159
Finally, the agreement between the O5 Council
and God was that they would work together.

01:46:58.159 --> 01:47:02.550
The Foundation and the counterparty would
be equal partners when it came to the containment

01:47:02.550 --> 01:47:05.390
of SCPs and anomalies.

01:47:05.390 --> 01:47:10.530
Of all the strange and unexplained phenomena
that the SCP Foundation encounters on a regular

01:47:10.530 --> 01:47:15.300
basis, it hardly comes as much of a surprise
that they’ve got a direct line to the big

01:47:15.300 --> 01:47:17.100
guy upstairs.

01:47:17.100 --> 01:47:19.560
Or at least one who purports to be.

01:47:19.560 --> 01:47:23.920
Still, the fact that the O5 Council have a
business arrangement with an ultra powerful

01:47:23.920 --> 01:47:29.159
deity like being, and express written permission
to use his Blind Spot where no person can

01:47:29.159 --> 01:47:32.790
die or age, is hardly a comforting thought.

01:47:32.790 --> 01:47:37.790
At least the SCP Foundation only ever uses
its power for good… right?

01:47:37.790 --> 01:47:42.010
Oh boy, here we go again.

01:47:42.010 --> 01:47:43.820
SCP-001.

01:47:43.820 --> 01:47:48.790
Over 30 different bizarre anomalies claim
this number one spot in the database - and

01:47:48.790 --> 01:47:50.960
in a sense, they’re all right.

01:47:50.960 --> 01:47:52.239
Or are they?

01:47:52.239 --> 01:47:56.940
If you’re feeling confused already, that’s
fine, we don’t expect that to change.

01:47:56.940 --> 01:48:01.389
Because today, we’re dealing with one of
the most strange and intricate 001 entries

01:48:01.389 --> 01:48:03.810
out there: Keter Duty.

01:48:03.810 --> 01:48:06.190
Just pray you never get assigned to it.

01:48:06.190 --> 01:48:11.460
You see, when you work around weirdness, you
sometimes get a little weird yourself.

01:48:11.460 --> 01:48:15.870
And nobody deals with more weirdness than
employees of the SCP Foundation.

01:48:15.870 --> 01:48:21.489
They regularly rub elbows with everything
from godlike cicadas to hyper-infectious supernatural

01:48:21.489 --> 01:48:22.770
viruses.

01:48:22.770 --> 01:48:28.370
And as the famous Tom Jones song goes, “it’s
not unusual to suddenly take on anomalous

01:48:28.370 --> 01:48:32.070
traits after consistently working with anomalies
for years.”

01:48:32.070 --> 01:48:34.780
That’s how the lyrics go, right?

01:48:34.780 --> 01:48:39.870
Anyway, one of the Foundation’s most iconic
researchers, Dr. Jack Bright, is technically

01:48:39.870 --> 01:48:42.610
just an anomalous necklace himself.

01:48:42.610 --> 01:48:47.659
But outside of some famous exceptions, the
SCP Foundation is in the business of containing

01:48:47.659 --> 01:48:53.510
anomalous entities, not hiring them on and
giving them a paycheck and retirement plan.

01:48:53.510 --> 01:48:58.330
That’s why, if you suddenly start displaying
anomalous traits while on the Foundation payroll,

01:48:58.330 --> 01:49:02.710
you might receive a company memo assigning
you to the dreaded “Keter Duty.”

01:49:02.710 --> 01:49:08.010
But what is Keter Duty, and what kind of anomalous
traits can get you assigned to it?

01:49:08.010 --> 01:49:10.570
Let’s start with the second question first.

01:49:10.570 --> 01:49:15.360
The Official Keter Duty guidelines list a
surprisingly vast number of afflictions.

01:49:15.360 --> 01:49:19.919
These include chronic anomalous illnesses,
such as Lycanthropy - turning into a werewolf

01:49:19.919 --> 01:49:25.290
- something called Stevenson Syndrome, and
the incredibly unpleasant-sounding Photonic

01:49:25.290 --> 01:49:27.570
Gastric Discharge Syndrome.

01:49:27.570 --> 01:49:31.210
You could also be placed on Keter Duty because
you’re suffering from the manifestation

01:49:31.210 --> 01:49:36.239
of spectral phenomena, including being haunted
by spirits, whether they’re there to torment

01:49:36.239 --> 01:49:37.989
you or protect you.

01:49:37.989 --> 01:49:43.260
The sudden expression of anomalous traits
in your DNA, which is unsettlingly vague will

01:49:43.260 --> 01:49:49.260
also land you on Keter Duty, as will the awakening
of powerful magical or psionic abilities,

01:49:49.260 --> 01:49:53.560
especially ones which could be used in a potentially
offensive manner.

01:49:53.560 --> 01:49:58.429
The “Keter Duty” assignment - which involves
being relocated and forced to work in a different,

01:49:58.429 --> 01:50:03.880
highly secretive location that will be discussed
soon - is framed as a punishment for the people

01:50:03.880 --> 01:50:04.880
involved.

01:50:04.880 --> 01:50:09.310
That way, it discourages Foundation employees
from ever trying to develop anomalous powers

01:50:09.310 --> 01:50:10.710
on purpose.

01:50:10.710 --> 01:50:14.140
So what exactly is Keter Duty, and where does
it happen?

01:50:14.140 --> 01:50:18.159
To reinforce that “punishment” element
mentioned, the Foundation has spread lies

01:50:18.159 --> 01:50:23.300
among their own personnel about where the
job takes place, often involving being posted

01:50:23.300 --> 01:50:27.140
in some of the least desirable Foundation
areas imaginable.

01:50:27.140 --> 01:50:31.719
These include Point Nemo - the area of the
ocean farthest from any piece of land on earth

01:50:31.719 --> 01:50:38.340
- Pyongyang in North Korea, Stonehenge, Roswell,
Lunar Area-32, and a number of Foundation

01:50:38.340 --> 01:50:40.159
waste disposal sites.

01:50:40.159 --> 01:50:46.300
However, the reality of where those on Keter
Duty end up is even stranger: Site-100, which

01:50:46.300 --> 01:50:51.179
in this particular instance, is the true SCP-001.

01:50:51.179 --> 01:50:55.790
This Thaumiel-class anomaly is perhaps the
most unique of all multi-anomaly Foundation

01:50:55.790 --> 01:51:02.440
containment sites, a bizarre labyrinth of
non-euclidean geometry that defies true explanation.

01:51:02.440 --> 01:51:04.310
But we’ll do the best we can.

01:51:04.310 --> 01:51:07.770
In a sense, Site-100 is a facility with a
mind of its own.

01:51:07.770 --> 01:51:12.929
It’s a sprawling underground base with a
layout that defies spacetime, and what’s

01:51:12.929 --> 01:51:16.510
more, it undergoes so-called “Migration
Events.”

01:51:16.510 --> 01:51:22.110
Every so often, it will begin to exhibit a
sense of dimensional instability, before teleporting

01:51:22.110 --> 01:51:25.030
to a different location somewhere on earth.

01:51:25.030 --> 01:51:30.100
Currently, the primary entrance to Site-100
- known as Alpha Entrance - is located in

01:51:30.100 --> 01:51:34.530
the Southwest United States, though all signs
point to another migration event happening

01:51:34.530 --> 01:51:36.139
this very year.

01:51:36.139 --> 01:51:40.430
But knowing where the entrance is will only
get you so far.

01:51:40.430 --> 01:51:44.330
People assigned to Keter Duty are sent from
the Alpha Entrance to the Administration Sector

01:51:44.330 --> 01:51:49.320
to be given their initial breaching, at which
point, the true madness begins.

01:51:49.320 --> 01:51:51.480
Let’s take a look at a map of Site-100.

01:51:51.480 --> 01:51:53.550
Yikes.

01:51:53.550 --> 01:51:58.900
So there are ten major sectors in Site-100
that you should be aware of: Entrance Alpha,

01:51:58.900 --> 01:52:06.320
Administration, Archives, Technological Containment,
Bio-Containment, Sapient Containment, Cognitohazardous/Memetic/and

01:52:06.320 --> 01:52:13.180
Semantic - or CMS Containment, Esoteric Containment,
Conceptual Containment, and the Core Sector.

01:52:13.180 --> 01:52:16.190
As you can tell, they have almost everything
covered here.

01:52:16.190 --> 01:52:21.260
But just as insane as the anomalies that Site-100
contains and the methods they use to contain

01:52:21.260 --> 01:52:24.960
them, is how you actually get around the site.

01:52:24.960 --> 01:52:28.469
Site-100 is a spatial anomaly of truly epic
proportions.

01:52:28.469 --> 01:52:33.480
While the Foundation is aware of the existence
of its component sectors, it’s impossible

01:52:33.480 --> 01:52:36.430
to map out any meaningful connections between
them.

01:52:36.430 --> 01:52:40.889
It would be pretty much impossible to even
travel from one to another without passageways

01:52:40.889 --> 01:52:42.739
known as The Roots.

01:52:42.739 --> 01:52:46.480
However, these aren’t just mere portals
that you can hop through like the Ways in

01:52:46.480 --> 01:52:48.850
and out of the Wanderer’s Library.

01:52:48.850 --> 01:52:54.330
Each Root between the sectors is its own complex
environment, with its own sets of protocols

01:52:54.330 --> 01:52:57.860
and rituals required to safely travel through
it.

01:52:57.860 --> 01:53:02.619
Root Aleph, the bridge between the Archives
and the inaccessible core of Site-100, is

01:53:02.619 --> 01:53:07.920
a Volcanic Beach blocked off by an apparently
limitless obsidian wall, where fish made from

01:53:07.920 --> 01:53:11.030
living rock swim in the nearby waters.

01:53:11.030 --> 01:53:15.449
Root Beth, connecting the core and Sapient
Containment, is a huge and sprawling funhouse

01:53:15.449 --> 01:53:17.200
hall of mirrors.

01:53:17.200 --> 01:53:21.460
Anyone who attempts to travel through it inevitably
ends up turned around and arrives back at

01:53:21.460 --> 01:53:24.190
their starting point in Sapient Containment.

01:53:24.190 --> 01:53:29.050
Root Daleth, the bridge that connects Conceptual
Containment and the Core, is a massive ocean

01:53:29.050 --> 01:53:32.680
that has resisted all attempts by the Foundation
to traverse it.

01:53:32.680 --> 01:53:38.440
Root Vav, the bridge between Esoteric Containment
and Conceptual Containment, is a massive field

01:53:38.440 --> 01:53:41.380
filled with unidentified fruit trees.

01:53:41.380 --> 01:53:45.590
Foundation expeditions have found that it
too seems impossible to traverse.

01:53:45.590 --> 01:53:49.900
One expedition team was trapped inside for
a whole year, until one member of the team

01:53:49.900 --> 01:53:52.020
expressed a desire to go home.

01:53:52.020 --> 01:53:56.380
At that point, they were immediately teleported
back to the starting point.

01:53:56.380 --> 01:53:59.270
Root Tzaddi
connecting Administration to the CMS Sector,

01:53:59.270 --> 01:54:02.929
is a huge, lush forest on top of a floating
mountain.

01:54:02.929 --> 01:54:07.320
The only animals that seem to populate this
forest are non-anomalous flamingos.

01:54:07.320 --> 01:54:12.350
Next, we have Root Peh, the bridge between
the Archive and Administration, which appears

01:54:12.350 --> 01:54:16.670
to be a hallway on the fifth floor of a tenement
building in a city that the Foundation haven’t

01:54:16.670 --> 01:54:18.260
been able to locate.

01:54:18.260 --> 01:54:22.770
This building is populated by non-hostile
humanoid creatures, who will approach Foundation

01:54:22.770 --> 01:54:27.010
staff traversing Root Peh and invite them
into their apartments, offering to partake

01:54:27.010 --> 01:54:32.480
in recreational activities with them such
as video games, board games, or watching movies.

01:54:32.480 --> 01:54:36.690
The Foundation discourages its staff from
accepting any of these offers while on the

01:54:36.690 --> 01:54:37.690
job.

01:54:37.690 --> 01:54:43.230
And then there’s Root Shin, which connects
the Sapient and Conceptual containment sectors.

01:54:43.230 --> 01:54:48.409
This Root is unique in the sense that it acts
as a power generator for the rest of Site-100,

01:54:48.409 --> 01:54:53.790
as it’s filled with hundreds of large perpetual
motion machines producing a constant 8.7 gigawatts

01:54:53.790 --> 01:54:55.330
of electricity.

01:54:55.330 --> 01:54:59.670
These are only some of the many Roots illustrated
on the Site-100 diagram.

01:54:59.670 --> 01:55:03.639
As you’ve probably gathered by now, it’s
less like a conventional building and more

01:55:03.639 --> 01:55:06.530
like a whole crazy dimension unto itself.

01:55:06.530 --> 01:55:10.340
Why does the Foundation work to maintain such
a crazy place?

01:55:10.340 --> 01:55:14.250
Wouldn’t it just be easier to keep it a
secret, and contain it like any other anomaly?

01:55:14.250 --> 01:55:20.510
Well Site-100 wouldn’t be given the SCP-001
designation if it wasn’t incredibly important.

01:55:20.510 --> 01:55:26.260
If Site-100 was ever compromised, it would
lead to an inevitable K-Class End of the World

01:55:26.260 --> 01:55:31.909
Scenario, because the site is intrinsically
tied to the nature and containment of literally

01:55:31.909 --> 01:55:37.320
every single Keter-Class SCP in our universe
- hence the nickname “Keter Duty” for

01:55:37.320 --> 01:55:38.969
those working at the site.

01:55:38.969 --> 01:55:44.020
In fact, an anomaly can’t even be classed
as a Keter if it isn’t given “permission”

01:55:44.020 --> 01:55:45.550
by Site-100.

01:55:45.550 --> 01:55:50.570
The various sectors of Site-100 cover the
entire spectrum of anomalies, and each sector

01:55:50.570 --> 01:55:55.320
is a massive panoptic structure connected
by networks of glass elevators.

01:55:55.320 --> 01:56:00.130
Whenever a new Keter-Class SCP is discovered,
its name and a brief description of its anomalous

01:56:00.130 --> 01:56:04.610
traits will inscribe itself on one of the
walls in its corresponding sector.

01:56:04.610 --> 01:56:08.920
Ever been frustrated when the 05 Council refused
to sign off on an upgrade to Keter Class for

01:56:08.920 --> 01:56:12.860
a clearly dangerous SCP that poses extreme
risk of containment breach?

01:56:12.860 --> 01:56:18.070
Don’t blame them - it’s simply that Site-100
didn’t sanction the change.

01:56:18.070 --> 01:56:24.270
Any time that Site-100 sanctions a new SCP,
it also undergoes another unique process:

01:56:24.270 --> 01:56:30.489
It selects an SCP-001-K instance for the new
Keter, and creates a connection between them

01:56:30.489 --> 01:56:33.860
- using access points known as “Thresholds.”

01:56:33.860 --> 01:56:39.170
Think of it as simply opening a spatially-anomalous
door between two SCPs.

01:56:39.170 --> 01:56:46.030
Much like A Good Boy, another SCP vying for
the 001 slot, Site-100 has an intuitive grasp

01:56:46.030 --> 01:56:52.790
of the unseen connections between Keter-Class
anomalies, and each SCP-001-K instance is

01:56:52.790 --> 01:56:57.770
a complementary Keter Class that will essentially
cancel out the threat of its other half.

01:56:57.770 --> 01:57:03.580
Site-100 is a containment matchmaker, its
innate ability to use the anomalous to contain

01:57:03.580 --> 01:57:06.340
the anomalous is second to none.

01:57:06.340 --> 01:57:11.969
First, it took SCP-3984, an anomalous phenomenon
that seemed to prevent death from happening

01:57:11.969 --> 01:57:13.469
to all lifeforms.

01:57:13.469 --> 01:57:19.190
In order to mitigate the effects of 3984,
Site-100 opened a threshold between it and

01:57:19.190 --> 01:57:25.800
SCP-2935, also known as “O, Death” - an
alternate universe hidden beyond a limestone

01:57:25.800 --> 01:57:31.960
cavern where all life simultaneously ceased
to exist, even down to the bacterial level.

01:57:31.960 --> 01:57:36.830
By opening the threshold and allowing these
two absolute opposites to mix, it seemed to

01:57:36.830 --> 01:57:42.540
undermine the effects of both and create a
non-anomalous happy medium: Life, but mortal

01:57:42.540 --> 01:57:43.660
life.

01:57:43.660 --> 01:57:45.900
Next, SCP-5007.

01:57:45.900 --> 01:57:50.710
This terrifying underwater anomaly manifests
as a series of tentacle-like protrusions that

01:57:50.710 --> 01:57:56.830
snatch unfortunate creatures that get too
close, and assimilate them into its own mass.

01:57:56.830 --> 01:58:05.480
Site-100 cleverly opened a threshold to SCP-169,
a massive underwater arthropod known as The

01:58:05.480 --> 01:58:06.480
Leviathan.

01:58:06.480 --> 01:58:11.750
SCP-169 was tangled up by the tentacles, but
it’s too big to be fully consumed or assimilated,

01:58:11.750 --> 01:58:18.230
and the result is that 5007 is trapped in
a perpetually incapaciated state akin to choking,

01:58:18.230 --> 01:58:21.860
keeping it contained and stopping it from
going after anyone else.

01:58:21.860 --> 01:58:26.970
Let’s take a look at two even more hostile
and dangerous Keter-Class anomalies matched

01:58:26.970 --> 01:58:27.970
up by Site-100.

01:58:27.970 --> 01:58:36.239
First, we’ve got SCP-5501, an old camera
from the 1800s that comes with 18 photographs.

01:58:36.239 --> 01:58:40.800
These photographs act as a kind of portal
to an incredibly frightening alternate reality

01:58:40.800 --> 01:58:46.270
that creatures regularly crawl out of, attacking
and killing anyone within reach.

01:58:46.270 --> 01:58:52.660
Site-100 found a perfect match for this nasty
customer: SCP-1983.

01:58:52.660 --> 01:58:56.950
This is a small house that acts as a portal
to a race of tall monsters with needle-like

01:58:56.950 --> 01:59:00.630
appendages that leave the house in search
of victims.

01:59:00.630 --> 01:59:05.790
When they catch these victims, they take out
their hearts, and bring them back to the nest.

01:59:05.790 --> 01:59:12.890
Site-100 opened a threshold into the SCP-1983
house and placed the 5501 photographs inside.

01:59:12.890 --> 01:59:17.530
As a result, the hostile creatures from both
dimensions now regulate each other’s populations

01:59:17.530 --> 01:59:19.230
by killing each other.

01:59:19.230 --> 01:59:21.869
Another job well done for Site-100.

01:59:21.869 --> 01:59:27.239
Another Keter-Class dealt with by Site-100
is SCP-PL-122.

01:59:27.239 --> 01:59:33.110
This is a deadly plot of land in Poland, which
decays and corrodes all matter - organic or

01:59:33.110 --> 01:59:36.199
inorganic - placed within its confines.

01:59:36.199 --> 01:59:40.150
This would be bad enough, but as you’ll
often find with anomalous plots of deadly

01:59:40.150 --> 01:59:43.130
land, its area of influence is growing.

01:59:43.130 --> 01:59:46.400
Even knowing about it can cause it to become
more powerful.

01:59:46.400 --> 01:59:52.730
But Site-100 found its perfect Keter-Class
counterpart: SCP-1262.

01:59:52.730 --> 01:59:57.550
This is a massive mass of plant matter that
grows at a truly astonishing rate, expanding

01:59:57.550 --> 02:00:00.389
by around seven kilometers an hour.

02:00:00.389 --> 02:00:07.619
Much like absolute death and absolute life,
by putting 1262 into SCP-PL-122, a healthy

02:00:07.619 --> 02:00:10.110
medium was found somewhere in between.

02:00:10.110 --> 02:00:16.620
And finally, perhaps the strangest and most
creative match Site-100 has ever pulled off:

02:00:16.620 --> 02:00:19.310
SCP-3852 and SCP-2547.

02:00:19.310 --> 02:00:27.100
3852 is an anonymous corpse that manifests
in small towns, sowing fear and suspicion.

02:00:27.100 --> 02:00:31.790
Eventually, a local person is believed to
be responsible for this murder, and is lynched

02:00:31.790 --> 02:00:35.980
in a rage by the townspeople as a form of
vigilante justice.

02:00:35.980 --> 02:00:38.929
The corpse then moves on to the next town.

02:00:38.929 --> 02:00:44.800
2547, if you can believe it, is even weirder:
It’s a pack of dogs led by an intelligent

02:00:44.800 --> 02:00:47.960
talking Coyote dressed as a priest.

02:00:47.960 --> 02:00:53.040
Site-100 had the truly galaxy-brain idea to
open a threshold and connect the two.

02:00:53.040 --> 02:00:58.100
As a result, whenever the corpse manifests
in the town, the dogs rampage in and take

02:00:58.100 --> 02:00:59.100
over.

02:00:59.100 --> 02:01:04.100
At that point, they set up a kind of ridiculous
kangaroo court, where a jury made up of people

02:01:04.100 --> 02:01:08.440
from the town are forced to find 3852’s
scapegoat innocent.

02:01:08.440 --> 02:01:14.260
If they don’t, the dogs will simply hold
the town’s water supply hostage until 3852’s

02:01:14.260 --> 02:01:15.820
anomalous effects pass.

02:01:15.820 --> 02:01:17.300
Such an obvious idea!

02:01:17.300 --> 02:01:19.960
Now why didn’t the Foundation think of that?

02:01:19.960 --> 02:01:25.000
Keter Duty may not be the most conventional,
easy, or attractive work, but like everything

02:01:25.000 --> 02:01:30.320
the Foundation does, making sure Site-100
can keep doing its job is a necessary part

02:01:30.320 --> 02:01:33.700
of keeping our world safe from anomalous threats.

02:01:33.700 --> 02:01:37.040
Now if you’ll excuse us, we need to get
going.

02:01:37.040 --> 02:01:38.040
Hmmm.

02:01:38.040 --> 02:01:39.679
Do you know which is the right Root out of
here?

02:01:39.679 --> 02:01:42.619
Say, kids, would you like to hear a story?

02:01:42.619 --> 02:01:45.869
Cause we’ve got a really good one for you.

02:01:45.869 --> 02:01:46.869
Seriously.

02:01:46.869 --> 02:01:48.590
You're going to love it.

02:01:48.590 --> 02:01:54.100
It's a classic rags to riches tale, about
one man's rise from humble beginnings to becoming

02:01:54.100 --> 02:01:58.260
one of history's greatest and most visionary
toymakers.

02:01:58.260 --> 02:02:04.190
Or maybe it isn't, maybe it's about a company
that literally came from nothing, whose origins

02:02:04.190 --> 02:02:06.640
are still shrouded in mystery.

02:02:06.640 --> 02:02:10.219
Maybe it's about a woman breaking the glass
ceiling to take over the toy company left

02:02:10.219 --> 02:02:13.090
to her by her eccentric father.

02:02:13.090 --> 02:02:18.120
Maybe it's about all of these things, but
the one thing we can tell you about the story

02:02:18.120 --> 02:02:23.179
of Dr. Wondertainment is that every word of
it is true.

02:02:23.179 --> 02:02:29.060
Or at least, as far as anything is true in
the weird, wonderful world of the SCP Foundation.

02:02:29.060 --> 02:02:33.040
As long as you believe, we’ll all have a
wonderful time.

02:02:33.040 --> 02:02:41.080
As long as you believe, nothing can hurt you...Not
in the fabulous world of Dr. Wondertainment!

02:02:41.080 --> 02:02:48.389
Dr. Wondertainment is the name given to SCP-001,
who due to his relatively benign nature, has

02:02:48.389 --> 02:02:51.210
been classed as Safe by the Foundation.

02:02:51.210 --> 02:02:55.890
Rather than focusing on containing Wondertainment
himself, the SCP Foundation has centered its

02:02:55.890 --> 02:02:59.290
efforts on containing the products that he
creates.

02:02:59.290 --> 02:03:04.010
He is a Class-1 reality warper, capable of
constructing otherwise normal objects and

02:03:04.010 --> 02:03:06.739
imbuing them with anomalous properties.

02:03:06.739 --> 02:03:12.170
He's become infamous for using this ability
to create bizarre, magical, and potentially

02:03:12.170 --> 02:03:18.600
dangerous toys and games that are distributed
by as-yet unknown means.

02:03:18.600 --> 02:03:25.240
Many of Wondertainment's toys are in the Foundation’s
possession, such as SCP-445, origami paper

02:03:25.240 --> 02:03:31.410
that takes on properties of whatever it's
folded to look like, and SCP-3147, lollipops

02:03:31.410 --> 02:03:34.040
that allow people to switch voices with each
other.

02:03:34.040 --> 02:03:38.330
Dr. Wondertainment was born into a family
of humble means.

02:03:38.330 --> 02:03:42.040
His mother was a seamstress and his father
was an accountant.

02:03:42.040 --> 02:03:47.970
Unsatisfied with his mundane life, Wondertainment's
only joy growing up was in the stories that

02:03:47.970 --> 02:03:54.150
his father would tell him about an ancestor
of his who was once a famous toymaker.

02:03:54.150 --> 02:03:58.350
Inspired by these stories, Wondertainment
developed an interest in crafting toys, and

02:03:58.350 --> 02:04:02.540
as an adult, set out to learn the secrets
he would need to create toys unlike anything

02:04:02.540 --> 02:04:04.430
the world had ever seen.

02:04:04.430 --> 02:04:10.099
He spent his life following rumors of magical
artifacts and enchanted trinkets, until his

02:04:10.099 --> 02:04:13.560
search brought him to a mysterious factory.

02:04:13.560 --> 02:04:19.130
If you've seen our previous videos on SCP-001
proposals, you can probably guess that this

02:04:19.130 --> 02:04:27.910
factory was The Factory, the mysterious place
where new SCPs are supposedly created.

02:04:27.910 --> 02:04:31.639
Wondertainment barely escaped the massacre
and the Foundation takeover of the Factory

02:04:31.639 --> 02:04:36.830
with his life, but he was able to find a variety
of notes that he took with him.

02:04:36.830 --> 02:04:43.150
These notes contained clues that led him to
the workshop of his famous toy maker ancestor,

02:04:43.150 --> 02:04:47.119
and from there, he reclaimed his birthright.

02:04:47.119 --> 02:04:52.090
That was the day that he truly became Dr.
Wondertainment.

02:04:52.090 --> 02:04:54.120
It's a fun story, isn't it?

02:04:54.120 --> 02:04:55.120
Very straightforward.

02:04:55.120 --> 02:05:00.739
But perhaps it's a little underwhelming for
an SCP-001 proposal.

02:05:00.739 --> 02:05:06.470
After all, SCP-001 is the collective designation
given to some of the most important anomalies

02:05:06.470 --> 02:05:11.380
of all time - including many that could have
potentially been involved in the Foundation’s

02:05:11.380 --> 02:05:13.300
very founding.

02:05:13.300 --> 02:05:14.849
Let's start again.

02:05:14.849 --> 02:05:20.760
Reginald Philbert Lionel Archibald Westinghouse
Wondertainment III is the name given to SCP-001,

02:05:20.760 --> 02:05:27.770
who, due to his highly unpredictable nature,
has been classed as Euclid by the Foundation,

02:05:27.770 --> 02:05:33.110
and he is to be detained as soon as his location
can be ascertained.

02:05:33.110 --> 02:05:37.290
Until he can be captured, the SCP Foundation
has focused its efforts on containing the

02:05:37.290 --> 02:05:38.860
products that he creates.

02:05:38.860 --> 02:05:44.420
He is a Class-2 reality warper, capable of
constructing otherwise normal objects and

02:05:44.420 --> 02:05:47.340
imbuing them with anomalous properties.

02:05:47.340 --> 02:05:52.980
He's become infamous for using this ability
to create bizarre, magical, and potentially

02:05:52.980 --> 02:05:58.510
dangerous toys, games, candy, soft drinks
and other products aimed at children and young

02:05:58.510 --> 02:05:59.969
teens.

02:05:59.969 --> 02:06:03.690
These products are distributed by as-yet unknown
means.

02:06:03.690 --> 02:06:08.810
Many of Wondertainment's creations are in
Foundation possession, such as the often imitated

02:06:08.810 --> 02:06:13.480
but never matched Little Misters collection,
which are a group of living collectibles with

02:06:13.480 --> 02:06:16.070
unique anomalous properties.

02:06:16.070 --> 02:06:21.640
Due to Wondertainment's reality-warping abilities,
it's impossible to pin down concrete information

02:06:21.640 --> 02:06:23.230
about his history.

02:06:23.230 --> 02:06:28.420
What we can tell you for sure is that he's
immortal, and ageless, and comes from a long

02:06:28.420 --> 02:06:32.890
line of Wondertainments stretching all the
way back to the Cretaceous Period, where they

02:06:32.890 --> 02:06:36.929
made all sorts of toys for the good little
dinosaur children.

02:06:36.929 --> 02:06:42.260
It's also widely known that he is in fact
not a real person, but merely the manifestation

02:06:42.260 --> 02:06:48.580
of the dreams of every child on earth, brought
forth solely by the power of imagination.

02:06:48.580 --> 02:06:53.360
No confirmed sightings of Dr Wondertainment
have ever occurred, but witnesses have described

02:06:53.360 --> 02:06:58.099
him as “dashing”, “very handsome for
his age”, and a “lovely chap, capable

02:06:58.099 --> 02:07:01.719
of creating whimsy and wonder with the snap
of his fingers.”

02:07:01.719 --> 02:07:06.000
He's a tall man, about the height of a piece
of string, and he's immediately recognizable

02:07:06.000 --> 02:07:09.400
by his walking stick and W-shaped moustache.

02:07:09.400 --> 02:07:13.761
It's also been reported that he has scarring
around the circumference of both wrists, almost

02:07:13.761 --> 02:07:17.070
as if his hands had been removed and reattached
at some point.

02:07:17.070 --> 02:07:20.099
However, the truth of the matter is that-
Hm.

02:07:20.099 --> 02:07:23.239
No, no, we're telling it all wrong again.

02:07:23.239 --> 02:07:27.260
This doesn't do anything to capture the scope
of the Wondertainment story.

02:07:27.260 --> 02:07:32.699
It needs to feel bigger, more comprehensive.

02:07:32.699 --> 02:07:34.469
Let's try it again.

02:07:34.469 --> 02:07:41.580
Dr Wondertainment is a trademark of the Wondertainment
Toy Company, the name given to SCP-001, a

02:07:41.580 --> 02:07:46.560
corporation that, due to its consistent output
of anomalous items, is classed by the Foundation

02:07:46.560 --> 02:07:48.080
as Keter.

02:07:48.080 --> 02:07:52.540
Until this company can be permanently shut
down, the SCP Foundation has focused its efforts

02:07:52.540 --> 02:07:55.469
on containing the products that it creates.

02:07:55.469 --> 02:08:00.260
The collective power of the company's constituent
employees and the technology they make use

02:08:00.260 --> 02:08:04.100
are equivalent to that of a Class-3 reality
warper.

02:08:04.100 --> 02:08:08.679
The Wondertainment company produces and sells
a range of products, ranging from the seemingly

02:08:08.679 --> 02:08:14.090
normal to the downright weird, all imbued
with anomalous properties.

02:08:14.090 --> 02:08:19.030
The company has become infamous for their
constant output of bizarre, magical, and potentially

02:08:19.030 --> 02:08:24.800
dangerous toys, games, candy, soft drinks
and other products aimed at children, teens,

02:08:24.800 --> 02:08:26.699
and young at heart adults.

02:08:26.699 --> 02:08:31.100
These products are made and distributed from
Wonder World - trademark - a location that

02:08:31.100 --> 02:08:36.870
is as-yet unknown to the Foundation but offers
factory tours every hour from Tuesday to Friday.

02:08:36.870 --> 02:08:41.190
Many of Wondertainment's creations are in
Foundation possession, such as Wondertainment's

02:08:41.190 --> 02:08:46.699
famous Dragon Snails – the real fire breathing
pet you can keep in your pocket!

02:08:46.699 --> 02:08:50.239
Not much is known about the inner workings
of the Wondertainment company.

02:08:50.239 --> 02:08:55.070
The SCP Foundation has no information currently
on the company's leadership structure, location,

02:08:55.070 --> 02:08:57.849
history, or corporate policies.

02:08:57.849 --> 02:09:01.400
Various former and current employees have
been interviewed regarding their experiences

02:09:01.400 --> 02:09:07.320
working for Wondertainment, but they never
seem to be able to remember very much of use.

02:09:07.320 --> 02:09:12.040
Those interviewed variously describe the Wondertainment
company as a regular office building, an immense

02:09:12.040 --> 02:09:18.130
toy factory, an amusement park, but all agree
it's the best place they've ever worked!

02:09:18.130 --> 02:09:20.449
In fact, you should apply for a job there!

02:09:20.449 --> 02:09:27.090
We- I mean- they- have a few openings in their
legal department....or so I've heard.

02:09:27.090 --> 02:09:30.800
Oh, silly me, it seems we've gotten off topic.

02:09:30.800 --> 02:09:34.080
You're here to hear about the SCP-001 proposal.

02:09:34.080 --> 02:09:40.400
Posting a job ad wasn't what I meant to do
when I hacked into- I mean, well… don’t

02:09:40.400 --> 02:09:41.840
worry about that.

02:09:41.840 --> 02:09:43.110
Forget I said a thing.

02:09:43.110 --> 02:09:47.670
Now, let's try this again, but this time,
we'll add a twist.

02:09:47.670 --> 02:09:54.630
Isabel Helga Anastasia Parvati Wondertainment
the Fifth is the name given to SCP-001, who

02:09:54.630 --> 02:09:58.619
due to her ability to spread sunshine and
whimsy wherever she goes, has been classed

02:09:58.619 --> 02:10:04.481
as Thaumiel by the Foundation, and due to
her immensely unpredictable nature, the SCP

02:10:04.481 --> 02:10:07.120
foundation has resolved to just leave her
be.

02:10:07.120 --> 02:10:10.980
Because she can't be captured, the SCP foundation
has focused its efforts on containing the

02:10:10.980 --> 02:10:13.210
products that she creates.

02:10:13.210 --> 02:10:18.719
She is a Class-4 reality warper, capable of
constructing wonderful, fun-tastic objects

02:10:18.719 --> 02:10:22.030
and imbuing them with anomalous properties.

02:10:22.030 --> 02:10:26.630
She's famous and widely beloved for using
this ability to create bizarre, magical and

02:10:26.630 --> 02:10:31.270
not even a little bit dangerous toys, games,
candy, soft drinks and other products aimed

02:10:31.270 --> 02:10:34.500
at everyone from ages 9 to 99.

02:10:34.500 --> 02:10:38.540
These products are distributed by as-yet unknown
means.

02:10:38.540 --> 02:10:44.110
Many of Wondertainment's creations are in
Foundation possession, such as SCP-3551 - the

02:10:44.110 --> 02:10:51.410
awesome inflatable alien invaders, and SCP-2514,
a lovely horse who can sing Happy Birthday!

02:10:51.410 --> 02:10:53.780
How grand!

02:10:53.780 --> 02:10:57.260
Wondertainment inherited the Wondertainment
name from her father, who either passed away

02:10:57.260 --> 02:10:59.400
or never existed at all.

02:10:59.400 --> 02:11:04.739
The circumstances of his death and perhaps
non-existence were very messy, involving a

02:11:04.739 --> 02:11:10.140
mass murderer, the leader of a shadowy international
extra-governmental paramilitary organization,

02:11:10.140 --> 02:11:13.260
at least one deity, and four bent paper clips.

02:11:13.260 --> 02:11:15.960
She owns six corgis, and all of them are named
Jeremy.

02:11:15.960 --> 02:11:24.550
In her free time, she likes to-
No no, this is still wrong.

02:11:24.550 --> 02:11:26.880
Alright, enough is enough.

02:11:26.880 --> 02:11:29.370
You want to know who Dr. Wondertainment really
is?

02:11:29.370 --> 02:11:31.380
Well, you asked for it.

02:11:31.380 --> 02:11:39.440
Dr. Wondertainment is the name given to SCP-001,
who due to his deity-level power, has been

02:11:39.440 --> 02:11:42.410
classed as Apollyon by the Foundation.

02:11:42.410 --> 02:11:45.720
There is no possible way to contain him.

02:11:45.720 --> 02:11:51.699
He is a Class-5 reality warper, capable of
breaking down and reconstructing the very

02:11:51.699 --> 02:11:53.590
laws of reality.

02:11:53.590 --> 02:11:57.610
Did you really think that those little trinkets
were the full extent of my...

02:11:57.610 --> 02:12:00.550
I mean his creations?

02:12:00.550 --> 02:12:03.639
Did you truly think of him as such a small,
petty creature?

02:12:03.639 --> 02:12:07.949
Dr. Wondertainment is no mere toysmith…

02:12:07.949 --> 02:12:10.929
No, he is a god.

02:12:10.929 --> 02:12:12.889
Want examples of his creations?

02:12:12.889 --> 02:12:14.650
Just look around you!

02:12:14.650 --> 02:12:19.239
Everything from the most innocent Safe-class
to the most harrowing Keter-class, it's all

02:12:19.239 --> 02:12:21.989
thanks to him.

02:12:21.989 --> 02:12:24.190
He's behind everything!

02:12:24.190 --> 02:12:28.739
Marshall Carter and Dark, the Sarkists, The
Church of the Broken God, even the Scarlet

02:12:28.739 --> 02:12:29.780
King himself!

02:12:29.780 --> 02:12:38.430
All that time, all that effort, all it came
down to was one entity, one singular living

02:12:38.430 --> 02:12:41.030
personification of chaos.

02:12:41.030 --> 02:12:46.090
One day the SCP Foundation will finally give
up trying to find out how he distributes his

02:12:46.090 --> 02:12:51.610
products, when they will finally see how small
and worthless their attempts to restore order

02:12:51.610 --> 02:12:53.239
really are.

02:12:53.239 --> 02:13:05.830
AND THEY WILL BE DRIVEN BEFORE HIS POWER,
THEY WILL CRUMBLE AND DECAY INTO NOTHINGNESS,

02:13:05.830 --> 02:13:10.030
YOU WILL BOW BEFORE DR.

02:13:10.030 --> 02:13:11.030
WONDERTAINMENT!

02:13:11.030 --> 02:13:13.370
Had you going for a second there, didn't we?

02:13:13.370 --> 02:13:15.679
You should've seen the looks on your faces.

02:13:15.679 --> 02:13:19.139
But let's start again, one more time.

02:13:19.139 --> 02:13:21.380
We're being serious this time.

02:13:21.380 --> 02:13:25.060
Mask off, here's the true story of Dr. Wondertainment.

02:13:25.060 --> 02:13:32.699
Dr. Wondertainment is the name given to SCP-001,
who due to his relatively benign nature, has

02:13:32.699 --> 02:13:35.699
been classed as Neutralized by the Foundation.

02:13:35.699 --> 02:13:40.540
Rather than focusing on containing Wondertainment
himself, the SCP foundation has focused its

02:13:40.540 --> 02:13:43.830
efforts on containing the products that he
creates.

02:13:43.830 --> 02:13:48.560
He is a reality warper whose limits have yet
to be documented, capable of constructing

02:13:48.560 --> 02:13:52.930
otherwise normal objects and imbuing them
with anomalous properties.

02:13:52.930 --> 02:13:57.890
He's become infamous for using this ability
to create bizarre, magical and potentially

02:13:57.890 --> 02:14:03.639
dangerous toys and games that are distributed
by as-yet unknown means.

02:14:03.639 --> 02:14:08.889
Due to his secretive nature, almost nothing
is known of Dr. Wondertainment's true origins,

02:14:08.889 --> 02:14:12.990
and the waters have been muddied extensively
by the side effects of his reality-warping

02:14:12.990 --> 02:14:13.990
ability.

02:14:13.990 --> 02:14:19.940
In fact, it's entirely possible that Dr. Wondertainment
himself doesn't know who he is anymore.

02:14:19.940 --> 02:14:24.000
It's possible that all the proposed origins
and descriptions of Dr. Wondertainment are

02:14:24.000 --> 02:14:29.389
true in their own way, but it's equally possible
that none of them are.

02:14:29.389 --> 02:14:36.369
All that's known for sure is that Dr. Wondertainment
- be they male or female, corporation or single

02:14:36.369 --> 02:14:42.000
individual - is a constant thorn in the SCP
Foundation's side.

02:14:42.000 --> 02:14:47.100
No matter what they really are, they’re
not going away soon, and only time will tell

02:14:47.100 --> 02:14:53.350
who they’ll be tomorrow, or what further
horrors they and their company will create.

02:14:53.350 --> 02:14:56.510
And that’s where our story will have to
come to an end.

02:14:56.510 --> 02:14:58.340
At least, for now.

02:14:58.340 --> 02:15:01.869
We hope you enjoyed it, and remember: Keep
believing.

02:15:01.869 --> 02:15:04.750
Let’s get one thing clear.

02:15:04.750 --> 02:15:10.000
As much as it is fun to go through the various
articles on the SCP Archive, we should take

02:15:10.000 --> 02:15:13.830
a moment to acknowledge that it’s all fun
and games.

02:15:13.830 --> 02:15:20.320
The SCP Foundation, all the entities and objects,
creatures and people, places and stories related

02:15:20.320 --> 02:15:23.760
to them are just that: stories.

02:15:23.760 --> 02:15:26.920
Fiction created by the authors of an online
wiki website.

02:15:26.920 --> 02:15:30.400
It’s all designed to be a bit of harmless
entertainment.

02:15:30.400 --> 02:15:33.239
But what if it isn’t harmless?

02:15:33.239 --> 02:15:38.030
What if the characters within the world of
the SCP Archive somehow knew they had been

02:15:38.030 --> 02:15:40.840
created by the SCP Wiki authors?

02:15:40.840 --> 02:15:45.940
What would happen if fiction was aware that
it was, in fact, fictional?

02:15:45.940 --> 02:15:51.659
Ask yourself, would you want to know if your
world, your life, everything you had ever

02:15:51.659 --> 02:15:54.760
seen or known was all just a fantasy?

02:15:54.760 --> 02:15:59.100
If the answer is no, then you need to stop
watching this video right now, but we’ll

02:15:59.100 --> 02:16:04.210
warn you, just because you don’t know about
something, doesn’t necessarily stop it from

02:16:04.210 --> 02:16:05.739
being true.

02:16:05.739 --> 02:16:07.670
Still want to find out what’s going on?

02:16:07.670 --> 02:16:12.349
Good, then you need to hear about SCP-001.

02:16:12.349 --> 02:16:17.570
First things first, which of the various SCP-001s
are we talking about?

02:16:17.570 --> 02:16:21.960
Anyone looking for the earliest SCP will quickly
discover that there are many different entities

02:16:21.960 --> 02:16:24.420
and anomalies that share that number.

02:16:24.420 --> 02:16:27.650
There are a few, in-universe reasons for this.

02:16:27.650 --> 02:16:32.800
One is that all these anomalies were discovered
in the earliest days of the SCP Foundation,

02:16:32.800 --> 02:16:35.129
before their current numbering system was
introduced.

02:16:35.129 --> 02:16:37.889
Then there’s the other theories.

02:16:37.889 --> 02:16:43.649
For example, some have speculated that the
existence of many different SCP-001s is an

02:16:43.649 --> 02:16:49.619
intentional misdirection by the Foundation,
their way of keeping the nature of the true

02:16:49.619 --> 02:16:52.709
first SCP a closely-guarded secret.

02:16:52.709 --> 02:16:57.849
Regardless of what the reason is, the SCP-001
we’re looking at today is also known as

02:16:57.849 --> 02:16:59.449
“The Database.”

02:16:59.449 --> 02:17:04.121
Any and all information about The Database
is kept a secret from the entire SCP Foundation

02:17:04.121 --> 02:17:06.370
apart from the Overseer Council.

02:17:06.370 --> 02:17:08.219
And why is it such a secret?

02:17:08.219 --> 02:17:14.709
Well, that’s because SCP-001 contains details
of the very nature of the Foundation itself,

02:17:14.709 --> 02:17:15.999
including its creation.

02:17:15.999 --> 02:17:21.069
But we don’t mean when and how the organization
was founded, or its history.

02:17:21.069 --> 02:17:25.630
We mean how it was created, and by whom, in
our reality.

02:17:25.630 --> 02:17:26.630
Confused?

02:17:26.630 --> 02:17:29.059
Well, allow us to explain it.

02:17:29.059 --> 02:17:34.179
At first, the file for SCP-001 describes a
group of humanoid entities that have an ability

02:17:34.179 --> 02:17:36.019
to influence reality.

02:17:36.019 --> 02:17:41.300
All sounds like pretty standard, bread and
butter stuff for the SCP Foundation, right?

02:17:41.300 --> 02:17:42.300
WRONG.

02:17:42.300 --> 02:17:46.939
These entities are, in actual fact, the authors
of the SCP Wiki themselves.

02:17:46.939 --> 02:17:49.760
As in, the people in the real world.

02:17:49.760 --> 02:17:55.550
The reality of the SCP Foundation is constantly
changed by these writers; written and rewritten

02:17:55.550 --> 02:17:58.949
whenever someone edits an article on the SCP
Wiki.

02:17:58.949 --> 02:18:03.489
That’s all fine and harmless for us, but
the Wiki authors’ impact on their world

02:18:03.489 --> 02:18:06.699
is a cause of grave concern for the Foundation.

02:18:06.699 --> 02:18:12.079
As we mentioned at the start, we all know
that the SCP Foundation and it’s vast catalogue

02:18:12.079 --> 02:18:17.209
of user-generated articles on the creative
and the creepy are nothing more than a source

02:18:17.209 --> 02:18:20.040
of fictional online entertainment.

02:18:20.040 --> 02:18:24.249
It can be fun to study the lore and the nuances
of the different SCPs.

02:18:24.249 --> 02:18:29.529
It can be enjoyable appreciating the creativity
and hard work that the authors put into writing

02:18:29.529 --> 02:18:30.529
them.

02:18:30.529 --> 02:18:35.989
In the case of fan fiction, independent stories,
original SCPs, or even animated videos dedicated

02:18:35.989 --> 02:18:40.729
to explaining them, it can even inspire and
fuel our own written endeavors.

02:18:40.729 --> 02:18:47.029
But, at the end of the day, when all is said
and done, we all know that the SCP Foundation

02:18:47.029 --> 02:18:48.649
is purely fictional.

02:18:48.649 --> 02:18:52.849
What we don’t realize is that the Foundation
knows it too.

02:18:52.849 --> 02:18:57.529
Containing several pieces of information from
within their own archive, The Database contains

02:18:57.529 --> 02:19:01.219
everything the Foundation knows about our
real world.

02:19:01.219 --> 02:19:04.969
This includes everything about the real authors
of the SCP Wiki.

02:19:04.969 --> 02:19:06.870
And you thought Deadpool was meta.

02:19:06.870 --> 02:19:11.819
You see, because the SCP Wiki has articles
from numerous different creative writers,

02:19:11.819 --> 02:19:17.339
chances are, the details of every new article
might not always line up with every previous

02:19:17.339 --> 02:19:18.339
one.

02:19:18.339 --> 02:19:23.069
For a long time, there has been much discussion
amongst devoted SCP fans regarding the “canon”

02:19:23.069 --> 02:19:24.109
of the website.

02:19:24.109 --> 02:19:27.949
Now, we don’t mean a big gun that launches
metal balls.

02:19:27.949 --> 02:19:32.760
When we say canon, we mean all of the events
and stories that are considered to be an official

02:19:32.760 --> 02:19:36.679
part of the on-going story of the SCP Foundation.

02:19:36.679 --> 02:19:38.399
Still with us so far?

02:19:38.399 --> 02:19:43.139
Because there are so many writers and articles
on the Wiki, the canon of the SCP Archive

02:19:43.139 --> 02:19:45.629
is a bit inconsistent, to say the least.

02:19:45.629 --> 02:19:49.899
And that’s fine for us, because we know
none of it is real.

02:19:49.899 --> 02:19:55.159
It doesn’t have to all line up, just as
long as a good story is being told.

02:19:55.159 --> 02:20:01.100
But these inconsistencies; all the little
cracks of discrepancy and disparity; are what

02:20:01.100 --> 02:20:06.140
made the Foundation themselves realize that
they are truly living in a fiction.

02:20:06.140 --> 02:20:12.510
In other words, SCP-001 is the SCP Foundation’s
window through what we would experience as

02:20:12.510 --> 02:20:13.810
the fourth wall.

02:20:13.810 --> 02:20:18.659
The fourth wall is the metaphorical barrier
that separates what we know to be real, from

02:20:18.659 --> 02:20:20.870
what we know to be purely fiction.

02:20:20.870 --> 02:20:26.090
In other words, it’s the line between the
audience and the fiction that they are watching,

02:20:26.090 --> 02:20:29.420
the edge of the stage or the glass of the
television screen.

02:20:29.420 --> 02:20:35.680
And the SCP Foundation is staring through
that fourth wall, looking out at you and me.

02:20:35.680 --> 02:20:40.579
That’s right, it isn’t just the authors
that the Foundation are aware of, it’s all

02:20:40.579 --> 02:20:41.829
of us.

02:20:41.829 --> 02:20:46.270
According to their own researchers, the Foundation
has determined that we, the audience and the

02:20:46.270 --> 02:20:49.720
writers, exist in something known as the Alpha
Layer.

02:20:49.720 --> 02:20:51.369
What on Earth is an Alpha Layer?

02:20:51.369 --> 02:20:57.169
Well, imagine our reality, the world and the
universe as we know it, is a slice of bread.

02:20:57.169 --> 02:21:00.550
It’s a strange analogy, we know, but stick
with us.

02:21:00.550 --> 02:21:05.649
Now, picture the fictional world of the SCP
Foundation as another slice of bread underneath

02:21:05.649 --> 02:21:06.850
ours.

02:21:06.850 --> 02:21:11.159
In-between the two can be whatever you like,
but the point isn’t that the world is a

02:21:11.159 --> 02:21:12.159
sandwich.

02:21:12.159 --> 02:21:17.989
The point is, that we exist on a layer of
reality above that of the SCP Wiki, and the

02:21:17.989 --> 02:21:21.529
filling is just what keeps reality and fiction
separate.

02:21:21.529 --> 02:21:27.439
So, as we mentioned, the Foundation is aware
of any writers and readers of the SCP Wiki,

02:21:27.439 --> 02:21:29.629
and this does include you.

02:21:29.629 --> 02:21:33.329
But the Wiki authors are the primary focus
of The Database.

02:21:33.329 --> 02:21:37.640
After all, it’s the writers who are responsible
for creating the fictional world that the

02:21:37.640 --> 02:21:39.869
SCP Foundation exists in.

02:21:39.869 --> 02:21:45.089
Anything that forms a part of the narrative
of that world, every article, every tale,

02:21:45.089 --> 02:21:50.220
every new SCP that gets published, even parts
of the Wiki that get taken down or rewritten

02:21:50.220 --> 02:21:53.450
all have an impact on the Foundation’s universe.

02:21:53.450 --> 02:21:58.770
When authors link their new SCPs to pre-existing
ones, or create connections to a Group of

02:21:58.770 --> 02:22:03.449
Interest like the Church of the Broken God
or the Global Occult Coalition, their writing

02:22:03.449 --> 02:22:08.529
ends up making even more of a substantial
development to the overall narrative.

02:22:08.529 --> 02:22:11.620
And all of it ends up in The Database.

02:22:11.620 --> 02:22:17.369
The readers of the SCP Wiki, on the other
hand, are a smaller part of SCP-001.

02:22:17.369 --> 02:22:22.170
Mainly because they do not write or publish
the content found on the website itself.

02:22:22.170 --> 02:22:26.760
Anything that is not specifically set in stone
by a Wiki author, can be interpreted in various

02:22:26.760 --> 02:22:28.689
ways by a reader.

02:22:28.689 --> 02:22:34.680
A reader’s interpretation is a powerful
concept, and should not be underestimated.

02:22:34.680 --> 02:22:38.420
Interpretation is the difference between reading
Animal Farm as a story about a group of animals

02:22:38.420 --> 02:22:43.319
rebelling against their human farmer, and
understanding it as a satirical and political

02:22:43.319 --> 02:22:46.750
allegory for the events leading up to the
Russian Revolution.

02:22:46.750 --> 02:22:51.409
So what does interpretation have to do with
SCP-001?

02:22:51.409 --> 02:22:56.319
The point we are getting at is that any unwritten
detail or anything that isn’t explicitly

02:22:56.319 --> 02:23:01.199
stated by a Wiki author, can be changed by
a reader’s own imagination.

02:23:01.199 --> 02:23:06.020
This can be anything, from the appearance
or personality of an SCP or character, to

02:23:06.020 --> 02:23:08.909
a detail about the world of the Foundation.

02:23:08.909 --> 02:23:13.979
And in the same vein, if something in one
SCP article contradicts something written

02:23:13.979 --> 02:23:19.369
in another, the reader is free to choose which
of them they accept as part of the universe’s

02:23:19.369 --> 02:23:20.510
true canon.

02:23:20.510 --> 02:23:25.300
Each reader of the SCP Wiki has their own
understanding of the material written there,

02:23:25.300 --> 02:23:29.539
and inevitably comprehends their own version
of the events within.

02:23:29.539 --> 02:23:35.209
And this is something that the SCP Foundation,
even in their world of fiction, is aware of

02:23:35.209 --> 02:23:39.589
- or more specifically, the O5 Council is
aware of.

02:23:39.589 --> 02:23:46.630
You see, the secretive overseers are the only
ones with any knowledge of SCP-001.

02:23:46.630 --> 02:23:51.229
Only they can access The Database, only they
know the truth.

02:23:51.229 --> 02:23:55.529
The fact that they exist in this fictional
capacity is something the Overseer Council

02:23:55.529 --> 02:23:58.859
hopes to hide from the rest of the Foundation’s
personnel.

02:23:58.859 --> 02:24:03.270
In an effort to keep the rest of their staff
from asking too many questions, the Council

02:24:03.270 --> 02:24:07.810
has told them that there is currently no way
in existence that they could possibly contain

02:24:07.810 --> 02:24:09.260
SCP-001.

02:24:09.260 --> 02:24:16.439
But, to reassure personnel, the O5s have also
stated that this does not pose any risk, nor

02:24:16.439 --> 02:24:21.020
would it lead to the total and utter destruction
of their observable, fictional universe.

02:24:21.020 --> 02:24:26.470
Instead, the Council aims to focus on what
they can control, by containing any and all

02:24:26.470 --> 02:24:30.609
information about SCP-001.

02:24:30.609 --> 02:24:35.609
Nothing about The Database, or the truth that
it contains, is to ever leave O5 Command under

02:24:35.609 --> 02:24:38.120
any circumstance whatsoever.

02:24:38.120 --> 02:24:45.169
All of the information about SCP-001, or what
it contains, is kept in an encrypted, highly-classified

02:24:45.169 --> 02:24:47.350
form, at an unknown location.

02:24:47.350 --> 02:24:52.209
The key needed to decrypt this data is a pass
code split into three parts.

02:24:52.209 --> 02:24:57.239
This key is then memorized by members of the
O5 Council, each memorizing a different portion

02:24:57.239 --> 02:24:58.560
of the pass code.

02:24:58.560 --> 02:25:02.760
It can only be accessed if every member of
the Council unanimously agrees that it is

02:25:02.760 --> 02:25:04.909
absolutely necessary.

02:25:04.909 --> 02:25:10.229
And even when they do decrypt the information
about SCP-001, it remains for the eyes of

02:25:10.229 --> 02:25:14.529
O5 Command, and strictly their eyes only.

02:25:14.529 --> 02:25:20.529
Any member of the SCP Foundation caught leaking
data about SCP-001 is to be contained by any

02:25:20.529 --> 02:25:22.359
means necessary.

02:25:22.359 --> 02:25:26.270
This also includes if a member of personnel
attempts to get this classified information

02:25:26.270 --> 02:25:31.640
out via espionage, psychic leakage, or other
devious methods.

02:25:31.640 --> 02:25:35.340
Foundation researchers are even banned from
conducting any of their own investigations

02:25:35.340 --> 02:25:40.560
into the nature of SCP-001, or the data it
contains.

02:25:40.560 --> 02:25:45.920
If a lower level staff member was to somehow
find out the truth, that the entire Foundation

02:25:45.920 --> 02:25:50.220
is just a fiction, then that person would
be at the mercy of the most senior figure

02:25:50.220 --> 02:25:52.149
on the O5 Council.

02:25:52.149 --> 02:25:56.640
It would be up to that senior figure to decide
the staff member’s fate.

02:25:56.640 --> 02:26:00.409
Anyone with high enough clearance or status
within the Foundation who found out about

02:26:00.409 --> 02:26:05.340
SCP-001, would alternatively be given a Class
A amnestic.

02:26:05.340 --> 02:26:09.710
These are memory altering drugs that the SCP
Foundation uses to keep information about

02:26:09.710 --> 02:26:11.669
anomalies a secret.

02:26:11.669 --> 02:26:14.039
Apparently, even from its own staff.

02:26:14.039 --> 02:26:18.819
Still, having your mind wiped has got to be
better than being killed or contained, just

02:26:18.819 --> 02:26:22.729
for realizing you’re a fictional character
on an online wiki.

02:26:22.729 --> 02:26:27.760
The O5 Council have plans in mind for us,
and for the SCP Wiki writers responsible for

02:26:27.760 --> 02:26:29.039
creating them.

02:26:29.039 --> 02:26:34.369
The SCP Wiki entry on The Database closes
with a proposal; a way that the O5 Council

02:26:34.369 --> 02:26:39.449
can reach out of their fiction, directly to
the wiki’s authors in the real world.

02:26:39.449 --> 02:26:40.449
From there?

02:26:40.449 --> 02:26:44.949
Their goal is simple: through memetic kill
agents, the SCP Foundation will put the Wiki

02:26:44.949 --> 02:26:47.310
authors to sleep and then kill them.

02:26:47.310 --> 02:26:49.539
Sounds pretty far-fetched, doesn’t it?

02:26:49.539 --> 02:26:54.680
After all, when was the last time something
fictional killed someone in our real world?

02:26:54.680 --> 02:26:58.310
Even more bizarre, what if this kill agent
already exists?

02:26:58.310 --> 02:27:02.800
The O5 Council must have known for a while
that their world is fictional, so they’ve

02:27:02.800 --> 02:27:07.939
had plenty of time to develop a kill agent,
some way of reaching us and the SCP Wiki authors

02:27:07.939 --> 02:27:09.720
in the real world.

02:27:09.720 --> 02:27:16.470
Worse still, what if this kill agent is already
out there somewhere, lurking on the SCP Archive,

02:27:16.470 --> 02:27:18.930
just waiting for you to find it?

02:27:18.930 --> 02:27:21.609
And if you read it, how would it kill you?

02:27:21.609 --> 02:27:24.739
If you don’t want to know, then that’s
your choice to make.

02:27:24.739 --> 02:27:30.379
But if curiosity is getting the better of
you, then remember this: Beware SCP-5999.

02:27:30.379 --> 02:27:38.380
If you ask anyone, any person from any culture,
any part of the world, to describe what death

02:27:38.380 --> 02:27:43.539
looks like, most people will immediately jump
to a depiction of the Grim Reaper.

02:27:43.539 --> 02:27:48.449
And rightly so, the Reaper has long been the
personification of death and decay.

02:27:48.449 --> 02:27:54.199
An omen of demise, the cloaked skeleton bearing
a sharp scythe, coming to collect souls and

02:27:54.199 --> 02:27:57.129
carry them off to either Heaven or Hell.

02:27:57.129 --> 02:28:01.629
For centuries, human beings have thought of
the Grim Reaper as death itself, but he’s

02:28:01.629 --> 02:28:07.800
more of an embodiment of it, a symbol meant
to represent that all-too-familiar fear of

02:28:07.800 --> 02:28:13.159
not knowing what lies beyond life on this
fragile mortal plane of existence.

02:28:13.159 --> 02:28:17.560
Death itself, the real death, looks completely
different.

02:28:17.560 --> 02:28:20.419
Welcome to the story of SCP-001.

02:28:20.419 --> 02:28:26.239
Now, first things first, to anyone familiar
with the SCP Foundation, you will most likely

02:28:26.239 --> 02:28:30.039
know that there are multiple SCP-001s.

02:28:30.039 --> 02:28:33.350
You might even think you know which of them
is the real one.

02:28:33.350 --> 02:28:39.039
But for those of you who are new here, allow
us to clarify for you this important context.

02:28:39.039 --> 02:28:45.899
The designation of “SCP-001” doesn’t
refer to a single creature, object or entity,

02:28:45.899 --> 02:28:50.760
but rather a collection of various anomalies
that are allegedly kept contained by the SCP

02:28:50.760 --> 02:28:51.760
Foundation.

02:28:51.760 --> 02:28:56.199
Now, there are multiple explanations as to
why these various files are all collected

02:28:56.199 --> 02:29:00.000
under the shared designation of SCP-001.

02:29:00.000 --> 02:29:04.109
One explanation could be that this is because
these anomalies are some of the earliest ever

02:29:04.109 --> 02:29:06.130
contained by the Foundation.

02:29:06.130 --> 02:29:11.810
By this rationale, all the SCP-001s share
the same designation because they were first

02:29:11.810 --> 02:29:17.749
encountered before the SCP Foundation established
the numbering system that it currently uses.

02:29:17.749 --> 02:29:23.560
However, there also exists a theory that this
is nothing more than intentional misdirection.

02:29:23.560 --> 02:29:27.790
If we choose to believe this explanation,
then it could mean that the many different

02:29:27.790 --> 02:29:32.289
SCP-001s are a devious ploy by the Foundation
themselves.

02:29:32.289 --> 02:29:37.010
In the interest of maintaining secrecy and
security, having many files sharing the name

02:29:37.010 --> 02:29:43.879
SCP-001 could be the Foundation’s way of
keeping the nature of the true first SCP a

02:29:43.879 --> 02:29:45.399
closely guarded secret.

02:29:45.399 --> 02:29:50.420
It seems plausible that the multiple SCP-001
files could be an attempt by the Foundation

02:29:50.420 --> 02:29:52.439
to conceal information.

02:29:52.439 --> 02:29:57.090
After all, it wouldn’t be the first time
this secretive organization deceived someone.

02:29:57.090 --> 02:30:01.479
So, what exactly is this particularly morbid
take on SCP-001?

02:30:01.479 --> 02:30:07.500
Well first, you have to have a pretty high
level of security clearance within the SCP

02:30:07.500 --> 02:30:10.590
Foundation if you want to even come close
to accessing this file.

02:30:10.590 --> 02:30:16.659
In fact, any and all details about the anomaly
codenamed Dead Men is protected by Hellenstic,

02:30:16.659 --> 02:30:22.330
an AIC used by the Foundation’s Overwatch
Command, also known as the O5 Council.

02:30:22.330 --> 02:30:27.310
An AIC, for those who are not yet aware, is
an advanced form of artificial intelligence

02:30:27.310 --> 02:30:32.180
that the Foundation develops and uses to run
parts of its archive of anomalies.

02:30:32.180 --> 02:30:34.160
What does that mean for SCP-001?

02:30:34.160 --> 02:30:39.529
Well, it’s pretty simple: the people in
charge of the Foundation want this file to

02:30:39.529 --> 02:30:41.459
remain secure.

02:30:41.459 --> 02:30:46.359
Or it could be because the O5 Council is hiding
something, something that the general staff

02:30:46.359 --> 02:30:48.699
members aren’t meant to know about.

02:30:48.699 --> 02:30:54.390
Getting past all the additional security surrounding
this particular file, we learn that SCP-001,

02:30:54.390 --> 02:30:57.229
or this one at least, is...

02:30:57.229 --> 02:30:58.229
An old man.

02:30:58.229 --> 02:31:01.069
An 84 year old man, to be precise.

02:31:01.069 --> 02:31:02.089
Wait, that’s it?

02:31:02.089 --> 02:31:04.720
That’s what the big, closely guarded secret
is?

02:31:04.720 --> 02:31:06.159
Just some old guy?

02:31:06.159 --> 02:31:11.069
No, of course he’s not just “some old
guy”, the Foundation’s highest ranking

02:31:11.069 --> 02:31:15.379
members wouldn’t go through such trouble
over one ordinary man.

02:31:15.379 --> 02:31:18.729
This particular man has become one with death.

02:31:18.729 --> 02:31:22.409
Not the Reaper, no… death itself.

02:31:22.409 --> 02:31:26.470
The very concept of death has been merged
with this individual.

02:31:26.470 --> 02:31:29.699
A lot more interesting than just a normal,
old man, right?

02:31:29.699 --> 02:31:34.489
To be clear, this man is not an incarnation
or embodiment of death like the Grim Reaper.

02:31:34.489 --> 02:31:40.749
Instead, he has become a vessel for the process
of making something that was once alive, not.

02:31:40.749 --> 02:31:46.350
So, this old man, SCP-001, can control life
and death?

02:31:46.350 --> 02:31:47.359
Not quite.

02:31:47.359 --> 02:31:51.649
The old man’s body is more like a way that
death itself can be influenced.

02:31:51.649 --> 02:31:57.439
It may help to picture it like this - Imagine
SCP-001 as a television remote control for

02:31:57.439 --> 02:31:58.439
death.

02:31:58.439 --> 02:32:02.170
Except instead of pressing buttons like you
would on a remote, you have to remove or alter

02:32:02.170 --> 02:32:04.300
parts of the old man’s body.

02:32:04.300 --> 02:32:10.589
And in doing so, you can manipulate the process
of death, albeit only to a limited extent.

02:32:10.589 --> 02:32:14.919
You can’t, for example, permanently stop
death from existing or occurring, stopping

02:32:14.919 --> 02:32:16.830
everyone around the world from dying.

02:32:16.830 --> 02:32:19.810
That’s not quite how SCP-001 works.

02:32:19.810 --> 02:32:23.119
Here, let’s give you an example.

02:32:23.119 --> 02:32:27.970
SCP-001 had his tongue removed as well as
had sustained damage to his eardrums before

02:32:27.970 --> 02:32:29.709
he was contained by the Foundation.

02:32:29.709 --> 02:32:34.609
So, as a result of those alterations to his
body, there are fewer “Deals with Death”

02:32:34.609 --> 02:32:36.350
events in the modern era.

02:32:36.350 --> 02:32:38.020
You see what we mean now?

02:32:38.020 --> 02:32:44.419
Changing SCP-001 changes how death functions,
but doesn’t necessarily stop it from happening.

02:32:44.419 --> 02:32:50.709
So in essence, although there are parameters,
SCP-001 is the Foundation’s way of controlling

02:32:50.709 --> 02:32:51.709
death itself.

02:32:51.709 --> 02:32:54.159
How did they decide to go about doing this?

02:32:54.159 --> 02:32:58.649
Well, once we tell you, you will understand
why the O5 Council wanted to keep information

02:32:58.649 --> 02:33:02.290
about SCP-001 such a secret.

02:33:02.290 --> 02:33:06.300
After performing a series of complex brain
surgeries and various other procedures on

02:33:06.300 --> 02:33:11.930
the old man, the Overwatch Command intentionally
engineered him to be unable to perceive certain

02:33:11.930 --> 02:33:12.930
people.

02:33:12.930 --> 02:33:14.379
Who were those people?

02:33:14.379 --> 02:33:17.810
You guessed it, the O5 Council themselves.

02:33:17.810 --> 02:33:23.770
Making SCP-001 unable to recognize the faces
of any O5 Council members, means that death

02:33:23.770 --> 02:33:27.760
is unable to see or perceive the council members
either.

02:33:27.760 --> 02:33:34.029
All those pieces fit together to form a particularly
unsettling jigsaw puzzle: by tampering with

02:33:34.029 --> 02:33:39.979
SCP-001, the O5 Council have made themselves
effectively immortal.

02:33:39.979 --> 02:33:45.550
They cannot die, nor will they age or decay
like normal, mortal human beings.

02:33:45.550 --> 02:33:50.659
Death still occurs of course, other beings
can die, but the council members are exempt

02:33:50.659 --> 02:33:53.479
from that fundamental law of nature.

02:33:53.479 --> 02:33:59.539
The Foundation believes that SCP-001 was initially
created by an occult group known as The Eternal

02:33:59.539 --> 02:34:00.539
Circle.

02:34:00.539 --> 02:34:04.839
Thanks to records recovered from the Circle’s
London headquarters, the SCP Foundation now

02:34:04.839 --> 02:34:09.300
knows that they were the ones responsible
for merging the old man with the concept of

02:34:09.300 --> 02:34:10.300
death.

02:34:10.300 --> 02:34:16.249
When their personnel first recovered SCP-001,
the old man was frail, in a poor physical

02:34:16.249 --> 02:34:20.600
condition and barely responded to any external
stimuli.

02:34:20.600 --> 02:34:24.890
Research staff believed he must have suffered
severe trauma at the hands of the Eternal

02:34:24.890 --> 02:34:29.810
Circle, evidenced by the circular symbols
that had been carved into his back, oh, and

02:34:29.810 --> 02:34:33.380
also the fact that his body parts had all
been modified.

02:34:33.380 --> 02:34:39.859
Contained within the file for this SCP-001
is a letter directly from the O5 Council themselves,

02:34:39.859 --> 02:34:43.029
explaining their reasons for using the old
man to become immortal.

02:34:43.029 --> 02:34:47.699
They justify their actions by claiming that
they have a wealth of experience in containing

02:34:47.699 --> 02:34:51.169
anomalies and keeping the SCP Foundation running.

02:34:51.169 --> 02:34:56.011
This is, to them, a perfectly valid reason
to make themselves exempt from death, rather

02:34:56.011 --> 02:35:02.539
than aging, retiring and dying, to later be
replaced by new members on the Overwatch Council.

02:35:02.539 --> 02:35:06.970
They claim that their immortality is not for
their own self benefit of course, but for

02:35:06.970 --> 02:35:13.169
the good of the Foundation as an organization,
and by extension, the world as a whole.

02:35:13.169 --> 02:35:17.319
The council also promised that the same death
exempt status would later be extended to other

02:35:17.319 --> 02:35:19.340
vital members of personnel.

02:35:19.340 --> 02:35:24.319
However, according to the Hellenstic AIC guarding
the file “No personnel have been considered

02:35:24.319 --> 02:35:26.560
for death-exempt status in the future.”

02:35:26.560 --> 02:35:31.089
In other words, the O5 Council were lying,
and intended to keep their Get out of Death

02:35:31.089 --> 02:35:33.149
Free card to themselves.

02:35:33.149 --> 02:35:37.109
It wasn’t long before the Foundation’s
very own Ethics Committee learned about what

02:35:37.109 --> 02:35:41.680
the Council was up to, and naturally, they
had some concerns.

02:35:41.680 --> 02:35:46.510
According to a report issued by committee
chairman Odongo Tejani, the way the O5 Council

02:35:46.510 --> 02:35:53.390
were using SCP-001 to prolong their own lives
was immoral and inhumane, even by their own

02:35:53.390 --> 02:35:54.960
strange standards.

02:35:54.960 --> 02:35:59.779
By using this poor, frail old man for their
own gain, the Council had warped the natural

02:35:59.779 --> 02:36:05.419
way death should work, and threatened to anomalously
unbalance the very laws of nature.

02:36:05.419 --> 02:36:09.779
The Ethics Committee had no other choice but
to dispatch its own Mobile Task Force, known

02:36:09.779 --> 02:36:14.419
as Omega 1, or the “Law’s Left Hand”,
to rectify the situation.

02:36:14.419 --> 02:36:15.419
Their mission?

02:36:15.419 --> 02:36:19.539
To detain all members of the O5 Council at
their next meeting, removing them from office

02:36:19.539 --> 02:36:24.770
and replacing them with high ranking candidates
from within the Foundation’s lower ranks.

02:36:24.770 --> 02:36:30.649
Finally, they also planned to neutralize SCP-001,
cleaning house and removing the temptation

02:36:30.649 --> 02:36:34.300
for future council members to make themselves
immortal.

02:36:34.300 --> 02:36:36.569
In short, this was a coup.

02:36:36.569 --> 02:36:41.080
The O5 Council was going to be overthrown
by their own ethics committee.

02:36:41.080 --> 02:36:45.529
Of course, the council were more than prepared
for this, and had their very own Mobile Task

02:36:45.529 --> 02:36:48.340
Force on hand to defend them against the plot.

02:36:48.340 --> 02:36:53.409
Alpha 1, also known under the codename “Red
Right Hand” - the legendary lackeys of the

02:36:53.409 --> 02:36:56.439
O5 Council - clashed with the Law’s Left
Hand.

02:36:56.439 --> 02:37:01.419
It is believed that the shadowy Administrator
of the SCP Foundation also had his own personal

02:37:01.419 --> 02:37:06.839
task force, possibly Rēsh 1, also called
the “Seat of Consciousness”, enter the

02:37:06.839 --> 02:37:07.839
fray.

02:37:07.839 --> 02:37:13.760
In other words, we were looking at an absolutely
insane three-way Foundation civil war bloodbath.

02:37:13.760 --> 02:37:16.039
How exciting!

02:37:16.039 --> 02:37:21.061
Security footage showed these three groups
engaged in a fire fight within Site 01, using

02:37:21.061 --> 02:37:25.550
Foundation training and tactics against each
other in what was probably the most epic battle

02:37:25.550 --> 02:37:27.359
of all of their lives.

02:37:27.359 --> 02:37:31.609
It was absolute chaos - the air thick with
screams and gunsmoke.

02:37:31.609 --> 02:37:36.619
Cameras also picked up a group of men and
women, lying all around Site 01, many wounded

02:37:36.619 --> 02:37:38.250
but still alive.

02:37:38.250 --> 02:37:42.300
Impressive, given how many of them had taken
gunshots right to their heads.

02:37:42.300 --> 02:37:47.760
That’s right, these were presumed to be
the members of the O5 Council, still unable

02:37:47.760 --> 02:37:49.939
to die despite being shot.

02:37:49.939 --> 02:37:54.949
It is unclear which of the MTFs was responsible
for this, the Ethics Committee had only intended

02:37:54.949 --> 02:37:57.189
Law’s Left Hand to secure the council members.

02:37:57.189 --> 02:38:01.420
It could well be that they were caught in
the crossfire that occurred as the Law’s

02:38:01.420 --> 02:38:04.090
Left Hand and Red Right Hand teams fought.

02:38:04.090 --> 02:38:08.439
Unless, of course, the Administrators task
force were the ones who had stepped in and

02:38:08.439 --> 02:38:10.159
shot the O5 Council.

02:38:10.159 --> 02:38:15.720
Through all the chaos that had unfurled, SCP-001
was still in his cell.

02:38:15.720 --> 02:38:17.989
And he wasn’t alone.

02:38:17.989 --> 02:38:24.169
An unknown figure had somehow gained access,
and he conversed with SCP-001.

02:38:24.169 --> 02:38:29.909
The man went on to tell SCP-001 that the Foundation
was wrong to tamper with the nature of death,

02:38:29.909 --> 02:38:31.359
and recounted a story.

02:38:31.359 --> 02:38:36.700
He said that he had once filed paperwork regarding
anomalies for an unknown organization, but

02:38:36.700 --> 02:38:39.819
couldn’t live with the horror of what his
job entailed.

02:38:39.819 --> 02:38:45.649
So, the man sold these files to a group of
thirteen individuals: the O5 Council.

02:38:45.649 --> 02:38:51.169
They then went on to form a full organization,
the SCP Foundation as we know it.

02:38:51.169 --> 02:38:57.649
The man then stated he was disgusted with
how the Foundation had used SCP-001, how the

02:38:57.649 --> 02:39:01.919
council members had engineered the frail,
old man to make themselves immortal.

02:39:01.919 --> 02:39:06.909
He had hoped they would be a force for good,
keeping any necessary evil to a minimum.

02:39:06.909 --> 02:39:12.279
The unknown figure told SCP-001 that the conflict
between the council and the Ethics Committee

02:39:12.279 --> 02:39:17.510
had happened many times before, with many
other versions of the old man.

02:39:17.510 --> 02:39:21.590
Earlier SCP-001s, previously merged with the
concept of death.

02:39:21.590 --> 02:39:28.060
He then helped SCP-001 identify the members
of the council, ending their immortality,

02:39:28.060 --> 02:39:32.149
promising the weak, tired old man that he’d
finally be able to rest.

02:39:32.149 --> 02:39:37.159
The unknown mystery man claimed that he would
always be in power, the O5 Council would always

02:39:37.159 --> 02:39:38.550
bring him back.

02:39:38.550 --> 02:39:46.220
After all, he was their figurehead, their
leader, the SCP Foundation Administrator himself.

02:39:46.220 --> 02:39:51.210
In the end, the Administrator himself chose
to let himself perish too, perhaps in shame

02:39:51.210 --> 02:39:53.619
of what his organization had become.

02:39:53.619 --> 02:39:55.529
Or did he?

02:39:55.529 --> 02:40:01.640
Because someone seems to have been accessing
the Hellenstic AIC and the SCP-001 file using

02:40:01.640 --> 02:40:04.250
his login since this incident.

02:40:04.250 --> 02:40:09.180
Maybe the hand of death doesn’t reach quite
as far as we were led to believe.

02:40:09.180 --> 02:40:15.060
And that’s where the tale of SCP-001 ends;
a story of the Foundation’s greed in their

02:40:15.060 --> 02:40:17.549
pursuit of eternal life.

02:40:17.549 --> 02:40:22.310
We mustn’t forget that death isn’t something
to be afraid of, after all, it gives our lives

02:40:22.310 --> 02:40:24.749
meaning knowing that they’ll one day end.

02:40:24.749 --> 02:40:30.289
But when you look at the kind of monsters
we can become in the pursuit of eternal life,

02:40:30.289 --> 02:40:31.289
well…

02:40:31.289 --> 02:40:36.249
In the words of another wise old man, “Sometimes,
dead is better.”

02:40:36.249 --> 02:40:38.600
Does the Black Moon Howl?

02:40:38.600 --> 02:40:40.790
No. Not yet.

02:40:40.790 --> 02:40:46.729
See the boy. He was born in a time before
names; there weren’t enough humans around

02:40:46.729 --> 02:40:53.129
to need them back then. He was one of a handful
occupying a coastal village, using a tongue

02:40:53.129 --> 02:41:00.239
long since dead. They eked out a simple life
- hunting, gathering, fishing. The only thing

02:41:00.239 --> 02:41:07.069
on most of their minds was surviving to see
the next sunrise. Yes, a simple life, free

02:41:07.069 --> 02:41:08.350
of complications.

02:41:08.350 --> 02:41:10.869
Until The Hermit appeared.

02:41:10.869 --> 02:41:17.390
The Boy would remember this man for an eternity.
Haggard and thin; skin weathered by time and

02:41:17.390 --> 02:41:23.609
pain. A man that, emaciated, walking with
a long, gnarled cane that honestly looked

02:41:23.609 --> 02:41:29.749
healthier than he did, shouldn’t be alive.
Even the Boy, who had scarcely seen beyond

02:41:29.749 --> 02:41:36.779
the bounds of his village, knew that the Hermit
was unnatural. An aberration. An anomaly.

02:41:36.779 --> 02:41:42.671
He walked into the center of the village,
sat down on a large stone, and waited. Nobody

02:41:42.671 --> 02:41:47.129
dared ask his business, nor what the Hermit
waited for.

02:41:47.129 --> 02:41:51.680
Then, a few days later, the Black Moon howled.

02:41:51.680 --> 02:41:56.200
The Boy saw the village’s youngest hunter
freeze one evening while out on a walk. Not

02:41:56.200 --> 02:42:03.819
simply stand still, but freeze. Then, for
an instant, he became solid black. A coal

02:42:03.819 --> 02:42:10.450
statue. And as soon as he’d changed, he
was gone. Obliterated. Not a trace of him

02:42:10.450 --> 02:42:11.450
remained.

02:42:11.450 --> 02:42:16.779
Such is the power of the Black Moon. It can
make any conscious being disappear in an instant.

02:42:16.779 --> 02:42:23.339
Turned black, then wiped from our plane of
existence, never to be seen again. Its choice

02:42:23.339 --> 02:42:28.699
of victim seemed, at each instance, to be
utterly random, but it would come for all

02:42:28.699 --> 02:42:35.420
who lived eventually. This is known to some
as the howling of the Black Moon.

02:42:35.420 --> 02:42:40.880
Later that same night, the Boy found himself
talking to the Hermit, who asked with small,

02:42:40.880 --> 02:42:47.220
frantic eyes what he had seen. When the Boy
told him, he let out a deep, rattling sigh.

02:42:47.220 --> 02:42:52.569
The Boy, curious, asked him if he knew about
the nightmare he’d just witnessed. The Hermit

02:42:52.569 --> 02:42:57.789
looked up. He’d been the first one, in the
Hermit’s millennia of pursuit, that had

02:42:57.789 --> 02:43:03.740
ever asked. In that moment, he knew he had
found his successor in the hunt for the Death

02:43:03.740 --> 02:43:05.180
of Ages.

02:43:05.180 --> 02:43:11.760
The Hermit told the Boy it went by many names.
The Great Finale, the Pale King, but most

02:43:11.760 --> 02:43:18.169
common of all was the Black Moon. The entity
existed beyond the veil of our reality, a

02:43:18.169 --> 02:43:24.220
creature of pure energy, though nobody could
really be sure of its true nature. The Hermit

02:43:24.220 --> 02:43:29.839
had been tracking it, learning about it, and
trying to destroy it for thousands of years.

02:43:29.839 --> 02:43:36.090
And yet, it only took him four pathetic minutes
to tell the Boy everything he knew.

02:43:36.090 --> 02:43:40.909
The Boy, knowing still that something about
the Hermit was unnatural, asked how he came

02:43:40.909 --> 02:43:48.049
to be in this position. The Hermit told the
boy he was the Counterbalance, a kind of chosen

02:43:48.049 --> 02:43:53.470
one, destined to face and perhaps even defeat
the Black Moon someday. The Counterbalance

02:43:53.470 --> 02:43:59.209
receives a number of truly extraordinary gifts
for inheriting the responsibility: Eternal

02:43:59.209 --> 02:44:03.510
life, eternal youth, near physical immortality.

02:44:03.510 --> 02:44:09.239
But they will be haunted by their purpose,
doomed to watch everyone they love die around

02:44:09.239 --> 02:44:16.430
them, as they continue to hunt their only
true equal and opposite, the Black Moon itself.

02:44:16.430 --> 02:44:21.879
The Hermit, in his own eyes, had failed at
his duty. He had grown weary, and now, he

02:44:21.879 --> 02:44:27.790
needed to pass the duty of Counterbalance
onto another. That other would be the Boy.

02:44:27.790 --> 02:44:32.339
He felt a sudden and profound change, along
with the knowledge that nothing would ever

02:44:32.339 --> 02:44:40.060
be the same again. He was no longer just the
Boy. Now, he was the Counterbalance.

02:44:40.060 --> 02:44:44.529
He watched the Hermit give him a slight nod
out of respect, and then crumble into dust

02:44:44.529 --> 02:44:51.630
before his eyes. The Boy, the Counterbalance,
looked up at the sky and saw the stars twinkling.

02:44:51.630 --> 02:44:57.720
So bright, so beautiful. Little did he know,
his battle with the Black Moon would outlast

02:44:57.720 --> 02:44:59.999
every single one of them.

02:44:59.999 --> 02:45:04.029
Does the Black Moon howl? Not without blood.

02:45:04.029 --> 02:45:10.359
The Boy grew into a man, as his village aged
and then died around him. Decades passed,

02:45:10.359 --> 02:45:16.249
then centuries, then millennia. Tens of thousands
of years, watching humanity develop and grow

02:45:16.249 --> 02:45:20.880
around him as he continued his pursuit of
that one elusive foe.

02:45:20.880 --> 02:45:25.829
As science and diagnostic technology gained
ground, absorbing and then evolving beyond

02:45:25.829 --> 02:45:30.700
all the old superstitions, the Counterbalance
gained a better understanding of the Black

02:45:30.700 --> 02:45:37.669
Moon - though even then, it still remained
essentially a stranger. The entity was entropic,

02:45:37.669 --> 02:45:43.760
a being of pure randomness and chaos without
consistent form. It didn’t exist in our

02:45:43.760 --> 02:45:49.719
universe, but it could exercise its influence
here with so-called “Obliteration Events”

02:45:49.719 --> 02:45:53.640
- much like the horrible fate that befell
the young hunter from the village.

02:45:53.640 --> 02:45:57.859
But that was only the proverbial tip of the
iceberg.

02:45:57.859 --> 02:46:04.310
The Counterbalance tracked and noted obliteration
events. They were exceedingly rare, at first.

02:46:04.310 --> 02:46:09.100
Something that occurred once every thousand
years or so, like a terrible curse. But he

02:46:09.100 --> 02:46:14.789
couldn’t help but notice a concerning trend
emerging. It started happening once a century...then

02:46:14.789 --> 02:46:20.069
once a decade. He could feel the terrible
future stretching out in front of him. How,

02:46:20.069 --> 02:46:24.979
over their shared eternity, the Black Moon
would gain more and more ground.

02:46:24.979 --> 02:46:31.689
Would there come a day where it took someone
once a year? One a month? A week, a day, an

02:46:31.689 --> 02:46:38.199
hour, a minute, a second? It’d spell the
end of all conscious life. A total victory

02:46:38.199 --> 02:46:45.619
for the Black Moon, the End of the Universe,
the Death of Ages. A complete existential

02:46:45.619 --> 02:46:47.350
obliteration.

02:46:47.350 --> 02:46:51.770
He was swept up in a sobering realization:
He couldn’t win this fight alone.

02:46:51.770 --> 02:46:56.850
However, while his hunt for the Black Moon
had been largely fruitless, the Counterbalance

02:46:56.850 --> 02:47:03.300
had discovered many other things along the
way, Strange creatures, objects with extraordinary

02:47:03.300 --> 02:47:08.859
powers, and events that couldn’t be explained
with rational science. Perhaps something among

02:47:08.859 --> 02:47:16.659
these oddities, these anomalies, would hold
the key to defeating his timeless enemy. And

02:47:16.659 --> 02:47:21.749
it hadn’t just been these objects, entities,
and events, he’d also discovered some truly

02:47:21.749 --> 02:47:27.460
exceptional people on his travels. Minds and
skills that rivaled even his own, despite

02:47:27.460 --> 02:47:28.529
his age.

02:47:28.529 --> 02:47:31.720
Perhaps they would be the ones to help him
win.

02:47:31.720 --> 02:47:36.319
With the thirteen most brilliant and trusted
people the Counterbalance ever met, he decided

02:47:36.319 --> 02:47:42.430
to form a Council. And from this Council,
they forged and directed an organization dedicated

02:47:42.430 --> 02:47:47.949
to understanding and counteracting the strange
in all its forms, with the secret hope that

02:47:47.949 --> 02:47:53.140
their search into darkness would yield the
answer to the Black Moon’s downfall.

02:47:53.140 --> 02:47:59.419
He called it the SCP Foundation. They would
Secure the anomalous, Contain it, and Protect

02:47:59.419 --> 02:48:05.399
all of humanity from its influence. The Counterbalance
also took on a new title, befitting of his

02:48:05.399 --> 02:48:11.789
new role: The Administrator. And even the
Black Moon itself was given a moniker, in

02:48:11.789 --> 02:48:15.919
hopes of robbing it of some of its frightening
power.

02:48:15.919 --> 02:48:18.049
SCP-001.

02:48:18.049 --> 02:48:22.020
Does the Black Moon howl? Only at the blind.

02:48:22.020 --> 02:48:28.239
The year was now 1987. The SCP Foundation
had been operating for over a century, and

02:48:28.239 --> 02:48:32.869
thanks to their secret possession of anomalous
wisdom and technology, their own advancement

02:48:32.869 --> 02:48:37.370
was thousands of years ahead of the rest of
humanity. While there still wasn’t a silver

02:48:37.370 --> 02:48:42.390
bullet solution to the Black Moon, and its
deadly howls were becoming all the more frequent

02:48:42.390 --> 02:48:47.909
as the decades went on, the Foundation did
have some irons in the fire to combat it.

02:48:47.909 --> 02:48:52.549
Their ability to gather intel on both the
entity itself and its obliteration events

02:48:52.549 --> 02:48:58.119
had improved considerably, thanks to their
new global information network. Their top

02:48:58.119 --> 02:49:03.710
minds were also working on a highly classified
device known as the Singular Conceptual Bunker,

02:49:03.710 --> 02:49:09.239
which may one day come in handy for combating
the extra-dimensional entity directly. But

02:49:09.239 --> 02:49:14.159
the most valuable piece of information they
ever gathered about the Black Moon was this:

02:49:14.159 --> 02:49:20.549
It couldn’t howl when it was being watched.
The very act of engaged observation defanged

02:49:20.549 --> 02:49:21.549
it.

02:49:21.549 --> 02:49:25.989
The problem is, how can you observe something
that doesn’t technically exist inside your

02:49:25.989 --> 02:49:32.350
own reality? In order to pull this off, the
Foundation would need to get extremely creative.

02:49:32.350 --> 02:49:37.229
Thankfully, creative solutions to strange
problems are the Foundation’s specialty.

02:49:37.229 --> 02:49:44.050
Flash forward to 1993. Enter Dr. Moto, a brilliant
young scientist and conceptual engineer working

02:49:44.050 --> 02:49:49.359
for the SCP Foundation. With The Administrator’s
consultation, he started the KEY Project,

02:49:49.359 --> 02:49:55.609
an arm of the wider Project Oromasdes - the
umbrella initiative for using modified anomalous

02:49:55.609 --> 02:49:58.560
objects in the battle against the Black Moon.

02:49:58.560 --> 02:50:03.169
The goal of the KEY Project was relatively
simple: If people couldn’t observe the Black

02:50:03.169 --> 02:50:08.840
Moon directly, then the Foundation could make
proxies of the Black Moon that could be observed,

02:50:08.840 --> 02:50:14.159
almost like a kind of voodoo doll. These new
anomalies would only need to satisfy three

02:50:14.159 --> 02:50:19.839
criteria: The inability to operate when being
observed, a hostility to conscious life, and

02:50:19.839 --> 02:50:24.660
the ability to end conscious life of their
own volition when not being observed. Through

02:50:24.660 --> 02:50:29.850
conceptual engineering, a link theoretically
could be forged between these objects and

02:50:29.850 --> 02:50:34.939
the Black Moon, allowing observation of them
to stop the obliteration events.

02:50:34.939 --> 02:50:39.649
However, despite being a good idea in theory,
Dr. Moto’s efforts were marred with errors

02:50:39.649 --> 02:50:44.560
and tragedies. One object wasn’t deadly
enough, simply appearing behind people in

02:50:44.560 --> 02:50:48.850
a threatening pose when they weren’t looking.
Another one killed purely through collateral

02:50:48.850 --> 02:50:53.399
damage - a giant sculpture of a human head
that immediately attempted escape by barging

02:50:53.399 --> 02:50:59.600
through Site-01 - the center for Anti-Black
Moon operations - and killing nineteen people

02:50:59.600 --> 02:51:05.869
in the process. Another one of Moto’s objects,
a huge black sphere, simply immediately exploded,

02:51:05.869 --> 02:51:07.470
killing twelve people.

02:51:07.470 --> 02:51:12.310
And in the most horrific misstep of all, one
of Moto’s objects caused a mass death event

02:51:12.310 --> 02:51:19.399
in a nearby hotel, where 142 people were spontaneously
incinerated when the object - a series of

02:51:19.399 --> 02:51:25.899
interlocking stalactites and stalagmites - was
left unobserved for 0.2 seconds. Almost all

02:51:25.899 --> 02:51:30.379
of Moto’s objects were terminated in the
aftermath, either being too useless or too

02:51:30.379 --> 02:51:36.090
dangerous to keep around. The young scientist
felt a deep shame, but forged on.

02:51:36.090 --> 02:51:42.239
He made one truly brilliant creation that
satisfied all the criteria: A sculpture, incapable

02:51:42.239 --> 02:51:46.770
of moving while being watched, but would snap
the neck of the nearest conscious entity if

02:51:46.770 --> 02:51:51.970
left unobserved for even a fraction of a second.
Its relatively minimal killing left it easy

02:51:51.970 --> 02:51:56.979
to contain without causing mass deaths, and
despite all the other deaths that had sadly

02:51:56.979 --> 02:52:01.812
occurred during the KEY Project, Dr. Moto
believed that the lives saved in the long

02:52:01.812 --> 02:52:06.409
run by stopping the Black Moon’s howls would
justify the sacrifice.

02:52:06.409 --> 02:52:11.100
The problem is...the KEY Project didn’t
stop anything.

02:52:11.100 --> 02:52:15.789
Not long after this, there was the first recorded
double obliteration event in Rome, where a

02:52:15.789 --> 02:52:20.750
young tourist couple had both been obliterated
simultaneously. All the deaths in the KEY

02:52:20.750 --> 02:52:26.399
Project had been for nothing. The Black Moon
was only getting more powerful.

02:52:26.399 --> 02:52:31.129
The shame and the guilt was too much for Dr.
Moto. He left a note in his office, reading,

02:52:31.129 --> 02:52:35.839
“We've been looking at nothing. I'm sorry,
Administrator. I've failed you, sir.”

02:52:35.839 --> 02:52:41.880
Moto’s corpse was later found in the sculpture’s
temporary containment chamber, his neck snapped.

02:52:41.880 --> 02:52:46.869
The KEY Project was, in summary, shut down
and its one surviving creation transported

02:52:46.869 --> 02:52:55.989
to Site-19 in late 1993, where it was designated
as SCP-173. Another painful failure for the

02:52:55.989 --> 02:52:59.289
Administrator. Back to the drawing board once
more.

02:52:59.289 --> 02:53:03.479
Does the Black Moon howl? Not while stars
shine.

02:53:03.479 --> 02:53:08.100
millennia stretched on. Almost everyone died,
except The Administrator, thanks to his gift

02:53:08.100 --> 02:53:14.279
- or perhaps curse - as the Counterbalance
to the Black Moon. Science marched on, the

02:53:14.279 --> 02:53:21.609
SCP Foundation marched on, but all this progress,
all this power, was nothing against the incomprehensible

02:53:21.609 --> 02:53:28.359
influence of SCP-001. The Black Moon was howling
more frequently than ever, all the way up

02:53:28.359 --> 02:53:34.109
to the year 3156, when the Foundation launched
the SEEK Project under the support of Project

02:53:34.109 --> 02:53:35.600
Oromasdes.

02:53:35.600 --> 02:53:40.020
As more and more people were wiped out in
frequent obliteration events, the Administrator

02:53:40.020 --> 02:53:44.970
became painfully aware that perhaps the answers
to the Black Moon problem wouldn’t be found

02:53:44.970 --> 02:53:50.080
on earth. Using state of the art technology,
with a little help from the anomalous, the

02:53:50.080 --> 02:53:54.850
SCP Foundation began work on an autonomous
space-faring vessel that could search the

02:53:54.850 --> 02:54:02.189
stars for the key to the Black Moon’s destruction.
It was an awe-inspiring creation, a huge craft

02:54:02.189 --> 02:54:07.770
powered by artificial intelligence, with a
universal translator, cryogenic units, and

02:54:07.770 --> 02:54:12.010
hundreds of autonomous drones to perform more
targeted searches.

02:54:12.010 --> 02:54:16.760
SEEK was waved off into the unforgiving depths
of space. The Administrator could only hope

02:54:16.760 --> 02:54:19.810
that it would come back with worthwhile answers.

02:54:19.810 --> 02:54:24.310
The first of the three notable planets SEEK
arrived on was one theoretically capable of

02:54:24.310 --> 02:54:30.430
supporting human life, except for its brutal
and constant blizzards and snowstorms. When

02:54:30.430 --> 02:54:35.310
SEEK’s drones were deployed, they did discover
signs of civilization, based around sentient

02:54:35.310 --> 02:54:40.859
spherical creatures, but no signs of actual
life remained. Records and statues found across

02:54:40.859 --> 02:54:44.999
the planet seemed to indicate that the Black
Moon was responsible for the destruction of

02:54:44.999 --> 02:54:49.939
the planet’s civilization, causing so many
obliteration events that the remaining survivors

02:54:49.939 --> 02:54:56.060
went mad from the fear and stress, leading
to mass death in the ensuing chaos.

02:54:56.060 --> 02:55:01.449
The next planet was discovered centuries later,
in the year 3499. While this planet could

02:55:01.449 --> 02:55:06.060
also theoretically support human life, it
suffered from frequent volcanic eruptions

02:55:06.060 --> 02:55:10.789
that rendered much of its surface a flaming
mess. However, there were still the dormant

02:55:10.789 --> 02:55:16.439
ruins of a once advanced civilization of conscious
beings. Much like the prior planet, they’d

02:55:16.439 --> 02:55:21.949
been driven extinct by Black Moon obliteration
events a century before the SEEK even arrived.

02:55:21.949 --> 02:55:27.049
Unlike the last planet, however, it seems
that they accepted their fate, and went gently

02:55:27.049 --> 02:55:32.080
into the night. The planet was now overrun
by billions of armored, bat-like creatures

02:55:32.080 --> 02:55:37.649
that operated on pure instinct, and thus,
were not considered conscious enough to be

02:55:37.649 --> 02:55:38.649
obliterated.

02:55:38.649 --> 02:55:44.779
The final planet was reached in 3764, and
was the most fruitful of the three discoveries.

02:55:44.779 --> 02:55:49.979
This planet was hyper-advanced, fully urbanized
and covered in sprawling megacities, with

02:55:49.979 --> 02:55:54.489
records and technology over a thousand years
ahead of Earth. Before the Black Moon killed

02:55:54.489 --> 02:55:59.540
almost all of them, they were a species of
humanoid telepathic fungi, and had developed

02:55:59.540 --> 02:56:03.859
an awareness of the Black Moon’s existence
that was on par with that of humanity’s.

02:56:03.859 --> 02:56:09.720
They even had their own equivalent of the
SCP Foundation actively working on countermeasures.

02:56:09.720 --> 02:56:15.450
And most amazingly of all, SEEK found one
surviving member of the species on the planet,

02:56:15.450 --> 02:56:19.949
cryogenically frozen. The craft was immediately
instructed to collect the survivor and return

02:56:19.949 --> 02:56:24.370
home for interrogation. The Administrator
was preparing for what could have been the

02:56:24.370 --> 02:56:30.350
most important conversation since he met the
Hermit, all those thousands of years ago.

02:56:30.350 --> 02:56:34.159
Does the Black Moon howl? Only when waning.

02:56:34.159 --> 02:56:38.989
When the surviving creature, codenamed SAGE,
was returned to Earth, The Administrator was

02:56:38.989 --> 02:56:44.479
eager to finally speak with it. Like the rest
of its now-extinct species, SAGE spoke through

02:56:44.479 --> 02:56:49.279
powerful telepathic mindwaves, which only
The Administrator - thanks to his Counterbalance

02:56:49.279 --> 02:56:53.640
abilities - was able to receive at close range
without being harmed.

02:56:53.640 --> 02:56:57.979
Incidentally, it wasn’t long until the very
fact of the Administrator’s nature as a

02:56:57.979 --> 02:57:04.140
Counterbalance came up in the mental conversation.
SAGE could tell, just by being in his presence.

02:57:04.140 --> 02:57:09.199
They discovered a number of vital truths over
their brief time communicating: That SAGE’s

02:57:09.199 --> 02:57:13.569
survival had been pure luck, for starters.
The Black Moon is still very much capable

02:57:13.569 --> 02:57:19.170
of obliterating conscious beings in an unconscious
state. The Administrator also learned that

02:57:19.170 --> 02:57:24.619
he was merely the latest in an extremely long
line of Counterbalances across time, space,

02:57:24.619 --> 02:57:30.670
and species, though everyone but him had waived
the duty, passed it on.

02:57:30.670 --> 02:57:37.640
SAGE had one question to ask the Administrator
in turn, “What is SCB?” The Singular Conceptual

02:57:37.640 --> 02:57:42.589
Bunker, being worked on and perfected for
thousands of years by now, by the Foundation’s

02:57:42.589 --> 02:57:45.720
top scientists and conceptual engineers.

02:57:45.720 --> 02:57:52.669
The Administrator replied, “Victory. But
it will take a very, very long time.” Specifically,

02:57:52.669 --> 02:57:58.370
so long that he would see the stars go out
around him, one by one. Shocked, SAGE asked

02:57:58.370 --> 02:58:04.020
him what good victory would do him then. Rather
than say it aloud, he replied with a thought.

02:58:04.020 --> 02:58:09.390
SAGE paused, and said, “I see. How blasphemous
of you. Hopefully it works.”

02:58:09.390 --> 02:58:13.819
After this, the Administrator proceeded to
the Singular Conceptual Bunker and entered

02:58:13.819 --> 02:58:19.209
it, leaving instructions for the Foundation
to be run by a newly formed O5 Council in

02:58:19.209 --> 02:58:25.899
his indefinite absence. Thousands of years
later, in the year 5011, SAGE spoke one more

02:58:25.899 --> 02:58:32.569
time, repeating the words, “Hopefully, hopefully”
before turning solid black, and disappearing.

02:58:32.569 --> 02:58:38.339
The Black Moon had claimed one more victim,
but billions more had gone in the interim.

02:58:38.339 --> 02:58:43.829
The Administrator had no more answers to give.
At least, no more answers that anyone but

02:58:43.829 --> 02:58:49.710
him would understand. He was inside the Singular
Conceptual Bunker now, loaded into a device

02:58:49.710 --> 02:58:56.060
known as TOME - an experimental memorial module,
meant to pick up and record all the last messages

02:58:56.060 --> 02:59:02.419
of every dying civilization across the universe,
when the time finally came. All he could do

02:59:02.419 --> 02:59:06.830
was wait. And wait was exactly what we did.

02:59:06.830 --> 02:59:08.430
Does the Black Moon howl?

02:59:08.430 --> 02:59:11.409
Yes. Yes it does.

02:59:11.409 --> 02:59:17.340
Years pass. Too many to count. It’s a time
after names now, and TOME sits in the very

02:59:17.340 --> 02:59:22.129
center, drinking in the end of the universe.
The last of all the human colonies across

02:59:22.129 --> 02:59:29.089
the universe were obliterated by the Black
Moon back in the year 7329, so, so, so long

02:59:29.089 --> 02:59:36.470
ago, but some of the final messages of fear,
panic, and distress still echoed around the

02:59:36.470 --> 02:59:37.470
Administrator’s mind.

02:59:37.470 --> 02:59:43.169
"Hello, is there anyone here? We — we require
assistance! There's … it's … it's taking

02:59:43.169 --> 02:59:49.590
people every day! We need help! There's barely
anyone left! We need help! Hello? Hello?!"

02:59:49.590 --> 02:59:54.840
"Cabal 09:43! We have abandoned the false
flesh! We have abandoned the false flesh!

02:59:54.840 --> 03:00:02.010
The shepherds crook broken 'neath my knee!
Cabal 09:43! Cabal 09:43! Forgive us! Forgive

03:00:02.010 --> 03:00:03.010
us!"

03:00:03.010 --> 03:00:08.219
"We're going to leave this on. It's so dark
outside now. It's blotting out the sun. It's

03:00:08.219 --> 03:00:09.539
… I have to go now."

03:00:09.539 --> 03:00:11.319
"RESPOND•FIRST•CONVENIENCE EMERGENCY•SITUATION•DEVELOPING
REQUIRE•ADDITIONAL•RESOURCES."

03:00:11.319 --> 03:00:20.859
"My fault. Your fault. Our fault. My fault.
Your fault. Our fault. My fault. Your fault.

03:00:20.859 --> 03:00:26.999
Our fault. Rip out my brain now. Rip out my
brain now!"

03:00:26.999 --> 03:00:34.310
And a small child, the last on Earth, simply
asking, “Hello?” into an indifferent microphone.

03:00:34.310 --> 03:00:40.060
But the Administrator had to wait, as the
Singular Conceptual Bunker became the Solitary

03:00:40.060 --> 03:00:45.609
Conceptual Bunker. He was the last conscious
being in the universe, and still, he needed

03:00:45.609 --> 03:00:51.919
to wait, as the stars went dark outside. Only
when there was nothing outside but black was

03:00:51.919 --> 03:00:56.510
it finally time for the Counterbalance’s
long game to pay off.

03:00:56.510 --> 03:01:01.720
There was nothing left of our universe. The
only thing here was the SCB, and the Black

03:01:01.720 --> 03:01:07.560
Moon itself. With everything else gone, the
Black Moon only had one conscious being left

03:01:07.560 --> 03:01:13.670
to obliterate. It opened the door to the Solitary
Conceptual Bunker, and stepped inside.

03:01:13.670 --> 03:01:20.199
This...this doesn’t make sense. How can
the Black Moon, an entity beyond our dimension,

03:01:20.199 --> 03:01:26.919
beyond physical form, take a step? Good question.
The same question, incidentally, that was

03:01:26.919 --> 03:01:31.220
going through the Black Moon’s mind as it
entered the bunker. It didn’t look at all

03:01:31.220 --> 03:01:37.749
how the entity expected: It was like a bar,
a counter with rows of bottles behind it,

03:01:37.749 --> 03:01:43.129
a jukebox playing in the corner. A man stood
behind the bar, cleaning glasses.

03:01:43.129 --> 03:01:46.649
The Counterbalance. The Administrator.

03:01:46.649 --> 03:01:52.449
He said, "Well, there you are! Certainly took
your time. Can I pour you a little something?"

03:01:52.449 --> 03:01:58.329
This only served to increase the Black Moon’s
confusion. It had form here, dark smoke compressed

03:01:58.329 --> 03:02:06.210
into a vaguely humanoid shape. It could speak?
It could think? None of this made any sense.

03:02:06.210 --> 03:02:10.680
The being that’d just wiped out all conscious
life and seen the very death of the universe

03:02:10.680 --> 03:02:14.049
was truly and utterly confused.

03:02:14.049 --> 03:02:18.749
The Administrator just seemed to be enjoying
himself, preparing for a confrontation hundreds

03:02:18.749 --> 03:02:24.529
of billions of years in the making. The Singular
Conceptual Bunker - or perhaps, the Singular

03:02:24.529 --> 03:02:31.350
Containment Bunker - was a truly ingenious
creation. A place of pure ideas, where everything

03:02:31.350 --> 03:02:38.850
inside was on the same level. Here, there
were no immortals. No Gods. Just ideas, on

03:02:38.850 --> 03:02:44.939
the same level playing field. And it was time
for the Black Moon’s idea to come to an

03:02:44.939 --> 03:02:45.939
end.

03:02:45.939 --> 03:02:49.839
It was a trap, and the entire universe was
the bait.

03:02:49.839 --> 03:02:53.630
Without warning, the Administrator pulled
up a shotgun from underneath the table, and

03:02:53.630 --> 03:02:56.649
unleashed both barrels into the Black Moon’s
chest.

03:02:56.649 --> 03:03:00.779
The creature took the hit and fought back,
dragging the Administrator to the ground,

03:03:00.779 --> 03:03:05.659
beating him, strangling him. He could feel
the light fading under the monster’s relentless

03:03:05.659 --> 03:03:10.939
assault, until he managed to get his desperate
hands on a glass ashtray. He beat the monster

03:03:10.939 --> 03:03:15.359
over the head with it until its grip loosened,
and he was able to slide out.

03:03:15.359 --> 03:03:20.149
There, the killer of the universe was on the
ground before him. He grabbed the monster,

03:03:20.149 --> 03:03:25.410
held it in place, and beat it to death. He
was gravely injured by the battle, but The

03:03:25.410 --> 03:03:32.089
Black Moon was no more. Here, in the Singular
Conceptual Bunker, he had won.

03:03:32.089 --> 03:03:36.380
The Administrator, no longer the counterbalance
in the absence of the Black Moon, hobbled

03:03:36.380 --> 03:03:42.249
over to the jukebox, producing a single, beautiful
coin from his pocket. He pushed the coin into

03:03:42.249 --> 03:03:45.410
the slot, wheezed a pained breath, and said:

03:03:45.410 --> 03:03:53.649
“The thing is … this place is only information.
T-There's nothing else out there. Not even

03:03:53.649 --> 03:03:59.879
matter. The universe closed its doors a long
time ago. But this place can go from information

03:03:59.879 --> 03:04:06.020
back to matter with just the press of a button.
L-Let's see what happens when we introduce

03:04:06.020 --> 03:04:08.209
something to nothing…”

03:04:08.209 --> 03:04:13.169
For a second, it looks as though he might
fall, but he doesn’t. Instead, he slams

03:04:13.169 --> 03:04:19.079
the button on the jukebox and, with a relieved
laugh, says, “Let there be light.”

03:04:19.079 --> 03:04:21.470
And there was light.

03:04:21.470 --> 03:04:22.669
Hour one.

03:04:22.669 --> 03:04:29.369
There is only one news story, on every website,
newspaper, and TV screen.

03:04:29.369 --> 03:04:33.369
The flowers are blooming everywhere, all across
the globe.

03:04:33.369 --> 03:04:36.020
Every country, every landmass.

03:04:36.020 --> 03:04:40.949
The bitter cold of the Antarctic gives way
to a glowing rainbow of petals.

03:04:40.949 --> 03:04:46.209
The Sahara Desert and Death Valley become
beacons of thriving technicolor plantlife.

03:04:46.209 --> 03:04:50.910
The highest mountains, the lowest valleys,
the darkest caves.

03:04:50.910 --> 03:04:56.169
The flowers even burst free from the concrete
of cities, as if reminding us that really,

03:04:56.169 --> 03:05:00.649
it was never our world, we were only borrowing
it.

03:05:00.649 --> 03:05:03.899
And today, our lease is up.

03:05:03.899 --> 03:05:06.629
This is SCP-001.

03:05:06.629 --> 03:05:09.409
Object Class: Unnecessary.

03:05:09.409 --> 03:05:15.470
It was foretold by tales from other dimensions,
a distant future coming down the tracks towards

03:05:15.470 --> 03:05:16.470
us.

03:05:16.470 --> 03:05:19.390
And today, the train has reached the station.

03:05:19.390 --> 03:05:23.590
Nobody’s reporting on how the economy or
the stock market is doing today.

03:05:23.590 --> 03:05:24.829
No point.

03:05:24.829 --> 03:05:28.419
Celebrity scandals have faded away into nothingness.

03:05:28.419 --> 03:05:33.100
Greedy businessmen, lying politicians, brutal
tyrants.

03:05:33.100 --> 03:05:35.699
None of them are making the headlines today.

03:05:35.699 --> 03:05:38.119
The very last headlines.

03:05:38.119 --> 03:05:40.319
The World’s Gone Beautiful.

03:05:40.319 --> 03:05:45.470
And what a shame it takes the end of it all
to make us realize what really matters to

03:05:45.470 --> 03:05:46.470
us.

03:05:46.470 --> 03:05:50.239
That’s right: You’re looking at the end
of the world.

03:05:50.239 --> 03:05:51.470
But it’s okay.

03:05:51.470 --> 03:05:52.589
Don’t panic.

03:05:52.589 --> 03:05:55.279
Take a deep breath, in and out.

03:05:55.279 --> 03:05:59.790
It was bound to happen eventually, so no point
worrying now.

03:05:59.790 --> 03:06:04.229
Even the Foundation knows that this just isn’t
something they can stop.

03:06:04.229 --> 03:06:08.909
So instead of asking things like, “How can
we prevent this?” or “Do we have any final

03:06:08.909 --> 03:06:10.600
tricks up our sleeve?”

03:06:10.600 --> 03:06:15.959
let’s ask a different question entirely:
“What would you do if you knew that you

03:06:15.959 --> 03:06:20.029
only had 24 hours until all life on earth
ends?”

03:06:20.029 --> 03:06:21.770
Think hard.

03:06:21.770 --> 03:06:27.180
After all, even if you never live to see the
flowers bloom, a final day will still come

03:06:27.180 --> 03:06:30.459
for you, just as it does for us all.

03:06:30.459 --> 03:06:31.760
Hour six.

03:06:31.760 --> 03:06:36.289
A D-Class sits alone in his cell when he sees
the flowers growing out of the ground.

03:06:36.289 --> 03:06:40.990
Normally, he’d assume this meant he was
in some kind of Foundation experiment.

03:06:40.990 --> 03:06:42.619
But not today.

03:06:42.619 --> 03:06:46.129
Everyone on earth has an innate sense that
the time is now.

03:06:46.129 --> 03:06:50.249
A kind of gallows calm spreads out over everyone
and everything.

03:06:50.249 --> 03:06:53.399
It’s over, and that’s okay.

03:06:53.399 --> 03:06:56.149
We all knew it was going to happen eventually,
right?

03:06:56.149 --> 03:06:58.930
He sighs and gives a slight smile.

03:06:58.930 --> 03:07:00.430
Those flowers sure are beautiful.

03:07:00.430 --> 03:07:03.939
That’s when he hears footsteps outside his
cell, approaching.

03:07:03.939 --> 03:07:07.010
A key slides into his cell door, and it opens.

03:07:07.010 --> 03:07:12.319
There stands Dr. Gears, holding a bottle of
wine and two glasses.

03:07:12.319 --> 03:07:16.739
Anyone who knows him might think he’s been
replaced by some kind of shapeshifting anomaly

03:07:16.739 --> 03:07:20.180
or had his mind taken over by a powerful cognitohazard.

03:07:20.180 --> 03:07:21.409
But no.

03:07:21.409 --> 03:07:22.649
It’s him.

03:07:22.649 --> 03:07:25.319
The famously cold Dr. Charles Ogden Gears.

03:07:25.319 --> 03:07:27.379
Dr. Gears says, “Come on.

03:07:27.379 --> 03:07:29.560
It’s a lovely day out there.

03:07:29.560 --> 03:07:32.899
It’d be a terrible waste to spend the whole
thing cooped up in here.”

03:07:32.899 --> 03:07:35.970
It’d feel like a trick, on any day but this.

03:07:35.970 --> 03:07:38.579
The D-Class nods and follows the doctor out.

03:07:38.579 --> 03:07:43.480
The normally oh-so-stoic Foundation senior
researcher pours himself and the D-Class each

03:07:43.480 --> 03:07:46.510
a glass of wine, and asks, “What’s your
name, by the way?

03:07:46.510 --> 03:07:48.279
I don’t think I ever checked.”

03:07:48.279 --> 03:07:50.829
The D-Class replies that his name is Harold.

03:07:50.829 --> 03:07:55.470
The two smile and chat as they exit the now
empty D-Class containment wing.

03:07:55.470 --> 03:07:57.350
Everyone else is outside already.

03:07:57.350 --> 03:08:02.859
Researchers, guards, administrative staff,
and D-Classes, all rubbing elbows, enjoying

03:08:02.859 --> 03:08:05.869
the beautiful sun on their last day together.

03:08:05.869 --> 03:08:11.049
Elsewhere on the site, a flock of SCP-514
is released, just as identical flocks are

03:08:11.049 --> 03:08:14.739
being released from every containment site
all over the world.

03:08:14.739 --> 03:08:17.959
They’ve prepared it all for this very day.

03:08:17.959 --> 03:08:23.930
SCP-514 is a special breed of homing pigeons
created by the Manna Charitable Foundation,

03:08:23.930 --> 03:08:27.909
which have the power to suppress aggression
for those within their field of anomalous

03:08:27.909 --> 03:08:28.909
influence.

03:08:28.909 --> 03:08:33.020
And now, millions of them are flying all over
the world.

03:08:33.020 --> 03:08:36.409
After all, there’s no point fighting on
a day like this.

03:08:36.409 --> 03:08:39.229
There is no future left to secure.

03:08:39.229 --> 03:08:43.479
People always told them there would forever
be hope until the flowers bloomed.

03:08:43.479 --> 03:08:47.760
No situation was ever truly over until the
world went beautiful.

03:08:47.760 --> 03:08:54.680
But in the absence of hope, there was something
even more inviting: Total, absolute calm.

03:08:54.680 --> 03:08:58.439
The Site-19 personnel sit together and watch
the flowers bloom.

03:08:58.439 --> 03:08:59.829
Hour Twelve.

03:08:59.829 --> 03:09:03.010
All militaries call a global ceasefire.

03:09:03.010 --> 03:09:07.909
Soldiers from opposing sides hug and shake
hands in flowery fields that once seemed choked

03:09:07.909 --> 03:09:09.649
by death and blood.

03:09:09.649 --> 03:09:13.310
Borders fade; bitter rivalries turn to dust.

03:09:13.310 --> 03:09:14.749
Korea unifies.

03:09:14.749 --> 03:09:16.909
All is quiet in the Middle East.

03:09:16.909 --> 03:09:21.739
Gangsters and drug cartels drop their weapons
and return home to their families and friends

03:09:21.739 --> 03:09:25.419
as flocks of SCP-514 fly above.

03:09:25.419 --> 03:09:29.250
What good is all the blood money in the world
on a day like this?

03:09:29.250 --> 03:09:34.079
Wardens walk cell to cell through all the
world’s prisons, granting people their freedom

03:09:34.079 --> 03:09:37.479
again, sometimes after lifetimes of not having
it.

03:09:37.479 --> 03:09:39.000
They taste the air again.

03:09:39.000 --> 03:09:41.020
Feel the sun on their face.

03:09:41.020 --> 03:09:45.579
They close their eyes, drink it in, and walk
among the flowers.

03:09:45.579 --> 03:09:47.270
Free men.

03:09:47.270 --> 03:09:51.649
Locations of Marshall, Carter, and Dark Ltd.
close their doors and shutter their windows

03:09:51.649 --> 03:09:52.649
worldwide.

03:09:52.649 --> 03:09:58.439
For the first time in as long as any of them
can remember, they turn their signs to “Closed.”

03:09:58.439 --> 03:10:00.470
They’ve earned a day off.

03:10:00.470 --> 03:10:01.470
Everyone has.

03:10:01.470 --> 03:10:04.859
The Chaos Insurgency rolls up their plans
and burns them.

03:10:04.859 --> 03:10:08.439
They drop their weapons and throw away their
tactical gear.

03:10:08.439 --> 03:10:13.850
As they do so, they can’t help but question
themselves: What was it all for, in the end?

03:10:13.850 --> 03:10:15.369
What was any of it for?

03:10:15.369 --> 03:10:17.930
All the fighting and bloodshed and death?

03:10:17.930 --> 03:10:21.739
We did it day after day, only to do it again
the next day.

03:10:21.739 --> 03:10:24.970
What silly reasons we killed and died for.

03:10:24.970 --> 03:10:27.109
What silly reasons indeed.

03:10:27.109 --> 03:10:31.640
The Global Occult Coalition dismisses its
staff, thanking them for their service and

03:10:31.640 --> 03:10:35.509
telling them to go spend their last hours
with the ones they love.

03:10:35.509 --> 03:10:40.909
Like the Foundation, they accept that this
is the one true, final end.

03:10:40.909 --> 03:10:47.629
No ritual to stop, no monster to fight, no
evil extra-dimensional entity to thwart.

03:10:47.629 --> 03:10:51.430
Just go outside and smell the flowers, while
you still can.

03:10:51.430 --> 03:10:53.300
The Serpent’s Hand are similar.

03:10:53.300 --> 03:10:57.670
They decide, after decades fighting a losing
battle, they’ll spend their last day in

03:10:57.670 --> 03:11:01.739
the Wanderer’s Library, reading some of
their favorite volumes.

03:11:01.739 --> 03:11:06.239
All these wonderful stories, now left for
other earths to read.

03:11:06.239 --> 03:11:10.689
Their own stories would be counted among them
in the end, and they take great comfort in

03:11:10.689 --> 03:11:11.689
that.

03:11:11.689 --> 03:11:15.949
In a sense, everyone will live forever in
the pages of the books in the Wanderer’s

03:11:15.949 --> 03:11:16.949
Library.

03:11:16.949 --> 03:11:20.930
Herman Fuller’s Circus of the Disquieting
releases all of its freaks and clowns from

03:11:20.930 --> 03:11:26.239
their twisted grasp, to go and live out whatever
small dreams and tiny pleasures they could

03:11:26.239 --> 03:11:28.460
find over their last hours.

03:11:28.460 --> 03:11:31.259
They have no Foundation to fear anymore.

03:11:31.259 --> 03:11:35.239
Nobody minds their strange appearances and
odd behaviors.

03:11:35.239 --> 03:11:38.779
Why would anyone waste such a beautiful day
judging others?

03:11:38.779 --> 03:11:42.589
On the last day on earth, there’s nothing
left to prove.

03:11:42.589 --> 03:11:47.449
Sarkicists drop their ancient, flesh-bound
tomes, and acolytes of the Broken God put

03:11:47.449 --> 03:11:49.419
down their gilded blades.

03:11:49.419 --> 03:11:56.069
On the slopes of Siberia, the jungles of Peru,
and the most isolated beaches of Mexico, twisted

03:11:56.069 --> 03:12:00.130
flesh finally touch living metal in the spirit
of husbandry.

03:12:00.130 --> 03:12:02.800
Their eternal war is at its end.

03:12:02.800 --> 03:12:07.439
In the face of the blooming world, they didn’t
seem so different after all.

03:12:07.439 --> 03:12:12.539
The agents of the Dr. Wondertainment corporation,
predictably, choose to spend their last hours

03:12:12.539 --> 03:12:15.220
sitting around and playing with toys together.

03:12:15.220 --> 03:12:17.339
Time well spent, if you ask us.

03:12:17.339 --> 03:12:23.529
In a highly secretive location, perhaps the
most heavily secured place in the entire world,

03:12:23.529 --> 03:12:28.649
the thirteen members of the legendary O5 Council
decide to just sit and talk.

03:12:28.649 --> 03:12:34.020
As anyone who knows anything about this secretive
cabal can tell you, the O5 Council has spent

03:12:34.020 --> 03:12:39.020
a considerable portion of their very, very
long lives trying to figure out ways to dodge

03:12:39.020 --> 03:12:40.529
and cheat death.

03:12:40.529 --> 03:12:45.949
But now, facing a death they can’t dodge,
the same calm washing over the rest of the

03:12:45.949 --> 03:12:47.899
world has finally reached them too.

03:12:47.899 --> 03:12:53.829
All they can really think this time is, “Well
played, Reaper, well played” as they chat

03:12:53.829 --> 03:12:59.299
about the kind of inane, casual things they
haven’t had the time to discuss in years.

03:12:59.299 --> 03:13:03.399
O5-3 suggests inviting the Ethics Committee
over to join.

03:13:03.399 --> 03:13:04.399
Nobody disagrees.

03:13:04.399 --> 03:13:06.119
Hour sixteen.

03:13:06.119 --> 03:13:07.999
It isn’t just the D-Classes.

03:13:07.999 --> 03:13:12.710
All sapient and non-aggressive SCPs have been
released from containment, free to spend the

03:13:12.710 --> 03:13:15.180
last of their time as they wish.

03:13:15.180 --> 03:13:19.470
Tens of thousands of anomalous individuals
are released from containment sites all over

03:13:19.470 --> 03:13:20.470
the globe.

03:13:20.470 --> 03:13:24.670
It’d be the greatest victory that the Serpent’s
Hand could ever ask for if they weren’t

03:13:24.670 --> 03:13:27.350
all too busy reading to notice.

03:13:27.350 --> 03:13:31.790
SCP-105, Iris Thompson, finally returns to
her parents.

03:13:31.790 --> 03:13:36.510
The Foundation had fed them the lie that their
daughter had died many years before, but as

03:13:36.510 --> 03:13:40.409
Iris had a tendency to do, she was ready to
work a miracle.

03:13:40.409 --> 03:13:42.659
Her parents embrace her with open arms.

03:13:42.659 --> 03:13:46.339
They’ll spend their last hours together
catching up on what’s happened since they

03:13:46.339 --> 03:13:49.600
parted ways, and making up for lost time.

03:13:49.600 --> 03:13:52.399
They couldn’t be happier.

03:13:52.399 --> 03:13:58.729
SCP-1867, Lord Blackwood the fantastical sea
snail, is delivered into a warm rockpool near

03:13:58.729 --> 03:14:01.220
the site where he was being contained.

03:14:01.220 --> 03:14:06.239
There, he might finally have one more grand
adventure before all is said and done.

03:14:06.239 --> 03:14:10.169
Though afterward, he may not have the time
to tell anyone about it.

03:14:10.169 --> 03:14:14.529
A terrible shame, really, because nobody spins
a yarn like Lord Blackwood.

03:14:14.529 --> 03:14:17.569
The non-aggressive little misters run free.

03:14:17.569 --> 03:14:23.000
Mr. Fish eagerly returns to his native Boston,
Massachusetts, where he enjoys one more lobster

03:14:23.000 --> 03:14:25.720
sandwich before the end of the world.

03:14:25.720 --> 03:14:30.569
Mr. Headless decides to go hat shopping because
he wants to look good for the apocalypse.

03:14:30.569 --> 03:14:36.189
Mr. Lost finally settles down for the afternoon,
deciding that, just this once, he’s earned

03:14:36.189 --> 03:14:38.430
himself a rest.

03:14:38.430 --> 03:14:43.640
SCP-2800, Cactusman, returns to Edinburgh,
to spend his last day picking up litter and

03:14:43.640 --> 03:14:45.739
helping old ladies cross the street.

03:14:45.739 --> 03:14:52.689
SCP-3663, the Tunnel Monster, walks the streets
of his hometown, searching for an old friend,

03:14:52.689 --> 03:14:55.640
hoping to reunite before it all ends.

03:14:55.640 --> 03:15:02.149
SCP-073, Cain, decides to take a walk outside
for the first time in thousands of years.

03:15:02.149 --> 03:15:06.859
He can’t help but smile, as the bright,
colorful life beneath his feet is growing

03:15:06.859 --> 03:15:09.649
faster than his presence can kill it.

03:15:09.649 --> 03:15:11.699
What a truly beautiful day.

03:15:11.699 --> 03:15:18.589
Knowing that there’s no longer time for
cults to form and bother him, SCP-2662, Cthulhu,

03:15:18.589 --> 03:15:23.520
decides to take a break from his intense Minecraft
session and go take a walk outside.

03:15:23.520 --> 03:15:29.509
It feels so good to have the sun on his tentacles
once more and to feel lush, green grass under

03:15:29.509 --> 03:15:30.790
his suction cups.

03:15:30.790 --> 03:15:35.159
He shakes his head, thinking once again about
the irritating cults that had been pestering

03:15:35.159 --> 03:15:36.589
him for decades.

03:15:36.589 --> 03:15:40.760
What kind of idiot would want him to destroy
a world like this?

03:15:40.760 --> 03:15:46.810
SCP-343, also known as God, sighs and looks
over all his creation for what he knows to

03:15:46.810 --> 03:15:48.409
be the last time.

03:15:48.409 --> 03:15:54.329
His mouth curls into a smile, as he thinks,
“Well, we had a pretty good run.”

03:15:54.329 --> 03:16:00.500
Still in his cell, SCP-049, the Plague Doctor,
puts his feet up and decides to relax.

03:16:00.500 --> 03:16:03.169
The Pestilence will soon be taken care of.

03:16:03.169 --> 03:16:10.140
On some animalistic level, below thought,
below even instinct, SCP-096 feels grateful

03:16:10.140 --> 03:16:13.049
that no gaze will ever fall upon it again.

03:16:13.049 --> 03:16:18.609
Somewhere, fizzling in a vat of acid within
a highly secure containment chamber, SCP-682

03:16:18.609 --> 03:16:25.760
is feeling, for the first time in its hellish
existence, a sense of profound relief.

03:16:25.760 --> 03:16:30.899
The pain, the hate, the rage, the constant
termination attempts.

03:16:30.899 --> 03:16:32.949
It’d all be over soon.

03:16:32.949 --> 03:16:34.379
Hour twenty-three.

03:16:34.379 --> 03:16:35.939
People gather in the streets.

03:16:35.939 --> 03:16:42.089
They laugh and dance and sing, as the moon
shines, fat and white, far above.

03:16:42.089 --> 03:16:45.649
Deep in their hearts, they quietly contemplate
the end of all this.

03:16:45.649 --> 03:16:47.159
But why worry?

03:16:47.159 --> 03:16:48.589
Why spoil the fun?

03:16:48.589 --> 03:16:51.329
There’s no future left to worry about.

03:16:51.329 --> 03:16:54.140
Strangers become as close as family in the
end.

03:16:54.140 --> 03:16:57.759
Human or otherwise, anomalous or non-anomalous.

03:16:57.759 --> 03:17:02.739
Chaos Insurgency agents have last suppers
with ex-Serpent’s Hands and GOC operatives.

03:17:02.739 --> 03:17:04.529
There is no hate left.

03:17:04.529 --> 03:17:05.670
No violence.

03:17:05.670 --> 03:17:06.890
No malice.

03:17:06.890 --> 03:17:08.129
No cruelty.

03:17:08.129 --> 03:17:13.189
The greatest tragedy in all of this is that
it took the ultimate end to bring it out in

03:17:13.189 --> 03:17:14.189
people.

03:17:14.189 --> 03:17:15.189
But why worry?

03:17:15.189 --> 03:17:16.359
Why worry?

03:17:16.359 --> 03:17:18.300
Seconds pass, then minutes.

03:17:18.300 --> 03:17:19.689
The world buzzes.

03:17:19.689 --> 03:17:21.090
It hums.

03:17:21.090 --> 03:17:26.399
Trillions of creatures, doing everything they’d
always wanted, even though they know it won’t

03:17:26.399 --> 03:17:27.399
last.

03:17:27.399 --> 03:17:32.109
In the face of the true end, the world has
never been more alive.

03:17:32.109 --> 03:17:33.109
Hour twenty-four.

03:17:33.109 --> 03:17:34.259
Silence.

03:17:34.259 --> 03:17:37.399
Forever, and ever, and ever...Goodnight.

03:17:37.399 --> 03:17:43.899
We’ll end this video the way it began, by
putting a question to you: How would you spend

03:17:43.899 --> 03:17:46.380
your last 24 hours on earth?

03:17:46.380 --> 03:17:48.339
Let us know down in the comments.

03:17:48.339 --> 03:17:51.510
Because it’ll happen to all of us eventually.

03:17:51.510 --> 03:17:57.370
For decades upon decades, conspiracy theories
have long captured the minds of many individuals

03:17:57.370 --> 03:17:59.540
and groups across the world.

03:17:59.540 --> 03:18:03.509
The infamous ones will always spring to mind
the moment somebody so much as speaks the

03:18:03.509 --> 03:18:09.069
phrase “conspiracy theory” aloud; the
words alone conjure up questions like “were

03:18:09.069 --> 03:18:13.619
the moon landings really faked?”, “did
aliens really have a hand in building the

03:18:13.619 --> 03:18:18.850
pyramids?”, and “is there really a shadowy,
ancient order called the Illuminati controlling

03:18:18.850 --> 03:18:21.209
the events of the world around us?”

03:18:21.209 --> 03:18:25.449
Of course, the answer to all of these questions
is often a plain and resounding “no, now

03:18:25.449 --> 03:18:30.329
please leave me alone”, but delving into
the world of conspiracy theories, collecting

03:18:30.329 --> 03:18:35.539
and connecting evidence can be an interesting
exercise in imagination when it’s all done

03:18:35.539 --> 03:18:37.000
in good fun.

03:18:37.000 --> 03:18:41.499
But there is often a dangerous side to conspiracy
theories as well, and we don’t mean getting

03:18:41.499 --> 03:18:45.350
so close to the truth that the men in black
show up at your front door and haul you away

03:18:45.350 --> 03:18:46.989
to Area 51.

03:18:46.989 --> 03:18:51.589
No, it’s important to remember the harm
that some conspiracy theories can do.

03:18:51.589 --> 03:18:56.149
It’s an unfortunate truth that a number
of conspiracy theories, especially those more

03:18:56.149 --> 03:19:01.020
prevalent in recent years, are often used
to unjustly villainize particular religious

03:19:01.020 --> 03:19:02.549
or ethnic minorities.

03:19:02.549 --> 03:19:06.979
Positing about ancient aliens can be fun when
you remember that conspiracy theories have

03:19:06.979 --> 03:19:12.129
no actual bearing on the real world, but the
line has to be drawn somewhere; the minute

03:19:12.129 --> 03:19:17.100
a ‘theory’ starts to delve into unseemly
territory, it’s best to realize that there’s

03:19:17.100 --> 03:19:18.989
very little truth to it.

03:19:18.989 --> 03:19:23.919
There is one infamous conspiracy theory, not
a vindictive or harmful one, that has stood

03:19:23.919 --> 03:19:28.850
the test of time for almost as long as the
moon landings or Area 51.

03:19:28.850 --> 03:19:31.909
Who really killed President John F Kennedy?

03:19:31.909 --> 03:19:38.189
We all know, or think we know what really
happened on November 22, 1963, on that fateful

03:19:38.189 --> 03:19:40.129
day in Dallas Texas.

03:19:40.129 --> 03:19:45.579
But what if that’s the point, we all think
we know, but each of us thinks differently?

03:19:45.579 --> 03:19:49.699
Grab your red string and shiniest tinfoil
hats and take a seat, folks.

03:19:49.699 --> 03:19:56.460
Welcome to SCP-001, otherwise known by the
appropriate nickname, The Conspiracy.

03:19:56.460 --> 03:20:00.020
Now, first things first, some important information.

03:20:00.020 --> 03:20:03.770
Anyone familiar with the SCP Foundation will
tell you that there are multiple entities

03:20:03.770 --> 03:20:07.739
and objects referred to as SCP-001.

03:20:07.739 --> 03:20:11.020
Everyone has some idea which of these they
think is the real one.

03:20:11.020 --> 03:20:14.689
But, just in case you happen to be new here,
we’ll clarify for you.

03:20:14.689 --> 03:20:20.350
The designation “SCP-001” doesn’t refer
to a single creature, object, or entity within

03:20:20.350 --> 03:20:21.829
the Foundation’s archive.

03:20:21.829 --> 03:20:26.999
Instead, it’s a collection of various anomalies
that have been encountered and - mostly - contained

03:20:26.999 --> 03:20:27.999
by the SCP Foundation.

03:20:27.999 --> 03:20:32.470
As for why these various files are all collected
under this shared designation?

03:20:32.470 --> 03:20:36.379
Well, that’s a conspiracy theory all in
itself.

03:20:36.379 --> 03:20:40.609
It could be that these anomalies are some
of the earliest ever contained by the Foundation,

03:20:40.609 --> 03:20:44.409
and were first encountered before they had
established the numbering system that they

03:20:44.409 --> 03:20:45.819
currently use.

03:20:45.819 --> 03:20:51.020
However, could these multiple SCP-001s be
an intentional misdirection?

03:20:51.020 --> 03:20:53.850
Smells like another conspiracy to us...

03:20:53.850 --> 03:20:59.779
Among the anomalies sharing the title of SCP-001
is the Gate Guardian, a powerful being believed

03:20:59.779 --> 03:21:03.149
to be an angel standing at the entrance to
the Garden of Eden.

03:21:03.149 --> 03:21:08.199
Then there’s the infamous Scarlet King,
another anomalous eldritch creature with similar

03:21:08.199 --> 03:21:14.039
levels of destructive power, who is intent
on one day causing the destruction of all

03:21:14.039 --> 03:21:15.039
creation.

03:21:15.039 --> 03:21:20.529
Also known as SCP-001 is a Database containing
all of the proof the Foundation’s top brass

03:21:20.529 --> 03:21:25.311
have collected that proves their entire universe
is the fictional creation of the SCP Wiki

03:21:25.311 --> 03:21:26.470
authors.

03:21:26.470 --> 03:21:28.020
Pretty wild stuff.

03:21:28.020 --> 03:21:33.939
And then, there’s this SCP-001, the Conspiracy
itself.

03:21:33.939 --> 03:21:37.859
As we mentioned before, it’s connected to
the assassination of United States President

03:21:37.859 --> 03:21:43.659
John F Kennedy; very closely connected, at
least for a few seconds before it came out

03:21:43.659 --> 03:21:51.720
the other side, that is, because in this instance,
SCP-001 is the bullet that killed JFK.

03:21:51.720 --> 03:21:58.279
Now, history tells us that on Friday, November
22, 1969, the 35th President of the United

03:21:58.279 --> 03:22:03.500
States John Fitzgerald Kennedy, was riding
in an open-top car as part of a presidential

03:22:03.500 --> 03:22:07.279
motorcade traveling through Dealey Plaza,
in Dallas, Texas.

03:22:07.279 --> 03:22:11.949
A former US Marine named Lee Harvey Oswald
opened fire on the President through the window

03:22:11.949 --> 03:22:15.239
of a nearby building, tragically killing JFK.

03:22:15.239 --> 03:22:19.729
But, ever since Kennedy’s death, there has
been rampant speculation about what really

03:22:19.729 --> 03:22:21.589
happened in Dallas.

03:22:21.589 --> 03:22:25.659
Most theories suggest that there was a secret
organization involved or multiple shooters

03:22:25.659 --> 03:22:28.550
in addition to Lee Harvey Oswald.

03:22:28.550 --> 03:22:32.810
According to the Foundation, through some
anomalous means, the shot that killed John

03:22:32.810 --> 03:22:38.499
F Kennedy was fired by multiple unidentified
assailants, acting as part of the same - or

03:22:38.499 --> 03:22:43.640
numerous - conspiracies, all shooting at the
exact same moment.

03:22:43.640 --> 03:22:50.049
The events surrounding the bullet’s trajectory
are designated under the codename Incident-001-Gamma.

03:22:50.049 --> 03:22:55.689
Anyone alive that has memories linked to Incident-001-Gamma
is part of the last population on Planet Earth

03:22:55.689 --> 03:22:58.989
that can agree on a shared concept of truth.

03:22:58.989 --> 03:23:03.329
They know what is true, thanks to all sharing
an experience of either hearing about the

03:23:03.329 --> 03:23:08.229
Kennedy Assassination, or witnessing it in
person or on television.

03:23:08.229 --> 03:23:15.729
When SCP-001 was fired, it created Incident-001-Gamma,
which was both a pivotal moment in history

03:23:15.729 --> 03:23:19.380
and also had a lasting effect on everything
that followed.

03:23:19.380 --> 03:23:24.239
It might not be obvious how just yet, but
we’ll get to the repercussions in a moment.

03:23:24.239 --> 03:23:29.359
The fact that multiple generations alive at
the time of Incident-001-Gamma have a consistent

03:23:29.359 --> 03:23:32.229
memory of it, establishes a baseline.

03:23:32.229 --> 03:23:36.659
Essentially, because these people have vivid
memories of the assassination, they also have

03:23:36.659 --> 03:23:43.669
a societal memory of everything that had occurred
in human history up until that day in 1969.

03:23:43.669 --> 03:23:48.539
The evolution of mankind, the various wars
that occurred had all been documented and

03:23:48.539 --> 03:23:50.239
were held to be true.

03:23:50.239 --> 03:23:56.249
There was a shared, collective truth among
Earth’s entire population, up until Incident-001-Gamma

03:23:56.249 --> 03:23:57.489
occurred.

03:23:57.489 --> 03:24:04.970
However, reality had shattered in some way,
the moment that SCP-001 was shot towards JFK.

03:24:04.970 --> 03:24:08.899
The sheer number of conspiracy theories that
tumbled out of the Kennedy Assassination weren’t

03:24:08.899 --> 03:24:11.089
just rampant speculation.

03:24:11.089 --> 03:24:15.479
Not only did everyone on Earth now have a
memory of what happened, they had their own

03:24:15.479 --> 03:24:18.979
version of what they believed they had remembered.

03:24:18.979 --> 03:24:24.789
For example, from the moment that Incident-001-Gamma
took place and JFK was shot, there were already

03:24:24.789 --> 03:24:29.829
conflicting witness testimonies from people
who were actually present in Dallas and saw

03:24:29.829 --> 03:24:30.829
it all happen.

03:24:30.829 --> 03:24:35.699
A significant percentage of eyewitnesses reported
some variation of seeing a strange, unidentified

03:24:35.699 --> 03:24:39.050
figure referred to only as ‘Badge Man’.

03:24:39.050 --> 03:24:43.510
Whoever he was, even if he was just a result
of civilians being unfamiliar with seeing

03:24:43.510 --> 03:24:49.300
Secret Service agents, not everyone that was
present at Incident-001-Gamma can agree if

03:24:49.300 --> 03:24:51.770
Badge Man was even there at all.

03:24:51.770 --> 03:24:56.569
The only two people that were definitely participants
in the assassination were President Kennedy

03:24:56.569 --> 03:24:58.839
and Lee Harvey Oswald.

03:24:58.839 --> 03:25:04.319
History diverged for everyone from this point
on, remembering everything that came before,

03:25:04.319 --> 03:25:09.999
but having conflicting memories of Incident-001-Gamma
and everything that followed it.

03:25:09.999 --> 03:25:14.720
What the SCP Foundation knows for a fact,
is that Lee Harvey Oswald fired three shots

03:25:14.720 --> 03:25:19.159
from his vantage point on the sixth floor
of the Texas Schoolbook Depository.

03:25:19.159 --> 03:25:23.330
The first missed, the second delivered a wound
to the President as well as Texas Governor

03:25:23.330 --> 03:25:27.189
John Connally who was riding in the same car
as JFK.

03:25:27.189 --> 03:25:33.640
The third and final shot was SCP-001, which
vaporized the cranial cavity, killing him

03:25:33.640 --> 03:25:36.640
and causing Incident-001-Gamma.

03:25:36.640 --> 03:25:42.259
From that moment on, there now existed a confusing
and contradictory number of different perspectives

03:25:42.259 --> 03:25:46.209
on the world’s history, all conflicting
with one another.

03:25:46.209 --> 03:25:50.890
People’s perceptions began to divert away
from reality over the course of the next decade,

03:25:50.890 --> 03:25:53.390
slowly and unnoticeably at first.

03:25:53.390 --> 03:25:58.379
Everyone could still agree on what had happened
since Incident-001-Gamma for the most part,

03:25:58.379 --> 03:26:05.089
until September 5th, 1975, the failed assassination
of Gerald Ford, the 38th President of the

03:26:05.089 --> 03:26:06.759
US.

03:26:06.759 --> 03:26:11.120
Multiple witnesses reported seeing different
versions of the event, some even certain that

03:26:11.120 --> 03:26:14.279
President Ford was, in fact, killed.

03:26:14.279 --> 03:26:19.479
This even resulted in another attempt on Ford’s
life only two weeks later by a woman who believed

03:26:19.479 --> 03:26:23.939
the President was already dead, attempting
to make reality align with what she thought

03:26:23.939 --> 03:26:25.109
to be real.

03:26:25.109 --> 03:26:31.170
But it gets worse, President Ford had equally
been affected by SCP-001, believing that the

03:26:31.170 --> 03:26:35.669
Soviet Union had withdrawn from Eastern Europe
during the Nixon administration.

03:26:35.669 --> 03:26:39.939
In reality, this didn’t occur until the
late 1980s.

03:26:39.939 --> 03:26:46.109
That is the true effect of SCP-001, the disparity
between what someone perceives to be real

03:26:46.109 --> 03:26:47.890
and what is actually real.

03:26:47.890 --> 03:26:52.749
It can often manifest in frustration, we’ve
all once felt that we have the skills required

03:26:52.749 --> 03:26:57.119
when applying for a job, only to have a rejection
email sent back to us.

03:26:57.119 --> 03:27:01.819
Some of us believe ourselves to be kind, good-hearted
people, yet can’t seem to find any friends

03:27:01.819 --> 03:27:03.109
that would agree.

03:27:03.109 --> 03:27:07.270
Living in a huge house can make a person feel
cramped and claustrophobic despite all the

03:27:07.270 --> 03:27:08.779
space around them.

03:27:08.779 --> 03:27:13.399
You can feel that there is something wrong
in situations like this, but you can’t explain

03:27:13.399 --> 03:27:14.399
it.

03:27:14.399 --> 03:27:19.629
This effect of SCP-001 can often result in
conditions like Imposter Syndrome, where someone

03:27:19.629 --> 03:27:24.549
has the belief that all of their achievements
and successes are nothing more than a sham,

03:27:24.549 --> 03:27:28.569
and that the best parts of their lives are
destined to fall apart because that person

03:27:28.569 --> 03:27:30.419
does not deserve them.

03:27:30.419 --> 03:27:35.460
That feeling of not belonging, the world not
aligning with what you think is true, all

03:27:35.460 --> 03:27:38.170
comes from SCP-001.

03:27:38.170 --> 03:27:43.169
The phenomenon known as the “Mandela Effect”
is also seemingly derived from the fractalization

03:27:43.169 --> 03:27:46.289
that occurred after Incident-001-Gamma.

03:27:46.289 --> 03:27:51.399
The Mandela Effect usually refers to a memory
held by an individual, or group of individuals,

03:27:51.399 --> 03:27:55.220
that they believe to be true, but actually
differs from fact.

03:27:55.220 --> 03:27:59.640
For example, the effect is named after Nelson
Mandela, who died in 2013.

03:27:59.640 --> 03:28:04.520
However, countless people distinctly remember
news that Mandela had died in prison during

03:28:04.520 --> 03:28:05.729
the 80s.

03:28:05.729 --> 03:28:10.439
Misremembering history comes as a result of
a person’s perception and their living memory

03:28:10.439 --> 03:28:13.079
being out of sync with that which is true.

03:28:13.079 --> 03:28:18.479
Often, trying to undo the effects of SCP-001
can be more harmful to a person as having

03:28:18.479 --> 03:28:21.819
their perception vary so dramatically from
reality.

03:28:21.819 --> 03:28:26.029
Say you believed that all the Beatles were
still alive, you were positive of it and it

03:28:26.029 --> 03:28:28.470
had always been that way all your life.

03:28:28.470 --> 03:28:33.199
Then, somebody presented you with actual historical
proof that John Lennon was killed outside

03:28:33.199 --> 03:28:36.119
his hotel in the year 1980.

03:28:36.119 --> 03:28:39.561
All the photographs, news reports, and other
evidence in the world couldn’t convince

03:28:39.561 --> 03:28:43.409
you that what you thought to be true, in fact,
wasn’t.

03:28:43.409 --> 03:28:48.829
Frequently, this leads to frustration and
confusion that could, and often does, damage

03:28:48.829 --> 03:28:54.979
relationships with friends and family, causing
isolation and disconnection of social associations.

03:28:54.979 --> 03:28:59.060
If everyone is telling you that John Lennon
died, but you can’t believe it because it

03:28:59.060 --> 03:29:03.329
doesn’t match your own perception, you would
gravitate towards people whose alternative

03:29:03.329 --> 03:29:05.759
viewpoints overlapped with yours.

03:29:05.759 --> 03:29:10.970
This is how echo chambers form, which spread
and strengthen conspiracy theories, often

03:29:10.970 --> 03:29:16.550
making them more resilient against outside
logic - as well as more extreme and pernicious.

03:29:16.550 --> 03:29:20.329
So, who really did kill President John F Kennedy?

03:29:20.329 --> 03:29:25.720
Ask Lee Harvey Oswald, he’d say he didn’t
do it and was instead being framed.

03:29:25.720 --> 03:29:29.720
Ask Fidel Castro and he’d tell you that
he and his men were there in Dallas that day,

03:29:29.720 --> 03:29:32.560
armed and on a mission to kill Kennedy themselves.

03:29:32.560 --> 03:29:38.549
Or there’s the “Umbrella Man”, who claimed
he killed JFK with a modified umbrella.

03:29:38.549 --> 03:29:44.020
But ultimately, speculating as to who killed
President Kennedy is pointless: every answer

03:29:44.020 --> 03:29:46.560
is right to someone.

03:29:46.560 --> 03:29:50.520
SCP-001 was the shot that changed the entire
world.

03:29:50.520 --> 03:29:55.159
Since Incident-001-Gamma, nobody has been
able to perceive the world in the exact same

03:29:55.159 --> 03:29:57.069
way as someone else does.

03:29:57.069 --> 03:30:02.760
If you feel confused, rely on what you know
to be real, what you believe is the truth,

03:30:02.760 --> 03:30:04.919
and find comfort in the normalcy of that.

03:30:04.919 --> 03:30:08.300
Honestly, it’s all you really have.

03:30:08.300 --> 03:30:13.479
At the time of this video’s writing, the
SCP Foundation currently contains well over

03:30:13.479 --> 03:30:15.239
6000 items.

03:30:15.239 --> 03:30:20.390
This organization really gets around, from
making deals with deities to containing horrors

03:30:20.390 --> 03:30:23.209
capable of ending the world in a heartbeat.

03:30:23.209 --> 03:30:28.060
So it’s hard to think of this secret group
ever having “Humble Beginnings”, but everyone

03:30:28.060 --> 03:30:31.590
and everything has to start somewhere, right?

03:30:31.590 --> 03:30:35.810
And would you believe that one of the most
powerful groups in the world all started with

03:30:35.810 --> 03:30:38.069
a little sheaf of papers?

03:30:38.069 --> 03:30:44.549
Of course, that’s if this particular iteration
of SCP-001 is to be believed.

03:30:44.549 --> 03:30:52.060
That’s right, we once again return to SCP-001,
the gift that keeps on taking.

03:30:52.060 --> 03:30:57.660
It’s a heavily contested spot, currently
held by over thirty different contradictory

03:30:57.660 --> 03:30:59.670
anomalies and counting.

03:30:59.670 --> 03:31:04.239
Their natures vary from things that started
the Foundation to things more than capable

03:31:04.239 --> 03:31:09.449
of ending it, along with the rest of the world,
and everything in between.

03:31:09.449 --> 03:31:15.839
The Scarlet King, The Gate Guardian, and the
ever-eccentric Dr. Wondertainment all exist

03:31:15.839 --> 03:31:17.279
under this banner.

03:31:17.279 --> 03:31:22.180
But today, we want to talk about a little
stack of paper, bound by a single staple in

03:31:22.180 --> 03:31:23.470
the top left corner.

03:31:23.470 --> 03:31:27.770
Who would have guessed that something this
simple would not only be pivotal in the creation

03:31:27.770 --> 03:31:32.689
of the SCP Foundation as we know it today
but could also be one of the most dangerous

03:31:32.689 --> 03:31:34.489
items ever discovered?

03:31:34.489 --> 03:31:36.939
We realize this is a lot to take in.

03:31:36.939 --> 03:31:42.470
Keeping with the SCP-001 spirit, let’s take
it all the way back to the beginning, to the

03:31:42.470 --> 03:31:46.189
fine oak desk of the late...hmmm...uhhh, I
guess uhhhh...

03:31:46.189 --> 03:31:49.680
Oh, we don’t have the name?

03:31:49.680 --> 03:31:50.680
Shame.

03:31:50.680 --> 03:31:54.170
Let’s just call him The First Administrator.

03:31:54.170 --> 03:31:59.960
He’s the head honcho of a precursor to the
Foundation as we know it today, a rinky-dink

03:31:59.960 --> 03:32:04.339
little organization with the thankless task
of keeping the paranormal under wraps.

03:32:04.339 --> 03:32:07.459
We’re talking a long, long time ago here.

03:32:07.459 --> 03:32:12.189
No lanky freaks who kill everybody who sees
their face, no gloopy sadists who can walk

03:32:12.189 --> 03:32:17.460
through walls, no giant unkillable reptiles
with major anger issues.

03:32:17.460 --> 03:32:22.970
This organization - let’s call them The
Precursors - was dealing with the real small

03:32:22.970 --> 03:32:23.970
fries.

03:32:23.970 --> 03:32:28.149
Paranoiacs reporting ghost sightings in their
garden sheds, old ladies finding the face

03:32:28.149 --> 03:32:33.649
of Jesus in a piece of toast, abnormally large
and strangely-shaped potato chips.

03:32:33.649 --> 03:32:37.430
Okay, maybe not that small-time, but you get
the idea.

03:32:37.430 --> 03:32:42.759
Truly exceptional anomalies were few and far
between, until the sheaf of papers landed

03:32:42.759 --> 03:32:45.549
on the dearly deceased Administrator’s desk.

03:32:45.549 --> 03:32:50.350
He didn’t even know how exactly the papers
got there, but given the numbers of mostly

03:32:50.350 --> 03:32:55.949
junk files that passed his desk every day,
he wasn’t in the business of questioning.

03:32:55.949 --> 03:33:00.689
The words “Confidential Report on Special
Items—Classified” were printed on the

03:33:00.689 --> 03:33:01.689
front.

03:33:01.689 --> 03:33:06.430
This made it more interesting than 90% of
the files he read on a daily basis already,

03:33:06.430 --> 03:33:09.470
so he turned the first page and began to read.

03:33:09.470 --> 03:33:15.039
It was much stranger than the usual paranormal
reports that the Precursor Foundation processed.

03:33:15.039 --> 03:33:17.919
No late-night wailing or rattling chains.

03:33:17.919 --> 03:33:24.009
Instead, it was a surprisingly sterile report
about a bizarre and frightening anomaly: A

03:33:24.009 --> 03:33:28.600
large, fleshy, tumor-like object fixed to
a set of metal stairs.

03:33:28.600 --> 03:33:34.229
Inside the object is a seemingly normal living
room, but on closer inspection, all the furniture

03:33:34.229 --> 03:33:38.129
is made out of living human tissue and flesh.

03:33:38.129 --> 03:33:43.010
Anyone who steps inside is transformed into
more nightmarish living furniture.

03:33:43.010 --> 03:33:45.229
The Administrator gave a nervous chuckle.

03:33:45.229 --> 03:33:49.909
It was disturbing, sure, but Stephen King
wrote about disturbing things all the time,

03:33:49.909 --> 03:33:54.210
and that didn’t mean that the Foundation
needed to be on the lookout for an evil clown

03:33:54.210 --> 03:33:59.579
- Well, until SCP-993, the sinister Bobble
the Clown, would enter the Foundation’s

03:33:59.579 --> 03:34:03.439
radar a few years later.

03:34:03.439 --> 03:34:07.879
The Administrator put the file into his incredibly
disorganized filing cabinet, and prepared

03:34:07.879 --> 03:34:10.689
to go home and drink bourbon until he fell
asleep.

03:34:10.689 --> 03:34:14.340
That’s exactly when his office phone began
to ring.

03:34:14.340 --> 03:34:18.629
When The Administrator picked up the phone,
he heard the excited voice of one of his field

03:34:18.629 --> 03:34:23.760
agents, telling him they’d just scored the
find of the century: A giant sphere made from

03:34:23.760 --> 03:34:26.850
living flesh with a room inside it.

03:34:26.850 --> 03:34:30.669
Finally, an honest to god, terrifying paranormal
anomaly!

03:34:30.669 --> 03:34:33.600
He could hardly believe what he was hearing.

03:34:33.600 --> 03:34:38.199
He needed to grab and reread the file, just
to make sure he wasn’t going insane.

03:34:38.199 --> 03:34:39.959
Where exactly did he put it?

03:34:39.959 --> 03:34:44.989
He scrambled through the filing cabinet, tossing
aside the files on shed ghosts and burnt toast

03:34:44.989 --> 03:34:49.939
Jesuses, until he found the file marked “Confidential
Report on Special Items—Classified.”

03:34:49.939 --> 03:34:55.919
However, when he opened the file, there was
nothing about the giant, fleshy room in there.

03:34:55.919 --> 03:35:00.220
It must have been a completely different file
that he’d somehow missed before, because

03:35:00.220 --> 03:35:04.220
this one was about something known as the
“Biological Motherboard.”

03:35:04.220 --> 03:35:08.979
The document detailed pretty much exactly
what the name suggested: A large and incredibly

03:35:08.979 --> 03:35:13.760
complex motherboard made out of biological
material like keratin and chitin.

03:35:13.760 --> 03:35:18.789
While the motherboard would remain inactive
if kept warm, if its environment ever fell

03:35:18.789 --> 03:35:24.749
below 35 degrees, it would begin to expand,
integrating nearby material into its mass

03:35:24.749 --> 03:35:30.050
and attempting to copy the structure of any
biological matter it comes into contact with.

03:35:30.050 --> 03:35:34.329
An interesting and frightening prospect, but
not what he was looking for.

03:35:34.329 --> 03:35:38.509
He threw this new file down onto his desk
and continued to work through his chaotic

03:35:38.509 --> 03:35:43.439
filing cabinet like a madman, searching for
the file on that frightening fleshy room that

03:35:43.439 --> 03:35:46.600
his subordinates had seemingly actually discovered.

03:35:46.600 --> 03:35:52.079
But not long after, he received another phone
call from a completely different field agent.

03:35:52.079 --> 03:35:57.209
This time, the agent was giddily telling the
Administrator about a new discovery: A huge

03:35:57.209 --> 03:36:02.359
computer motherboard, seemingly made out of
entirely organic material!

03:36:02.359 --> 03:36:03.979
The Administrator was floored.

03:36:03.979 --> 03:36:08.670
He hung up the phone and slowly turned back
to the file now laying on his desk.

03:36:08.670 --> 03:36:13.479
Those words on the cover, “Confidential
Report on Special Items—Classified”, seemed

03:36:13.479 --> 03:36:15.089
almost mocking now.

03:36:15.089 --> 03:36:19.939
Had all these incredible supernatural anomalies
been reported before and just lost in his

03:36:19.939 --> 03:36:21.520
awful filing cabinet?

03:36:21.520 --> 03:36:25.100
Was he one of the most incompetent team leaders
who’d ever walked the earth?

03:36:25.100 --> 03:36:27.640
Just what exactly was going on here?

03:36:27.640 --> 03:36:33.499
He sat back down at his desk, now fantasizing
about that tumbler of bourbon more than ever,

03:36:33.499 --> 03:36:37.819
and opened the file again, hoping to read
up a little more on the impossible motherboard

03:36:37.819 --> 03:36:40.249
that his personnel had just discovered.

03:36:40.249 --> 03:36:44.120
But there was nothing about the Biological
Motherboard on these pages.

03:36:44.120 --> 03:36:50.060
Instead, it described a large door inside
a factory, and the twelve rusty keys capable

03:36:50.060 --> 03:36:51.369
of opening it.

03:36:51.369 --> 03:36:55.630
Each of these keys would open the doorway,
but the key used would affect the reality

03:36:55.630 --> 03:36:58.289
waiting for them on the other side.

03:36:58.289 --> 03:37:02.669
Only the seventh and twelfth keys were safe,
opening the door with any of the others would

03:37:02.669 --> 03:37:07.779
lead to a horrible death for anyone brave
or foolish enough to walk through.

03:37:07.779 --> 03:37:12.479
Several days later, an anomaly matching that
exact description was discovered and contained

03:37:12.479 --> 03:37:13.949
by the Foundation.

03:37:13.949 --> 03:37:18.579
All of this had been an unprecedented escalation
of anomalous stakes.

03:37:18.579 --> 03:37:23.369
Suddenly, two crucial facts clicked into place
for The Administrator: Firstly, this file

03:37:23.369 --> 03:37:26.549
was an anomalous supernatural artifact of
its own.

03:37:26.549 --> 03:37:31.100
Secondly, the reason it was never the same
thing was that this strange sheaf of papers

03:37:31.100 --> 03:37:37.550
had a very specific purpose: To act as a kind
of oracle, an advanced warning system of the

03:37:37.550 --> 03:37:42.689
next anomaly that would appear and fall into
their grasp, giving them all the knowledge

03:37:42.689 --> 03:37:46.329
and tools they needed to safely lock these
things away.

03:37:46.329 --> 03:37:51.659
The whole thing had been timed perfectly - what
a miracle that this immensely useful item

03:37:51.659 --> 03:37:56.659
would appear in his office just as the anomalies
would start to come in thick and fast.

03:37:56.659 --> 03:38:01.529
It would facilitate their mission in the coming
struggles to secure, contain, and protect

03:38:01.529 --> 03:38:03.069
the world’s anomalies.

03:38:03.069 --> 03:38:07.129
Hmm, there’s a certain ring to that, isn’t
there?

03:38:07.129 --> 03:38:11.339
They were finding enough anomalies to start
classifying them numerically, starting with

03:38:11.339 --> 03:38:15.680
the sheaf of papers themselves as SCP-001.

03:38:15.680 --> 03:38:19.979
With another turn of the page, The Administrator
discovered a file on a magical key that can

03:38:19.979 --> 03:38:21.609
open any lock.

03:38:21.609 --> 03:38:29.159
Not long after, that exact key was discovered
and brought in, before being designated SCP-005.

03:38:29.159 --> 03:38:34.129
Little by little, as more real anomalies came
in, the organization was able to expand and

03:38:34.129 --> 03:38:39.409
bring in more personnel, as well as bringing
in more sources of funding and opening new

03:38:39.409 --> 03:38:40.409
sites.

03:38:40.409 --> 03:38:43.969
The rate this organization was expanding,
they couldn’t even leave management up to

03:38:43.969 --> 03:38:45.719
one person anymore.

03:38:45.719 --> 03:38:48.810
They needed to form a whole council to take
over management.

03:38:48.810 --> 03:38:52.250
An O5 Council, if you will.

03:38:52.250 --> 03:38:57.259
And it just so happened that just after that,
the sheaf of papers revealed a mythical spring

03:38:57.259 --> 03:39:01.469
that could provide eternal health and vitality
for anyone who drinks from it.

03:39:01.469 --> 03:39:06.969
What a perfect way to keep your management
safe in a job dealing with dangerous supernatural

03:39:06.969 --> 03:39:07.969
entities.

03:39:07.969 --> 03:39:11.799
And things only got stranger and more fascinating
from there.

03:39:11.799 --> 03:39:16.680
After that came a man with a miniature version
of planet earth inside his abdomen, soon known

03:39:16.680 --> 03:39:19.310
as SCP-007.

03:39:19.310 --> 03:39:23.899
Next came a horrifying virus that kills and
reanimates its victims into flesh-eating zombies,

03:39:23.899 --> 03:39:31.319
only capable of being destroyed with sufficient
trauma to the head, dubbed SCP-008 after containment.

03:39:31.319 --> 03:39:37.329
Another turn of the page, and not long after,
a frightening red ice was discovered in Alaska.

03:39:37.329 --> 03:39:41.600
This mysterious substance breaks the laws
of physics, and also has the potential to

03:39:41.600 --> 03:39:43.609
break all life on earth.

03:39:43.609 --> 03:39:48.640
It can infect water supplies, and when a hapless
lifeform happens to drink this water, their

03:39:48.640 --> 03:39:51.680
organs crystalize from the inside.

03:39:51.680 --> 03:39:54.729
This became SCP-009.

03:39:54.729 --> 03:39:58.869
Another turn of the page, and this new SCP
Foundation found a collection of six metal

03:39:58.869 --> 03:40:02.270
collars created for human-sized necks.

03:40:02.270 --> 03:40:06.619
When these collars are placed around the necks
of a victim, the person holding a corresponding

03:40:06.619 --> 03:40:10.100
controller has utter domination over their
every action.

03:40:10.100 --> 03:40:11.810
It carried on like that.

03:40:11.810 --> 03:40:14.739
Hundreds of anomalies, and then thousands.

03:40:14.739 --> 03:40:20.079
Years passed, the staff changed, the old guard
stepped down or died.

03:40:20.079 --> 03:40:24.460
Every time the sheaf of papers were opened,
new astonishing premonitions of anomalies

03:40:24.460 --> 03:40:26.909
soon to be discovered slipped through.

03:40:26.909 --> 03:40:29.680
There were Plague Doctors who could kill with
a touch.

03:40:29.680 --> 03:40:31.949
A giant angel with bladed wings.

03:40:31.949 --> 03:40:35.259
A sea snail that believed he was an English
lord.

03:40:35.259 --> 03:40:38.869
A Sculpture that would kill anything that
dared to stop looking at it.

03:40:38.869 --> 03:40:43.379
A nightmarish fusion of a giant bovine heart
and a scorpion, capable of setting things

03:40:43.379 --> 03:40:45.619
on fire with its venom.

03:40:45.619 --> 03:40:49.770
Whatever would the SCP Foundation have done
without the advanced warning system provided

03:40:49.770 --> 03:40:51.839
by the sheaf of papers?

03:40:51.839 --> 03:40:56.130
Whatever it predicted would inevitably be
the next thing Foundation field agents would

03:40:56.130 --> 03:40:57.130
find.

03:40:57.130 --> 03:41:02.590
It seems like one of the few unambiguously
good SCP-001 entries out there, right?

03:41:02.590 --> 03:41:03.899
Well, not quite.

03:41:03.899 --> 03:41:08.459
If we have any scientists in the audience,
they’ve no doubt been gritting their teeth

03:41:08.459 --> 03:41:11.539
and pulling their hair out in frustration.

03:41:11.539 --> 03:41:16.049
Allow us to introduce you to a little phrase
that the latest iteration of the O5 Council

03:41:16.049 --> 03:41:22.140
is very interested in when it comes to the
sheaf of papers: “Direction of causality.”

03:41:22.140 --> 03:41:27.310
This whole time, we and the earlier Foundation
administrations believed that the emergence

03:41:27.310 --> 03:41:31.890
of new anomalies led to changes in SCP-001.

03:41:31.890 --> 03:41:36.589
But this current administration has quite
the opposite question: What if the changes

03:41:36.589 --> 03:41:42.719
in SCP-001 were actually causing the emergence
of new anomalies?

03:41:42.719 --> 03:41:47.140
What if every time the prior administration
opened up the sheaf of papers to take a look

03:41:47.140 --> 03:41:52.669
at the next anomaly, before giving themselves
a pat on the back for being so well-prepared,

03:41:52.669 --> 03:41:55.930
they were actually unleashing that very anomaly?

03:41:55.930 --> 03:41:59.959
Could it be that what had seemed like the
most helpful item of the bunch was actually

03:41:59.959 --> 03:42:05.260
the most dangerous of them all, releasing
new anomaly after new anomaly, blighting the

03:42:05.260 --> 03:42:07.760
world with countless horrors?

03:42:07.760 --> 03:42:12.209
That probably leaves you with one question:
So, which is correct?

03:42:12.209 --> 03:42:15.670
Is it a method of seeing the future, or manipulating
it?

03:42:15.670 --> 03:42:20.319
And our answer is a strong...we don’t know.

03:42:20.319 --> 03:42:25.129
But frankly, the current leadership of the
SCP Foundation sees no merit in taking that

03:42:25.129 --> 03:42:26.129
risk.

03:42:26.129 --> 03:42:30.020
That’s why the sheaf of papers has been
given the Keter Class designation, and is

03:42:30.020 --> 03:42:35.419
kept under extensive and severe containment
methods, forbidding any future research into

03:42:35.419 --> 03:42:38.859
the true nature of its anomalous abilities.

03:42:38.859 --> 03:42:57.759
Seems a little severe, sure, but better safe
than sorry, right?

